msgid "Availability"
msgstr "可用性"

#: ../../library/os.rst:183
msgid ""
"A :term:`mapping` object where keys and values are strings that represent "
"the process environment.  For example, ``environ['HOME']`` is the pathname "
"of your home directory (on some platforms), and is equivalent to "
"``getenv(\"HOME\")`` in C."
msgstr ""
"一個\\ :term:`對映 <mapping>`\\ 物件，其鍵與值皆為代表行程環境的字串。舉例來"
"說，``environ['HOME']`` 是你的家目錄路徑名稱（在某些平台上），等同於 C 中的 "
"``getenv(\"HOME\")``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:188
msgid ""
"This mapping is captured the first time the :mod:`!os` module is imported, "
"typically during Python startup as part of processing :file:`site.py`.  "
"Changes to the environment made after this time are not reflected "
"in :data:`os.environ`, except for changes made by "
"modifying :data:`os.environ` directly."
msgstr ""
"此對映會在 :mod:`!os` 模組第一次被引入時擷取，通常是在 Python 啟動、處"
"理 :file:`site.py` 的過程中。在此之後對環境所做的變更不會反映"
"在 :data:`os.environ` 中，除非是直接修改 :data:`os.environ` 所做的變更。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:193
msgid ""
"This mapping may be used to modify the environment as well as query the "
"environment.  :func:`putenv` will be called automatically when the mapping "
"is modified."
msgstr ""
"此對映除了可用來查詢環境，也可以用來修改環境。修改此對映時會自動呼"
"叫 :func:`putenv`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:197
msgid ""
"On Unix, keys and values use :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` and "
"``'surrogateescape'`` error handler. Use :data:`environb` if you would like "
"to use a different encoding."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，鍵與值會使用 :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` 和 "
"``'surrogateescape'`` 錯誤處理函式。如果你想使用不同的編碼，請使"
"用 :data:`environb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:201
msgid ""
"On Windows, the keys are converted to uppercase. This also applies when "
"getting, setting, or deleting an item. For example, ``environ['monty'] = "
"'python'`` maps the key ``'MONTY'`` to the value ``'python'``."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，鍵會被轉換為大寫。這也適用於取得、設定或刪除項目時。舉例來說，"
"``environ['monty'] = 'python'`` 會將鍵 ``'MONTY'`` 對映到值 ``'python'``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:208
msgid ""
"Calling :func:`putenv` directly does not change :data:`os.environ`, so it's "
"better to modify :data:`os.environ`."
msgstr ""
"呼叫 :func:`putenv` 並不會改變 :data:`os.environ`，所以建議直接修"
"改 :data:`os.environ`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:213
msgid ""
"On some platforms, including FreeBSD and macOS, setting ``environ`` may "
"cause memory leaks.  Refer to the system documentation for :c:func:`!putenv`."
msgstr ""
"在包括 FreeBSD 與 macOS 在內的某些平台上，設定 ``environ`` 可能會導致記憶體洩"
"漏。請參閱系統中 :c:func:`!putenv` 的文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:217
msgid ""
"You can delete items in this mapping to unset environment "
"variables. :func:`unsetenv` will be called automatically when an item is "
"deleted from :data:`os.environ`, and when one of the :meth:`~dict.pop` "
"or :meth:`~dict.clear` methods is called."
msgstr ""
"你可以刪除此對映中的項目來取消設定環境變數。當從 :data:`os.environ` 刪除項"
"目，以及呼叫 :meth:`~dict.pop` 或 :meth:`~dict.clear` 方法其中之一時，會自動"
"呼叫 :func:`unsetenv`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:222
msgid ""
"If the :manpage:`clearenv(3)` function is available, the :meth:`~dict.clear` "
"method uses it and emits a single ``os._clearenv`` audit event. Otherwise, "
"it emits an ``os.unsetenv`` event on each deleted variable."
msgstr ""
"如果 :manpage:`clearenv(3)` 函式可用，:meth:`~dict.clear` 方法會使用它，並只"
"發出一個 ``os._clearenv`` 稽核事件。否則，它會對每個被刪除的變數各發出一個 "
"``os.unsetenv`` 事件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:226 ../../library/os.rst:873
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.unsetenv`` with argument "
"``key``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``key`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.unsetenv``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:228
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os._clearenv`` with no "
"arguments."
msgstr "引發一個不附帶引數的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os._clearenv``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:232
msgid "The :func:`os.reload_environ` function."
msgstr ":func:`os.reload_environ` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:234 ../../library/os.rst:254
msgid ""
"Updated to support :pep:`584`'s merge (``|``) and update (``|=``) operators."
msgstr "更新以支援 :pep:`584` 的合併 (``|``) 和更新 (``|=``) 運算子。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:237
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~dict.clear` method can now emit an ``os._clearenv`` audit event."
msgstr ":meth:`~dict.clear` 方法現在可以發出 ``os._clearenv`` 稽核事件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:244
msgid ""
"Bytes version of :data:`environ`: a :term:`mapping` object where both keys "
"and values are :class:`bytes` objects representing the process "
"environment. :data:`environ` and :data:`environb` are synchronized "
"(modifying :data:`environb` updates :data:`environ`, and vice versa)."
msgstr ""
":data:`environ` 的位元組版本：一個\\ :term:`對映 <mapping>`\\ 物件，其鍵與值"
"皆為代表行程環境的 :class:`bytes` 物件。:data:`environ` 和 :data:`environb` "
"會保持同步（修改 :data:`environb` 會更新 :data:`environ`，反之亦然）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:249
msgid ""
":data:`environb` is only available if :const:`supports_bytes_environ` is "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
"只有在 :const:`supports_bytes_environ` 為 ``True`` 時才能使"
"用 :data:`environb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:260
msgid ""
"The :data:`os.environ` and :data:`os.environb` mappings are a cache of "
"environment variables at the time that Python started. As such, changes to "
"the current process environment are not reflected if made outside Python, or "
"by :func:`os.putenv` or :func:`os.unsetenv`. Use :func:`!os.reload_environ` "
"to update :data:`os.environ` and :data:`os.environb` with any such changes "
"to the current process environment."
msgstr ""
":data:`os.environ` 和 :data:`os.environb` 對映是 Python 啟動時環境變數的快"
"取。因此，若是在 Python 之外，或是透過 :func:`os.putenv` "
"或 :func:`os.unsetenv` 對目前行程環境做出變更，這些變更不會被反映出來。請使"
"用 :func:`!os.reload_environ`，將目前行程環境的這類變更更新"
"到 :data:`os.environ` 和 :data:`os.environb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:268
msgid ""
"This function is not thread-safe. Calling it while the environment is being "
"modified in another thread is an undefined behavior. Reading "
"from :data:`os.environ` or :data:`os.environb`, or calling :func:`os.getenv` "
"while reloading, may return an empty result."
msgstr ""
"此函式不是執行緒安全的。在另一個執行緒正在修改環境時呼叫它，屬於未定義行為。"
"在重新載入期間讀取 :data:`os.environ` 或 :data:`os.environb`，或呼"
"叫 :func:`os.getenv`，可能會回傳空的結果。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:281
msgid "These functions are described in :ref:`os-file-dir`."
msgstr "這些函式的說明請見\\ :ref:`os-file-dir`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:286
msgid ""
"Encode :term:`path-like <path-like object>` *filename* to "
"the :term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`; return :class:`bytes` "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"以\\ :term:`檔案系統編碼和錯誤處理函式 <filesystem encoding and error "
"handler>`\\ 將\\ :term:`類路徑 <path-like object>` *filename* 編"
"碼；:class:`bytes` 則原樣回傳。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:290
msgid ":func:`fsdecode` is the reverse function."
msgstr ":func:`fsdecode` 是反函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:294 ../../library/os.rst:309
msgid ""
"Support added to accept objects implementing the :class:`os.PathLike` "
"interface."
msgstr "新增對實作 :class:`os.PathLike` 介面之物件的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:301
msgid ""
"Decode the :term:`path-like <path-like object>` *filename* from "
"the :term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`; return :class:`str` "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"以\\ :term:`檔案系統編碼和錯誤處理函式 <filesystem encoding and error "
"handler>`\\ 將\\ :term:`類路徑 <path-like object>` *filename* 解"
"碼；:class:`str` 則原樣回傳。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:305
msgid ":func:`fsencode` is the reverse function."
msgstr ":func:`fsencode` 是反函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:316
msgid "Return the file system representation of the path."
msgstr "回傳路徑的檔案系統表示法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:318
msgid ""
"If :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` is passed in, it is returned unchanged. "
"Otherwise :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__` is called and its value is "
"returned as long as it is a :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` object. In all "
"other cases, :exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"如果傳入的是 :class:`str` 或 :class:`bytes`，則會原樣回傳。否則會呼"
"叫 :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__`，只要其回傳值是 :class:`str` "
"或 :class:`bytes` 物件就會回傳該值。在其他所有情況下都會引"
"發 :exc:`TypeError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:328
msgid ""
"An :term:`abstract base class` for objects representing a file system path, "
"e.g. :class:`pathlib.PurePath`."
msgstr ""
"表示檔案系統路徑之物件的\\ :term:`抽象基底類別 <abstract base class>`，例"
"如 :class:`pathlib.PurePath`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:336
msgid "Return the file system path representation of the object."
msgstr "回傳物件的檔案系統路徑表示法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:338
msgid ""
"The method should only return a :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` object, with "
"the preference being for :class:`str`."
msgstr ""
"此方法應該只回傳 :class:`str` 或 :class:`bytes` 物件，且偏好 :class:`str`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:344
msgid ""
"Return the value of the environment variable *key* as a string if it exists, "
"or *default* if it doesn't. *key* is a string. Note that "
"since :func:`getenv` uses :data:`os.environ`, the mapping of :func:`getenv` "
"is similarly also captured on import, and the function may not reflect "
"future environment changes."
msgstr ""
"如果環境變數 *key* 存在，則以字串回傳其值，否則回傳 *default*。*key* 是一個字"
"串。請注意，由於 :func:`getenv` 使用 :data:`os.environ`，:func:`getenv` 的對"
"映同樣會在引入時被擷取，因此此函式可能不會反映之後的環境變更。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:350
msgid ""
"On Unix, keys and values are decoded with :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` "
"and ``'surrogateescape'`` error handler. Use :func:`os.getenvb` if you would "
"like to use a different encoding."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，鍵與值會以 :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` 和 "
"``'surrogateescape'`` 錯誤處理函式解碼。如果你想使用不同的編碼，請使"
"用 :func:`os.getenvb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:359
msgid ""
"Return the value of the environment variable *key* as bytes if it exists, or "
"*default* if it doesn't. *key* must be bytes. Note that "
"since :func:`getenvb` uses :data:`os.environb`, the mapping "
"of :func:`getenvb` is similarly also captured on import, and the function "
"may not reflect future environment changes."
msgstr ""
"如果環境變數 *key* 存在，則以位元組回傳其值，否則回傳 *default*。*key* 必須是"
"位元組。請注意，由於 :func:`getenvb` 使"
"用 :data:`os.environb`，:func:`getenvb` 的對映同樣會在引入時被擷取，因此此函"
"式可能不會反映之後的環境變更。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:366
msgid ""
":func:`getenvb` is only available if :const:`supports_bytes_environ` is "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
"只有在 :const:`supports_bytes_environ` 為 ``True`` 時才能使"
"用 :func:`getenvb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:376
msgid ""
"Returns the list of directories that will be searched for a named "
"executable, similar to a shell, when launching a process. *env*, when "
"specified, should be an environment variable dictionary to lookup the PATH "
"in. By default, when *env* is ``None``, :data:`environ` is used."
msgstr ""
"回傳在啟動行程時，會像 shell 一樣用來搜尋具名可執行檔的目錄串列。若有指定 "
"*env*，它應該是一個環境變數字典，用來在其中查詢 PATH。預設情況下，當 *env* "
"為 ``None`` 時會使用 :data:`environ`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:387
msgid ""
"Return the effective group id of the current process.  This corresponds to "
"the \"set id\" bit on the file being executed in the current process."
msgstr ""
"回傳目前行程的有效群組 ID。這對應於目前行程中正在執行之檔案的「set id」位元。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:397
msgid "Return the current process's effective user id."
msgstr "回傳目前行程的有效使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:406
msgid "Return the real group id of the current process."
msgstr "回傳目前行程的真實群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:410 ../../library/os.rst:483 ../../library/os.rst:567
#: ../../library/os.rst:792
msgid ""
"The function is a stub on WASI, see :ref:`wasm-availability` for more "
"information."
msgstr "此函式在 WASI 上是一個 stub，詳情請參閱 :ref:`wasm-availability`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:416
msgid ""
"Return list of group ids that *user* belongs to. If *group* is not in the "
"list, it is included; typically, *group* is specified as the group ID field "
"from the password record for *user*, because that group ID will otherwise be "
"potentially omitted."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *user* 所屬的群組 ID 串列。如果 *group* 不在串列中，它會被加入；通常 "
"*group* 會指定為 *user* 密碼紀錄中的群組 ID 欄位，因為若不這麼做，該群組 ID "
"可能會被遺漏。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:428
msgid ""
"Return list of supplemental group ids associated with the current process."
msgstr "回傳與目前行程關聯的補充群組 ID 串列。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:434
msgid ""
"On macOS, :func:`getgroups` behavior differs somewhat from other Unix "
"platforms. If the Python interpreter was built with a deployment target of "
"``10.5`` or earlier, :func:`getgroups` returns the list of effective group "
"ids associated with the current user process; this list is limited to a "
"system-defined number of entries, typically 16, and may be modified by calls "
"to :func:`setgroups` if suitably privileged. If built with a deployment "
"target greater than ``10.5``, :func:`getgroups` returns the current group "
"access list for the user associated with the effective user id of the "
"process; the group access list may change over the lifetime of the process, "
"it is not affected by calls to :func:`setgroups`, and its length is not "
"limited to 16.  The deployment target value can be obtained "
"with :func:`sysconfig.get_config_var('MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET') "
"<sysconfig.get_config_var>`."
msgstr ""
"在 macOS 上，:func:`getgroups` 的行為與其他 Unix 平台有些不同。如果 Python 直"
"譯器是以 ``10.5`` 或更早的部署目標 (deployment target) 建置"
"的，:func:`getgroups` 會回傳與目前使用者行程關聯的有效群組 ID 串列；此串列的"
"項目數受限於系統定義的數量（通常為 16），且在具備適當權限時可能會因呼"
"叫 :func:`setgroups` 而被修改。如果是以大於 ``10.5`` 的部署目標建置"
"的，:func:`getgroups` 會回傳該行程有效使用者 ID 所對應之使用者的目前群組存取"
"串列；此群組存取串列在行程的生命週期中可能會改變，不受 :func:`setgroups` 呼叫"
"的影響，且其長度不限於 16。部署目標的值可以透"
"過 :func:`sysconfig.get_config_var('MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET') "
"<sysconfig.get_config_var>` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:451
msgid ""
"Return the name of the user logged in on the controlling terminal of the "
"process.  For most purposes, it is more useful to "
"use :func:`getpass.getuser` since the latter checks the environment "
"variables :envvar:`LOGNAME` or :envvar:`USERNAME` to find out who the user "
"is, and falls back to ``pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid())[0]`` to get the login name "
"of the current real user id."
msgstr ""
"回傳登入在該行程之控制終端機上的使用者名稱。在大多數情況下，使"
"用 :func:`getpass.getuser` 會更有用，因為後者會檢查環境變"
"數 :envvar:`LOGNAME` 或 :envvar:`USERNAME` 來找出使用者是誰，並會退而使用 "
"``pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid())[0]`` 來取得目前真實使用者 ID 的登入名稱。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:463
msgid ""
"Return the process group id of the process with process id *pid*. If *pid* "
"is 0, the process group id of the current process is returned."
msgstr ""
"回傳行程 ID 為 *pid* 之行程的行程群組 ID。如果 *pid* 為 0，則回傳目前行程的行"
"程群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:472
msgid "Return the id of the current process group."
msgstr "回傳目前行程群組的 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:481
msgid "Return the current process id."
msgstr "回傳目前的行程 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:490
msgid ""
"Return the parent's process id.  When the parent process has exited, on Unix "
"the id returned is the one of the init process (1), on Windows it is still "
"the same id, which may be already reused by another process."
msgstr ""
"回傳父行程的行程 ID。當父行程已經結束時，在 Unix 上回傳的 ID 是 init 行程的 "
"ID (1)，在 Windows 上則仍是相同的 ID，而該 ID 可能已被其他行程重複使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:496
msgid "Added support for Windows."
msgstr "新增對 Windows 的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:504
msgid ""
"Get program scheduling priority.  The value *which* is one "
"of :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, or :const:`PRIO_USER`, and "
"*who* is interpreted relative to *which* (a process identifier "
"for :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, process group identifier for :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, "
"and a user ID for :const:`PRIO_USER`).  A zero value for *who* denotes "
"(respectively) the calling process, the process group of the calling "
"process, or the real user ID of the calling process."
msgstr ""
"取得程式排程優先權。*which* 的值為 :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`、:const:`PRIO_PGRP` "
"或 :const:`PRIO_USER` 其中之一，而 *who* 會依據 *which* 來解讀"
"（:const:`PRIO_PROCESS` 為行程 ID、:const:`PRIO_PGRP` 為行程群組 "
"ID、:const:`PRIO_USER` 為使用者 ID）。*who* 的值為零時（分別）表示呼叫端行"
"程、呼叫端行程的行程群組或呼叫端行程的真實使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:521 ../../library/os.rst:533
msgid ""
"Parameters for the :func:`getpriority` and :func:`setpriority` functions."
msgstr ":func:`getpriority` 和 :func:`setpriority` 函式的參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:541
msgid ""
"Return a tuple (ruid, euid, suid) denoting the current process's real, "
"effective, and saved user ids."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個元組 (ruid, euid, suid)，表示目前行程的真實、有效與保存的使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:551
msgid ""
"Return a tuple (rgid, egid, sgid) denoting the current process's real, "
"effective, and saved group ids."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個元組 (rgid, egid, sgid)，表示目前行程的真實、有效與保存的群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:563
msgid "Return the current process's real user id."
msgstr "回傳目前行程的真實使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:573
msgid ""
"Call the system ``initgroups()`` to initialize the group access list with "
"all of the groups of which the specified username is a member, plus the "
"specified group id."
msgstr ""
"呼叫系統的 ``initgroups()``，以指定使用者名稱所屬的所有群組，再加上指定的群"
"組 ID，來初始化群組存取串列。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:586
msgid ""
"Set the environment variable named *key* to the string *value*.  Such "
"changes to the environment affect subprocesses started "
"with :func:`os.system`, :func:`popen` or :func:`fork` and :func:`execv`."
msgstr ""
"將名為 *key* 的環境變數設定為字串 *value*。對環境的這類變更會影響"
"以 :func:`os.system`、:func:`popen` 或 :func:`fork` 和 :func:`execv` 啟動的子"
"行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:590
msgid ""
"Assignments to items in :data:`os.environ` are automatically translated into "
"corresponding calls to :func:`putenv`; however, calls to :func:`putenv` "
"don't update :data:`os.environ`, so it is actually preferable to assign to "
"items of :data:`os.environ`. This also applies to :func:`getenv` "
"and :func:`getenvb`, which respectively use :data:`os.environ` "
"and :data:`os.environb` in their implementations."
msgstr ""
"對 :data:`os.environ` 中項目的賦值會自動轉換為對應的 :func:`putenv` 呼叫；然"
"而，呼叫 :func:`putenv` 並不會更新 :data:`os.environ`，所以實際上更建議"
"對 :data:`os.environ` 的項目賦值。這也適用於 :func:`getenv` "
"和 :func:`getenvb`，它們的實作分別使用了 :data:`os.environ` "
"和 :data:`os.environb`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:596 ../../library/os.rst:871
msgid "See also the :func:`os.reload_environ` function."
msgstr "也請見 :func:`os.reload_environ` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:600
msgid ""
"On some platforms, including FreeBSD and macOS, setting ``environ`` may "
"cause memory leaks. Refer to the system documentation for :c:func:`!putenv`."
msgstr ""
"在包括 FreeBSD 與 macOS 在內的某些平台上，設定 ``environ`` 可能會導致記憶體洩"
"漏。請參閱系統中 :c:func:`!putenv` 的文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:603
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.putenv`` with arguments "
"``key``, ``value``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``key``、``value`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.putenv``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:605
msgid "The function is now always available."
msgstr "此函式現在都會是可用的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:611
msgid "Set the current process's effective group id."
msgstr "設定目前行程的有效群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:618
msgid "Set the current process's effective user id."
msgstr "設定目前行程的有效使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:625
msgid "Set the current process' group id."
msgstr "設定目前行程的群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:632
msgid ""
"Set the list of supplemental group ids associated with the current process "
"to *groups*. *groups* must be a sequence, and each element must be an "
"integer identifying a group. This operation is typically available only to "
"the superuser."
msgstr ""
"將與目前行程關聯的補充群組 ID 串列設定為 *groups*。*groups* 必須是一個序列，"
"且每個元素都必須是識別群組的整數。此操作通常只有超級使用者能夠使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:638
msgid ""
"On macOS, the length of *groups* may not exceed the system-defined maximum "
"number of effective group ids, typically 16. See the documentation "
"for :func:`getgroups` for cases where it may not return the same group list "
"set by calling setgroups()."
msgstr ""
"在 macOS 上，*groups* 的長度不得超過系統定義的有效群組 ID 最大數量，通常為 "
"16。關於它可能不會回傳與呼叫 setgroups() 所設定之群組串列相同結果的情況，請參"
"閱 :func:`getgroups` 的文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:645
msgid ""
"Reassociate the current thread with a Linux namespace. See "
"the :manpage:`setns(2)` and :manpage:`namespaces(7)` man pages for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"將目前執行緒重新關聯到一個 Linux 命名空間。更多細節請見 :manpage:`setns(2)` "
"和 :manpage:`namespaces(7)` 使用手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:649
msgid ""
"If *fd* refers to a :file:`/proc/{pid}/ns/` link, ``setns()`` reassociates "
"the calling thread with the namespace associated with that link, and "
"*nstype* may be set to one of the :ref:`CLONE_NEW* constants <os-unshare-"
"clone-flags>` to impose constraints on the operation (``0`` means no "
"constraints)."
msgstr ""
"如果 *fd* 指向一個 :file:`/proc/{pid}/ns/` 連結，``setns()`` 會將呼叫端執行緒"
"重新關聯到與該連結關聯的命名空間，而 *nstype* 可以設定為其中一"
"個 :ref:`CLONE_NEW* 常數 <os-unshare-clone-flags>`\\ 來對此操作施加限制"
"（``0`` 表示沒有限制）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:656
msgid ""
"Since Linux 5.8, *fd* may refer to a PID file descriptor obtained "
"from :func:`~os.pidfd_open`. In this case, ``setns()`` reassociates the "
"calling thread into one or more of the same namespaces as the thread "
"referred to by *fd*. This is subject to any constraints imposed by *nstype*, "
"which is a bit mask combining one or more of the :ref:`CLONE_NEW* constants "
"<os-unshare-clone-flags>`, e.g. ``setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWUTS | "
"os.CLONE_NEWPID)``. The caller's memberships in unspecified namespaces are "
"left unchanged."
msgstr ""
"自 Linux 5.8 起，*fd* 可以指向由 :func:`~os.pidfd_open` 取得的 PID 檔案描述"
"器。在這種情況下，``setns()`` 會將呼叫端執行緒重新關聯到與 *fd* 所指之執行緒"
"相同的一個或多個命名空間中。這會受到 *nstype* 所施加之任何限制的約束，"
"*nstype* 是一個結合了一個或多個 :ref:`CLONE_NEW* 常數 <os-unshare-clone-"
"flags>`\\ 的位元遮罩，例如 ``setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWUTS | os.CLONE_NEWPID)``。"
"呼叫者在未指定之命名空間中的成員資格會保持不變。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:665
msgid ""
"*fd* can be any object with a :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` method, or a raw "
"file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"*fd* 可以是任何具有 :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` 方法的物件，或是原始的檔案描述"
"器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:667
msgid ""
"This example reassociates the thread with the ``init`` process's network "
"namespace::"
msgstr "此範例會將執行緒重新關聯到 ``init`` 行程的網路命名空間： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:669
msgid ""
"fd = os.open(\"/proc/1/ns/net\", os.O_RDONLY)\n"
"os.setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWNET)\n"
"os.close(fd)"
msgstr ""
"fd = os.open(\"/proc/1/ns/net\", os.O_RDONLY)\n"
"os.setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWNET)\n"
"os.close(fd)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:679
msgid "The :func:`~os.unshare` function."
msgstr ":func:`~os.unshare` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:683
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setpgrp` or ``setpgrp(0, 0)`` depending on "
"which version is implemented (if any).  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"呼叫系統呼叫 :c:func:`!setpgrp` 或 ``setpgrp(0, 0)``，取決於實作的是哪個版本"
"（如果有的話）。語意請參閱 Unix 手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:691
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setpgid` to set the process group id of the "
"process with id *pid* to the process group with id *pgrp*.  See the Unix "
"manual for the semantics."
msgstr ""
"呼叫系統呼叫 :c:func:`!setpgid`，將 ID 為 *pid* 之行程的行程群組 ID 設定為 "
"ID 為 *pgrp* 的行程群組。語意請參閱 Unix 手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:702
msgid ""
"Set program scheduling priority. The value *which* is one "
"of :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, or :const:`PRIO_USER`, and "
"*who* is interpreted relative to *which* (a process identifier "
"for :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, process group identifier for :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, "
"and a user ID for :const:`PRIO_USER`). A zero value for *who* denotes "
"(respectively) the calling process, the process group of the calling "
"process, or the real user ID of the calling process. *priority* is a value "
"in the range -20 to 19. The default priority is 0; lower priorities cause "
"more favorable scheduling."
msgstr ""
"設定程式排程優先權。*which* 的值為 :const:`PRIO_PROCESS`、:const:`PRIO_PGRP` "
"或 :const:`PRIO_USER` 其中之一，而 *who* 會依據 *which* 來解讀"
"（:const:`PRIO_PROCESS` 為行程 ID、:const:`PRIO_PGRP` 為行程群組 "
"ID、:const:`PRIO_USER` 為使用者 ID）。*who* 的值為零時（分別）表示呼叫端行"
"程、呼叫端行程的行程群組或呼叫端行程的真實使用者 ID。*priority* 是介於 -20 "
"到 19 之間的值。預設優先權為 0；數值越低，排程時就越受優待。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:719
msgid "Set the current process's real and effective group ids."
msgstr "設定目前行程的真實與有效群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:726
msgid "Set the current process's real, effective, and saved group ids."
msgstr "設定目前行程的真實、有效與保存的群組 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:735
msgid "Set the current process's real, effective, and saved user ids."
msgstr "設定目前行程的真實、有效與保存的使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:744
msgid "Set the current process's real and effective user ids."
msgstr "設定目前行程的真實與有效使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:751
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!getsid`.  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr "呼叫系統呼叫 :c:func:`!getsid`。語意請參閱 Unix 手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:758
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setsid`.  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr "呼叫系統呼叫 :c:func:`!setsid`。語意請參閱 Unix 手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:767
msgid "Set the current process's user id."
msgstr "設定目前行程的使用者 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:775
msgid ""
"Return the error message corresponding to the error code in *code*. On "
"platforms where :c:func:`!strerror` returns ``NULL`` when given an unknown "
"error number, :exc:`ValueError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"回傳對應於 *code* 中錯誤碼的錯誤訊息。在給定未知錯誤編號時 :c:func:`!"
"strerror` 會回傳 ``NULL`` 的平台上，會引發 :exc:`ValueError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:782
msgid ""
"``True`` if the native OS type of the environment is bytes (eg. ``False`` on "
"Windows)."
msgstr ""
"如果環境的原生作業系統型別是位元組，則為 ``True``\\ （例如在 Windows 上為 "
"``False``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:790
msgid "Set the current numeric umask and return the previous umask."
msgstr "設定目前的數值 umask，並回傳先前的 umask。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:802
msgid ""
"Returns information identifying the current operating system. The return "
"value is a :class:`uname_result`."
msgstr "回傳識別目前作業系統的資訊。回傳值是一個 :class:`uname_result`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:805
msgid ""
"On macOS, iOS and Android, this returns the *kernel* name and release (i.e., "
"``'Darwin'`` on macOS and iOS; ``'Linux'`` on "
"Android). :func:`platform.uname` can be used to get the user-facing "
"operating system name and release on iOS and Android."
msgstr ""
"在 macOS、iOS 與 Android 上，此函式回傳的是\\ *核心*\\ 名稱與發行版本（即 "
"macOS 和 iOS 上為 ``'Darwin'``；Android 上為 ``'Linux'``）。在 iOS 與 "
"Android 上，可以使用 :func:`platform.uname` 取得面向使用者的作業系統名稱與發"
"行版本。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:811
msgid ":data:`sys.platform` which has finer granularity."
msgstr "粒度更細的 :data:`sys.platform`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:818 ../../library/os.rst:5661
msgid ""
"Return type changed from a tuple to a tuple-like object with named "
"attributes."
msgstr "回傳型別從元組改為具有具名屬性的類元組物件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:825
msgid ""
"Name and information about the system returned by :func:`os.uname`. These "
"attributes correspond to the members described in :manpage:`uname(2)`."
msgstr ""
"由 :func:`os.uname` 回傳的系統名稱與資訊。這些屬性對應於 :manpage:`uname(2)` "
"中描述的成員。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:828
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility, this object is also iterable, behaving like a "
"five-tuple "
"containing :attr:`~uname_result.sysname`, :attr:`~uname_result.nodename`, :attr:`~uname_result.release`, :attr:`~uname_result.version`, "
"and :attr:`~uname_result.machine` in that order."
msgstr ""
"為了向後相容，此物件也是可疊代的，其行為就像一個依序包"
"含 :attr:`~uname_result.sysname`、:attr:`~uname_result.nodename`、:attr:`~uname_result.release`、:attr:`~uname_result.version` "
"與 :attr:`~uname_result.machine` 的五元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:836
msgid "Operating system name."
msgstr "作業系統名稱。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:840
msgid ""
"Name of machine on network. Some systems "
"truncate :attr:`~uname_result.nodename` to 8 characters or to the leading "
"component; a better way to get the hostname is :func:`socket.gethostname` or "
"even ``socket.gethostbyaddr(socket.gethostname())``."
msgstr ""
"機器在網路上的名稱。有些系統會將 :attr:`~uname_result.nodename` 截斷為 8 個字"
"元或只保留開頭的部分；取得主機名稱更好的方式是 :func:`socket.gethostname`，或"
"甚至是 ``socket.gethostbyaddr(socket.gethostname())``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:847
msgid "Operating system release."
msgstr "作業系統發行版本。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:851
msgid "Operating system version."
msgstr "作業系統版本。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:855
msgid "Hardware identifier."
msgstr "硬體識別碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:862
msgid ""
"Unset (delete) the environment variable named *key*. Such changes to the "
"environment affect subprocesses started "
"with :func:`os.system`, :func:`popen` or :func:`fork` and :func:`execv`."
msgstr ""
"取消設定（刪除）名為 *key* 的環境變數。對環境的這類變更會影響"
"以 :func:`os.system`、:func:`popen` 或 :func:`fork` 和 :func:`execv` 啟動的子"
"行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:866
msgid ""
"Deletion of items in :data:`os.environ` is automatically translated into a "
"corresponding call to :func:`unsetenv`; however, calls to :func:`unsetenv` "
"don't update :data:`os.environ`, so it is actually preferable to delete "
"items of :data:`os.environ`."
msgstr ""
"刪除 :data:`os.environ` 中的項目會自動轉換為對應的 :func:`unsetenv` 呼叫；然"
"而，呼叫 :func:`unsetenv` 並不會更新 :data:`os.environ`，所以實際上更建議直接"
"刪除 :data:`os.environ` 的項目。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:875
msgid "The function is now always available and is also available on Windows."
msgstr "此函式現在一律可用，在 Windows 上也可使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:881
msgid ""
"Disassociate parts of the process execution context, and move them into a "
"newly created namespace. See the :manpage:`unshare(2)` man page for more "
"details. The *flags* argument is a bit mask, combining zero or more of "
"the :ref:`CLONE_* constants <os-unshare-clone-flags>`, that specifies which "
"parts of the execution context should be unshared from their existing "
"associations and moved to a new namespace. If the *flags* argument is ``0``, "
"no changes are made to the calling process's execution context."
msgstr ""
"將行程執行情境的部分內容解除關聯，並將它們移到一個新建立的命名空間中。更多細"
"節請見 :manpage:`unshare(2)` 使用手冊。*flags* 引數是一個位元遮罩，結合零個或"
"多個 :ref:`CLONE_* 常數 <os-unshare-clone-flags>`，用來指定執行情境的哪些部分"
"應從其既有的關聯中解除共享 (unshare)，並移到新的命名空間。如果 *flags* 引數"
"為 ``0``，則不會對呼叫端行程的執行情境做任何變更。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:898
msgid "The :func:`~os.setns` function."
msgstr ":func:`~os.setns` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:902
msgid ""
"Flags to the :func:`unshare` function, if the implementation supports them. "
"See :manpage:`unshare(2)` in the Linux manual for their exact effect and "
"availability."
msgstr ""
"如果實作有支援，這些是 :func:`unshare` 函式的旗標。它們的確切效果與可用性請參"
"閱 Linux 使用手冊中的 :manpage:`unshare(2)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:925
msgid "File Object Creation"
msgstr "建立檔案物件"

#: ../../library/os.rst:927
msgid ""
"These functions create new :term:`file objects <file object>`.  (See "
"also :func:`~os.open` for opening file descriptors.)"
msgstr ""
"這些函式會建立新的\\ :term:`檔案物件 <file object>`。（另請參閱用來開啟檔案描"
"述器的 :func:`~os.open`。）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:933
msgid ""
"Return an open file object connected to the file descriptor *fd*.  This is "
"an alias of the :func:`open` built-in function and accepts the same "
"arguments. The only difference is that the first argument of :func:`fdopen` "
"must always be an integer."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個連接到檔案描述器 *fd* 的已開啟檔案物件。這是內建函式 :func:`open` 的"
"別名，並接受相同的引數。唯一的差別是 :func:`fdopen` 的第一個引數必須永遠是整"
"數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:942
msgid "File Descriptor Operations"
msgstr "檔案描述器操作"

#: ../../library/os.rst:944
msgid ""
"These functions operate on I/O streams referenced using file descriptors."
msgstr "這些函式會對以檔案描述器參照的 I/O 串流進行操作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:946
msgid ""
"File descriptors are small integers corresponding to a file that has been "
"opened by the current process.  For example, standard input is usually file "
"descriptor 0, standard output is 1, and standard error is 2.  Further files "
"opened by a process will then be assigned 3, 4, 5, and so forth.  The name "
"\"file descriptor\" is slightly deceptive; on Unix platforms, sockets and "
"pipes are also referenced by file descriptors."
msgstr ""
"檔案描述器是對應於目前行程所開啟之檔案的小整數。舉例來說，標準輸入通常是檔案"
"描述器 0，標準輸出是 1，標準錯誤是 2。行程之後再開啟的檔案則會被指派為 3、4、"
"5，依此類推。「檔案描述器」這個名稱有點容易誤導；在 Unix 平台上，socket 和管"
"道 (pipe) 也是透過檔案描述器來參照的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:953
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` method can be used to obtain the file "
"descriptor associated with a :term:`file object` when required.  Note that "
"using the file descriptor directly will bypass the file object methods, "
"ignoring aspects such as internal buffering of data."
msgstr ""
"在需要時，可以使用 :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` 方法取得與\\ :term:`檔案物件 "
"<file object>`\\ 關聯的檔案描述器。請注意，直接使用檔案描述器會繞過檔案物件的"
"方法，忽略諸如資料的內部緩衝等面向。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:961
msgid "Close file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "關閉檔案描述器 *fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:965
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To close a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or "
"by :func:`popen` or :func:`fdopen`, use its :meth:`~io.IOBase.close` method."
msgstr ""
"此函式用於低階 I/O，且必須套用在由 :func:`os.open` 或 :func:`pipe` 回傳的檔案"
"描述器上。若要關閉由內建函式 :func:`open`、:func:`popen` 或 :func:`fdopen` 回"
"傳的「檔案物件」，請使用其 :meth:`~io.IOBase.close` 方法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:973
msgid ""
"Close all file descriptors from *fd_low* (inclusive) to *fd_high* "
"(exclusive), ignoring errors. Equivalent to (but much faster than)::"
msgstr ""
"關閉從 *fd_low*\\ （包含）到 *fd_high*\\ （不包含）的所有檔案描述器，並忽略錯"
"誤。等同於下列程式碼（但快得多）： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:976
msgid ""
"for fd in range(fd_low, fd_high):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        os.close(fd)\n"
"    except OSError:\n"
"        pass"
msgstr ""
"for fd in range(fd_low, fd_high):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        os.close(fd)\n"
"    except OSError:\n"
"        pass"

#: ../../library/os.rst:985
msgid ""
"Copy *count* bytes from file descriptor *src*, starting from offset "
"*offset_src*, to file descriptor *dst*, starting from offset *offset_dst*. "
"If *offset_src* is ``None``, then *src* is read from the current position; "
"respectively for *offset_dst*."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *src* 的偏移量 *offset_src* 開始，複製 *count* 個位元組到檔案描"
"述器 *dst* 的偏移量 *offset_dst* 處。如果 *offset_src* 為 ``None``，則會從目"
"前位置讀取 *src*；*offset_dst* 亦同，此時會從目前位置寫入 *dst*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:990
msgid ""
"In Linux kernel older than 5.3, the files pointed to by *src* and *dst* must "
"reside in the same filesystem, otherwise an :exc:`OSError` is raised "
"with :attr:`~OSError.errno` set to :const:`errno.EXDEV`."
msgstr ""
"在 5.3 版之前的 Linux 核心中，*src* 和 *dst* 所指向的檔案必須位於同一個檔案系"
"統，否則會引發 :exc:`OSError`，且其 :attr:`~OSError.errno` 會被設"
"為 :const:`errno.EXDEV`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:994
msgid ""
"This copy is done without the additional cost of transferring data from the "
"kernel to user space and then back into the kernel. Additionally, some "
"filesystems could implement extra optimizations, such as the use of reflinks "
"(i.e., two or more inodes that share pointers to the same copy-on-write disk "
"blocks; supported file systems include btrfs and XFS) and server-side copy "
"(in the case of NFS)."
msgstr ""
"此複製操作不會產生將資料從核心傳輸到使用者空間、再送回核心的額外成本。此外，"
"有些檔案系統可以實作額外的最佳化，例如使用 reflink（即兩個或多個 inode 共享指"
"向同一個寫入時複製 (copy-on-write) 磁碟區塊的指標；支援的檔案系統包括 btrfs "
"和 XFS），以及伺服器端複製（在 NFS 的情況下）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1001
msgid ""
"The function copies bytes between two file descriptors. Text options, like "
"the encoding and the line ending, are ignored."
msgstr "此函式會在兩個檔案描述器之間複製位元組。編碼和行尾等文字選項會被忽略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1004
msgid ""
"The return value is the amount of bytes copied. This could be less than the "
"amount requested."
msgstr "回傳值是已複製的位元組數量，這可能會少於所請求的數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1009
msgid ""
"On Linux, :func:`os.copy_file_range` should not be used for copying a range "
"of a pseudo file from a special filesystem like procfs and sysfs. It will "
"always copy no bytes and return 0 as if the file was empty because of a "
"known Linux kernel issue."
msgstr ""
"在 Linux 上，不應使用 :func:`os.copy_file_range` 從 procfs 和 sysfs 等特殊檔"
"案系統複製偽檔案 (pseudo file) 的某個範圍。由於一個已知的 Linux 核心問題，它"
"一律不會複製任何位元組，並且會回傳 0，就像檔案是空的一樣。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1021
msgid ""
"Return a string describing the encoding of the device associated with *fd* "
"if it is connected to a terminal; else return :const:`None`."
msgstr ""
"如果 *fd* 連接到終端機，則回傳描述其所關聯裝置之編碼的字串；否則回"
"傳 :const:`None`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1024
msgid ""
"On Unix, if the :ref:`Python UTF-8 Mode <utf8-mode>` is enabled, return "
"``'UTF-8'`` rather than the device encoding."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，如果啟用了 :ref:`Python UTF-8 模式 <utf8-mode>`，則回傳 "
"``'UTF-8'`` 而非裝置編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1027
msgid "On Unix, the function now implements the Python UTF-8 Mode."
msgstr "在 Unix 上，此函式現在實作了 Python UTF-8 模式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1033
msgid ""
"Return a duplicate of file descriptor *fd*. The new file descriptor "
"is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"回傳檔案描述器 *fd* 的副本。新的檔案描述器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 "
"<fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1036
msgid ""
"On Windows, when duplicating a standard stream (0: stdin, 1: stdout, 2: "
"stderr), the new file descriptor is :ref:`inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，複製標準串流（0：stdin、1：stdout、2：stderr）時，新的檔案描述"
"器為\\ :ref:`可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1042 ../../library/os.rst:1324
msgid "The new file descriptor is now non-inheritable."
msgstr "新的檔案描述器現在是不可繼承的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1048
msgid ""
"Duplicate file descriptor *fd* to *fd2*, closing the latter first if "
"necessary. Return *fd2*. The new file descriptor is :ref:`inheritable "
"<fd_inheritance>` by default or non-inheritable if *inheritable* is "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
"將檔案描述器 *fd* 複製到 *fd2*，必要時會先關閉後者。回傳 *fd2*。新的檔案描述"
"器預設為\\ :ref:`可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`，若 *inheritable* 為 ``False`` 則為"
"不可繼承。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1055
msgid "Add the optional *inheritable* parameter."
msgstr "新增可選的 *inheritable* 參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1058
msgid "Return *fd2* on success. Previously, ``None`` was always returned."
msgstr "成功時回傳 *fd2*。以前總是回傳 ``None``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1064
msgid ""
"Change the mode of the file given by *fd* to the numeric *mode*.  See the "
"docs for :func:`chmod` for possible values of *mode*.  As of Python 3.3, "
"this is equivalent to ``os.chmod(fd, mode)``."
msgstr ""
"將 *fd* 所指定之檔案的模式更改為數值 *mode*。*mode* 可能的值請參"
"閱 :func:`chmod` 的文件。從 Python 3.3 開始，這等同於 ``os.chmod(fd, "
"mode)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1068 ../../library/os.rst:2267
#: ../../library/os.rst:2368
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.chmod`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``mode``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``mode``、``dir_fd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``os.chmod``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1072 ../../library/os.rst:1090
#: ../../library/os.rst:1178 ../../library/os.rst:1811
#: ../../library/os.rst:2264 ../../library/os.rst:2297
#: ../../library/os.rst:4099
msgid ""
"The function is limited on WASI, see :ref:`wasm-availability` for more "
"information."
msgstr "此函式在 WASI 上有所限制，詳情請參閱 :ref:`wasm-availability`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1075 ../../library/os.rst:2375
msgid "Added support on Windows."
msgstr "新增對 Windows 的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1081
msgid ""
"Change the owner and group id of the file given by *fd* to the numeric *uid* "
"and *gid*.  To leave one of the ids unchanged, set it to -1.  "
"See :func:`chown`.  As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.chown(fd, "
"uid, gid)``."
msgstr ""
"將 *fd* 所指定之檔案的擁有者和群組 ID 更改為數值 *uid* 和 *gid*。若要讓其中一"
"個 ID 保持不變，請將其設為 -1。請參閱 :func:`chown`。從 Python 3.3 開始，這等"
"同於 ``os.chown(fd, uid, gid)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1086 ../../library/os.rst:2293
#: ../../library/os.rst:2384
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.chown`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``uid``, ``gid``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``uid``、``gid``、``dir_fd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``os.chown``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1096
msgid ""
"Force write of file with filedescriptor *fd* to disk. Does not force update "
"of metadata."
msgstr "強制將檔案描述器為 *fd* 的檔案寫入磁碟。不會強制更新詮釋資料。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1104
msgid ""
"Return system configuration information relevant to an open file. *name* "
"specifies the configuration value to retrieve; it may be a string which is "
"the name of a defined system value; these names are specified in a number of "
"standards (POSIX.1, Unix 95, Unix 98, and others).  Some platforms define "
"additional names as well.  The names known to the host operating system are "
"given in the ``pathconf_names`` dictionary.  For configuration variables not "
"included in that mapping, passing an integer for *name* is also accepted."
msgstr ""
"回傳與已開啟檔案相關的系統設定資訊。*name* 指定要取得的設定值；它可以是一個字"
"串，為已定義之系統值的名稱；這些名稱定義於多項標準中（POSIX.1、Unix 95、Unix "
"98 等）。有些平台也會定義額外的名稱。主機作業系統已知的名稱列在 "
"``pathconf_names`` 字典中。對於未包含在該對映中的設定變數，也可以傳入整數作"
"為 *name*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1112 ../../library/os.rst:2727
msgid ""
"If *name* is a string and is not known, :exc:`ValueError` is raised.  If a "
"specific value for *name* is not supported by the host system, even if it is "
"included in ``pathconf_names``, an :exc:`OSError` is raised "
"with :const:`errno.EINVAL` for the error number."
msgstr ""
"如果 *name* 是字串但未知，會引發 :exc:`ValueError`。如果主機系統不支援 "
"*name* 的特定值，即使它包含在 ``pathconf_names`` 中，也會引"
"發 :exc:`OSError`，其錯誤編號為 :const:`errno.EINVAL`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1117
msgid "As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.pathconf(fd, name)``."
msgstr "從 Python 3.3 開始，這等同於 ``os.pathconf(fd, name)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1124
msgid ""
"Get the status of the file descriptor *fd*. Return a :class:`stat_result` "
"object."
msgstr "取得檔案描述器 *fd* 的狀態。回傳一個 :class:`stat_result` 物件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1127
msgid "As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.stat(fd)``."
msgstr "從 Python 3.3 開始，這等同於 ``os.stat(fd)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1131 ../../library/os.rst:2536
msgid "The :func:`.stat` function."
msgstr ":func:`.stat` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1136
msgid ""
"Return information about the filesystem containing the file associated with "
"file descriptor *fd* in a :class:`statvfs_result`, like :func:`statvfs`. As "
"of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.statvfs(fd)``."
msgstr ""
"以 :class:`statvfs_result` 回傳包含與檔案描述器 *fd* 關聯之檔案的檔案系統資"
"訊，就像 :func:`statvfs` 一樣。從 Python 3.3 開始，這等同於 "
"``os.statvfs(fd)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1145
msgid ""
"Force write of file with filedescriptor *fd* to disk.  On Unix, this calls "
"the native :c:func:`!fsync` function; on Windows, the MS :c:func:`!_commit` "
"function."
msgstr ""
"強制將檔案描述器為 *fd* 的檔案寫入磁碟。在 Unix 上，這會呼叫原生的 :c:func:`!"
"fsync` 函式；在 Windows 上則是 MS 的 :c:func:`!_commit` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1148
msgid ""
"If you're starting with a buffered Python :term:`file object` *f*, first do "
"``f.flush()``, and then do ``os.fsync(f.fileno())``, to ensure that all "
"internal buffers associated with *f* are written to disk."
msgstr ""
"如果你一開始使用的是有緩衝的 Python :term:`檔案物件 <file object>` *f*，請先"
"執行 ``f.flush()``，再執行 ``os.fsync(f.fileno())``，以確保與 *f* 關聯的所有"
"內部緩衝區都會寫入磁碟。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1157
msgid ""
"Truncate the file corresponding to file descriptor *fd*, so that it is at "
"most *length* bytes in size.  As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to "
"``os.truncate(fd, length)``."
msgstr ""
"截斷與檔案描述器 *fd* 對應的檔案，使其大小最多為 *length* 個位元組。從 "
"Python 3.3 開始，這等同於 ``os.truncate(fd, length)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1161
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.truncate`` with arguments "
"``fd``, ``length``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``fd``、``length`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.truncate``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1165 ../../library/os.rst:4138
msgid "Added support for Windows"
msgstr "新增對 Windows 的支援"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1171
msgid ""
"Get the blocking mode of the file descriptor: ``False`` if "
"the :data:`O_NONBLOCK` flag is set, ``True`` if the flag is cleared."
msgstr ""
"取得檔案描述器的阻塞模式：如果設定了 :data:`O_NONBLOCK` 旗標則為 ``False``，"
"如果該旗標已清除則為 ``True``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1174
msgid "See also :func:`set_blocking` and :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."
msgstr "另請參閱 :func:`set_blocking` 與 :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1181 ../../library/os.rst:1814
msgid "On Windows, this function is limited to pipes."
msgstr "在 Windows 上，此函式僅限用於管道。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1185 ../../library/os.rst:1818
msgid "Added support for pipes on Windows."
msgstr "新增對 Windows 上管道的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1191
msgid ""
"Grant access to the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the master "
"pseudo-terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The file "
"descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"授予對從屬 (slave) 偽終端裝置的存取權，該裝置與檔案描述器 *fd* 所指的主 "
"(master) 偽終端裝置相關聯。失敗時不會關閉檔案描述器 *fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1195
msgid "Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`grantpt`."
msgstr "呼叫 C 標準函式庫函式 :c:func:`grantpt`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1204
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the file descriptor *fd* is open and connected to a tty(-"
"like) device, else ``False``."
msgstr ""
"如果檔案描述器 *fd* 已開啟並連接到 tty（或類 tty）裝置，則回傳 ``True``，否則"
"回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1210
msgid ""
"Apply, test or remove a POSIX lock on an open file descriptor. *fd* is an "
"open file descriptor. *cmd* specifies the command to use - one "
"of :data:`F_LOCK`, :data:`F_TLOCK`, :data:`F_ULOCK` or :data:`F_TEST`. *len* "
"specifies the section of the file to lock."
msgstr ""
"在已開啟的檔案描述器上套用、測試或移除 POSIX 鎖。*fd* 是一個已開啟的檔案描述"
"器。*cmd* 指定要使用的命令，"
"為 :data:`F_LOCK`、:data:`F_TLOCK`、:data:`F_ULOCK` 或 :data:`F_TEST` 其中之"
"一。*len* 指定要鎖定的檔案區段。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1216
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.lockf`` with arguments "
"``fd``, ``cmd``, ``len``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``fd``、``cmd``、``len`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.lockf``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1228
msgid "Flags that specify what action :func:`lockf` will take."
msgstr "指定 :func:`lockf` 將採取何種動作的旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1237
msgid ""
"Prepare the tty of which fd is a file descriptor for a new login session. "
"Make the calling process a session leader; make the tty the controlling tty, "
"the stdin, the stdout, and the stderr of the calling process; close fd."
msgstr ""
"為新的登入 session 準備 tty，fd 是該 tty 的檔案描述器。讓呼叫端行程成為 "
"session 領導者 (session leader)；讓該 tty 成為呼叫端行程的控制 tty、stdin、"
"stdout 與 stderr；關閉 fd。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1248
msgid ""
"Set the current position of file descriptor *fd* to position *pos*, modified "
"by *whence*, and return the new position in bytes relative to the start of "
"the file. Valid values for *whence* are:"
msgstr ""
"將檔案描述器 *fd* 的目前位置設定為位置 *pos*，並依 *whence* 進行調整，然後回"
"傳相對於檔案開頭的新位置（以位元組為單位）。*whence* 的有效值為："

#: ../../library/os.rst:1253
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_SET` or ``0`` -- set *pos* relative to the beginning of the file"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_SET` 或 ``0`` -- 將 *pos* 設定為相對於檔案的開頭"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1254
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_CUR` or ``1`` -- set *pos* relative to the current file position"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_CUR` 或 ``1`` -- 將 *pos* 設定為相對於目前的檔案位置"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1255
msgid ":const:`SEEK_END` or ``2`` -- set *pos* relative to the end of the file"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_END` 或 ``2`` -- 將 *pos* 設定為相對於檔案的結尾"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1256
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_DATA` -- set *pos* to the next data location, relative to *pos*"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_DATA` -- 將 *pos* 設定為相對於 *pos* 的下一個資料位置"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1257
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_HOLE` -- set *pos* to the next data hole, relative to *pos*"
msgstr ""
":const:`SEEK_HOLE` -- 將 *pos* 設定為相對於 *pos* 的下一個資料空洞 (hole)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1261
msgid "Add support for :const:`!SEEK_HOLE` and :const:`!SEEK_DATA`."
msgstr "新增對 :const:`!SEEK_HOLE` 和 :const:`!SEEK_DATA` 的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1268
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`lseek` function and the :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` "
"method on :term:`file-like objects <file object>`, for whence to adjust the "
"file position indicator."
msgstr ""
":func:`lseek` 函式與\\ :term:`類檔案物件 <file object>`\\ "
"之 :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` 方法的參數，作為 whence 用來調整檔案位置指示器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1272
msgid ":const:`SEEK_SET`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_SET`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1273
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the beginning of the file."
msgstr "相對於檔案的開頭調整檔案位置。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1274
msgid ":const:`SEEK_CUR`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_CUR`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1275
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the current file position."
msgstr "相對於目前的檔案位置調整檔案位置。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1276
msgid ":const:`SEEK_END`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_END`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1277
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the end of the file."
msgstr "相對於檔案的結尾調整檔案位置。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1279
msgid "Their values are 0, 1, and 2, respectively."
msgstr "它們的值分別為 0、1 和 2。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1285
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`lseek` function and the :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` "
"method on :term:`file-like objects <file object>`, for seeking file data and "
"holes on sparsely allocated files."
msgstr ""
":func:`lseek` 函式與\\ :term:`類檔案物件 <file object>`\\ "
"之 :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` 方法的參數，用於在稀疏配置的檔案中搜尋資料與空洞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1289
msgid ":data:`!SEEK_DATA`"
msgstr ":data:`!SEEK_DATA`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1290
msgid ""
"Adjust the file offset to the next location containing data, relative to the "
"seek position."
msgstr "將檔案偏移量調整到從 seek 位置起算、下一個包含資料的位置。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1293
msgid ":data:`!SEEK_HOLE`"
msgstr ":data:`!SEEK_HOLE`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1294
msgid ""
"Adjust the file offset to the next location containing a hole, relative to "
"the seek position. A hole is defined as a sequence of zeros."
msgstr ""
"將檔案偏移量調整到從 seek 位置起算、下一個包含空洞的位置。空洞的定義是一連串"
"的零。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1300
msgid "These operations only make sense for filesystems that support them."
msgstr "這些操作只對支援它們的檔案系統有意義。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1309
msgid ""
"Open the file *path* and set various flags according to *flags* and possibly "
"its mode according to *mode*.  When computing *mode*, the current umask "
"value is first masked out.  Return the file descriptor for the newly opened "
"file. The new file descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"開啟檔案 *path*，並根據 *flags* 設定各種旗標，可能還會根據 *mode* 設定其模"
"式。在計算 *mode* 時，會先遮罩掉目前的 umask 值。回傳新開啟檔案的檔案描述器。"
"新的檔案描述器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1314
msgid ""
"For a description of the flag and mode values, see the C run-time "
"documentation; flag constants (like :const:`O_RDONLY` and :const:`O_WRONLY`) "
"are defined in the :mod:`!os` module.  In particular, on Windows "
"adding :const:`O_BINARY` is needed to open files in binary mode."
msgstr ""
"關於旗標與模式值的說明，請參閱 C runtime 文件；旗標常數（例"
"如 :const:`O_RDONLY` 和 :const:`O_WRONLY`）定義在 :mod:`!os` 模組中。特別是"
"在 Windows 上，需要加上 :const:`O_BINARY` 才能以二進位模式開啟檔案。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1319
msgid ""
"This function can support :ref:`paths relative to directory descriptors "
"<dir_fd>` with the *dir_fd* parameter."
msgstr ""
"此函式可以支援以 *dir_fd* 參數使用\\ :ref:`相對於目錄描述器的路徑 <dir_fd>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1322
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``open`` with arguments ``path``, "
"``mode``, ``flags``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``mode``、``flags`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``open``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1329
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O.  For normal usage, use the "
"built-in function :func:`open`, which returns a :term:`file object` "
"with :meth:`~io.BufferedIOBase.read` and :meth:`~io.BufferedIOBase.write` "
"methods. To wrap a file descriptor in a file object, use :func:`fdopen`."
msgstr ""
"此函式用於低階 I/O。一般用途請使用內建函式 :func:`open`，它會回傳一個具"
"有 :meth:`~io.BufferedIOBase.read` 和 :meth:`~io.BufferedIOBase.write` 方法的"
"\\ :term:`檔案物件 <file object>`。若要將檔案描述器包裝成檔案物件，請使"
"用 :func:`fdopen`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1334 ../../library/os.rst:2541
#: ../../library/os.rst:2581 ../../library/os.rst:2664
#: ../../library/os.rst:2686 ../../library/os.rst:2774
#: ../../library/os.rst:2804 ../../library/os.rst:2911
#: ../../library/os.rst:4154
msgid "Added the *dir_fd* parameter."
msgstr "新增 *dir_fd* 參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1337 ../../library/os.rst:1709
#: ../../library/os.rst:1944 ../../library/os.rst:5757
msgid ""
"If the system call is interrupted and the signal handler does not raise an "
"exception, the function now retries the system call instead of raising "
"an :exc:`InterruptedError` exception (see :pep:`475` for the rationale)."
msgstr ""
"如果系統呼叫被中斷，但訊號處理程式沒有引發例外，此函式現在會重試系統呼叫，而"
"不是引發 :exc:`InterruptedError` 例外（原因詳見 :pep:`475`）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1342 ../../library/os.rst:2155
#: ../../library/os.rst:2192 ../../library/os.rst:2223
#: ../../library/os.rst:2273 ../../library/os.rst:2314
#: ../../library/os.rst:2354 ../../library/os.rst:2372
#: ../../library/os.rst:2388 ../../library/os.rst:2448
#: ../../library/os.rst:2544 ../../library/os.rst:2584
#: ../../library/os.rst:2635 ../../library/os.rst:2667
#: ../../library/os.rst:2689 ../../library/os.rst:2737
#: ../../library/os.rst:2807 ../../library/os.rst:2826
#: ../../library/os.rst:2914 ../../library/os.rst:3222
#: ../../library/os.rst:3823 ../../library/os.rst:4141
#: ../../library/os.rst:4157 ../../library/os.rst:4198
#: ../../library/os.rst:4301 ../../library/os.rst:4362
#: ../../library/os.rst:4759 ../../library/os.rst:4943
#: ../../library/os.rst:5516
msgid "Accepts a :term:`path-like object`."
msgstr "接受一個\\ :term:`類路徑物件 <path-like object>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1345
msgid ""
"The following constants are options for the *flags* parameter to "
"the :func:`~os.open` function.  They can be combined using the bitwise OR "
"operator ``|``.  Some of them are not available on all platforms.  For "
"descriptions of their availability and use, consult the :manpage:`open(2)` "
"manual page on Unix or `the MSDN <https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/"
"z0kc8e3z.aspx>`_ on Windows."
msgstr ""
"下列常數是 :func:`~os.open` 函式之 *flags* 參數的選項。它們可以使用位元 OR 運"
"算子 ``|`` 組合。其中有些並非在所有平台上都可用。關於它們的可用性與用法說明，"
"請參閱 Unix 上的 :manpage:`open(2)` 使用手冊，或 Windows 上的 `MSDN <https://"
"msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/z0kc8e3z.aspx>`_。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1360
msgid "The above constants are available on Unix and Windows."
msgstr "上述常數在 Unix 和 Windows 上皆可使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1371
msgid "The above constants are only available on Unix."
msgstr "上述常數僅在 Unix 上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1373
msgid "Add :data:`O_CLOEXEC` constant."
msgstr "新增 :data:`O_CLOEXEC` 常數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1384
msgid "The above constants are only available on Windows."
msgstr "上述常數僅在 Windows 上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1391
msgid "The above constants are only available on macOS."
msgstr "上述常數僅在 macOS 上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1393
msgid ""
"Add :data:`O_EVTONLY`, :data:`O_FSYNC`, :data:`O_SYMLINK` "
"and :data:`O_NOFOLLOW_ANY` constants."
msgstr ""
"新增 :data:`O_EVTONLY`、:data:`O_FSYNC`、:data:`O_SYMLINK` "
"和 :data:`O_NOFOLLOW_ANY` 常數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1407
msgid ""
"The above constants are extensions and not present if they are not defined "
"by the C library."
msgstr "上述常數為擴充功能，若 C 函式庫未定義它們，則不會存在。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1410
msgid ""
"Add :data:`O_PATH` on systems that support it. Add :data:`O_TMPFILE`, only "
"available on Linux Kernel 3.11   or newer."
msgstr ""
"在支援的系統上新增 :data:`O_PATH`。新增 :data:`O_TMPFILE`，僅在 Linux 核心 "
"3.11 或更新版本上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1420
msgid ""
"Open a new pseudo-terminal pair. Return a pair of file descriptors "
"``(master, slave)`` for the pty and the tty, respectively. The new file "
"descriptors are :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`. For a (slightly) "
"more portable approach, use the :mod:`pty` module."
msgstr ""
"開啟一對新的偽終端。回傳一對檔案描述器 ``(master, slave)``，分別對應 pty 與 "
"tty。新的檔案描述器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。若要使用（稍微）更"
"具可移植性的方法，請使用 :mod:`pty` 模組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1427 ../../library/os.rst:1439
msgid "The new file descriptors are now non-inheritable."
msgstr "新的檔案描述器現在是不可繼承的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1433
msgid ""
"Create a pipe.  Return a pair of file descriptors ``(r, w)`` usable for "
"reading and writing, respectively. The new file descriptor is :ref:`non-"
"inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"建立一個管道。回傳一對檔案描述器 ``(r, w)``，分別可用於讀取和寫入。新的檔案描"
"述器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1445
msgid ""
"Create a pipe with *flags* set atomically. *flags* can be constructed by "
"ORing together one or more of these "
"values: :data:`O_NONBLOCK`, :data:`O_CLOEXEC`. Return a pair of file "
"descriptors ``(r, w)`` usable for reading and writing, respectively."
msgstr ""
"建立一個以原子方式設定 *flags* 的管道。*flags* 可以透過將下列一個或多個值做 "
"OR 運算來建構：:data:`O_NONBLOCK`、:data:`O_CLOEXEC`。回傳一對檔案描述器 "
"``(r, w)``，分別可用於讀取和寫入。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1458
msgid ""
"Ensures that enough disk space is allocated for the file specified by *fd* "
"starting from *offset* and continuing for *len* bytes."
msgstr ""
"確保為 *fd* 所指定的檔案配置足夠的磁碟空間，範圍從 *offset* 開始，持續 *len* "
"個位元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1468
msgid ""
"Announces an intention to access data in a specific pattern thus allowing "
"the kernel to make optimizations. The advice applies to the region of the "
"file specified by *fd* starting at *offset* and continuing for *len* bytes. "
"*advice* is one "
"of :data:`POSIX_FADV_NORMAL`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_RANDOM`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED` "
"or :data:`POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED`."
msgstr ""
"宣告以特定模式存取資料的意圖，讓核心得以進行最佳化。此建議適用於 *fd* 所指定"
"之檔案中從 *offset* 開始、持續 *len* 個位元組的區域。*advice* "
"為 :data:`POSIX_FADV_NORMAL`、:data:`POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL`、:data:`POSIX_FADV_RANDOM`、:data:`POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE`、:data:`POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED` "
"或 :data:`POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED` 其中之一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1488
msgid ""
"Flags that can be used in *advice* in :func:`posix_fadvise` that specify the "
"access pattern that is likely to be used."
msgstr ""
"可用於 :func:`posix_fadvise` 之 *advice* 的旗標，用來指定可能使用的存取模式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1498
msgid ""
"Read at most *n* bytes from file descriptor *fd* at a position of *offset*, "
"leaving the file offset unchanged."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *fd* 的 *offset* 位置讀取最多 *n* 個位元組，並保持檔案偏移量不"
"變。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1501 ../../library/os.rst:1698
msgid ""
"Return a bytestring containing the bytes read. If the end of the file "
"referred to by *fd* has been reached, an empty bytes object is returned."
msgstr ""
"回傳包含所讀取位元組的位元組串。如果已經到達 *fd* 所指檔案的結尾，則回傳空的"
"位元組物件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1511
msgid "Open and return a file descriptor for a master pseudo-terminal device."
msgstr "開啟並回傳主偽終端裝置的檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1513
msgid ""
"Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`posix_openpt`. The *oflag* "
"argument is used to set file status flags and file access modes as specified "
"in the manual page of :c:func:`posix_openpt` of your system."
msgstr ""
"呼叫 C 標準函式庫函式 :c:func:`posix_openpt`。*oflag* 引數用來設定檔案狀態旗"
"標與檔案存取模式，如你系統上 :c:func:`posix_openpt` 使用手冊中所述。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1517
msgid ""
"The returned file descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`. If "
"the value :data:`O_CLOEXEC` is available on the system, it is added to "
"*oflag*."
msgstr ""
"回傳的檔案描述器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。如果系統上"
"有 :data:`O_CLOEXEC` 值，它會被加入 *oflag* 中。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1528
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* at a position of *offset* into "
"mutable :term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>` *buffers*, leaving "
"the file offset unchanged.  Transfer data into each buffer until it is full "
"and then move on to the next buffer in the sequence to hold the rest of the "
"data."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *fd* 的 *offset* 位置讀取資料到可變的\\ :term:`類位元組串物件 "
"<bytes-like object>` *buffers* 中，並保持檔案偏移量不變。資料會被傳入每個緩衝"
"區直到填滿，再移到序列中的下一個緩衝區來存放其餘資料。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1533 ../../library/os.rst:1637
msgid ""
"The flags argument contains a bitwise OR of zero or more of the following "
"flags:"
msgstr "flags 引數包含零個或多個下列旗標的位元 OR 結果："

#: ../../library/os.rst:1536
msgid ":data:`RWF_HIPRI`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_HIPRI`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1537
msgid ":data:`RWF_NOWAIT`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_NOWAIT`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1538 ../../library/os.rst:1643
msgid ":data:`RWF_DONTCACHE`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_DONTCACHE`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1540 ../../library/os.rst:1881
msgid ""
"Return the total number of bytes actually read which can be less than the "
"total capacity of all the objects."
msgstr "回傳實際讀取的位元組總數，這可能會少於所有物件的總容量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1543 ../../library/os.rst:1648
#: ../../library/os.rst:1884 ../../library/os.rst:1959
msgid ""
"The operating system may set a limit (:func:`sysconf` value "
"``'SC_IOV_MAX'``) on the number of buffers that can be used."
msgstr ""
"作業系統可能會對可使用的緩衝區數量設下限制（:func:`sysconf` 值 "
"``'SC_IOV_MAX'``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1546
msgid "Combine the functionality of :func:`os.readv` and :func:`os.pread`."
msgstr "結合 :func:`os.readv` 與 :func:`os.pread` 的功能。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1550 ../../library/os.rst:1655
msgid "Using flags requires Linux >= 4.6."
msgstr "使用 flags 需要 Linux >= 4.6。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1557
msgid ""
"Do not wait for data which is not immediately available. If this flag is "
"specified, the system call will return instantly if it would have to read "
"data from the backing storage or wait for a lock."
msgstr ""
"不等待無法立即取得的資料。如果指定了此旗標，當系統呼叫必須從後端儲存裝置讀取"
"資料或等待鎖時，就會立即回傳。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1561
msgid ""
"If some data was successfully read, it will return the number of bytes read. "
"If no bytes were read, it will return ``-1`` and set errno "
"to :const:`errno.EAGAIN`."
msgstr ""
"如果成功讀取了一些資料，它會回傳讀取的位元組數。如果沒有讀取到任何位元組，它"
"會回傳 ``-1`` 並將 errno 設為 :const:`errno.EAGAIN`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1572
msgid ""
"High priority read/write. Allows block-based filesystems to use polling of "
"the device, which provides lower latency, but may use additional resources."
msgstr ""
"高優先權的讀取／寫入。允許以區塊為基礎的檔案系統對裝置使用輪詢 (polling)，這"
"能提供較低的延遲，但可能會使用額外的資源。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1576
msgid ""
"Currently, on Linux, this feature is usable only on a file descriptor opened "
"using the :data:`O_DIRECT` flag."
msgstr ""
"目前在 Linux 上，此功能只能用於以 :data:`O_DIRECT` 旗標開啟的檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1586
msgid "Use uncached buffered IO."
msgstr "使用無快取的緩衝 IO。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1595
msgid ""
"Write data atomically. Requires alignment to the device's atomic write unit."
msgstr "以原子方式寫入資料。需要對齊裝置的原子寫入單位。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1604
msgid ""
"Return the name of the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the "
"master pseudo-terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The "
"file descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"回傳從屬偽終端裝置的名稱，該裝置與檔案描述器 *fd* 所指的主偽終端裝置相關聯。"
"失敗時不會關閉檔案描述器 *fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1608
msgid ""
"Calls the reentrant C standard library function :c:func:`ptsname_r` if it is "
"available; otherwise, the C standard library function :c:func:`ptsname`, "
"which is not guaranteed to be thread-safe, is called."
msgstr ""
"如果可用，會呼叫可重入的 C 標準函式庫函式 :c:func:`ptsname_r`；否則會呼叫不保"
"證執行緒安全的 C 標準函式庫函式 :c:func:`ptsname`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1619
msgid ""
"Write the bytestring in *str* to file descriptor *fd* at position of "
"*offset*, leaving the file offset unchanged."
msgstr ""
"將 *str* 中的位元組串寫入檔案描述器 *fd* 的 *offset* 位置，並保持檔案偏移量不"
"變。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1622 ../../library/os.rst:1934
msgid "Return the number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "回傳實際寫入的位元組數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1631
msgid ""
"Write the *buffers* contents to file descriptor *fd* at an offset *offset*, "
"leaving the file offset unchanged.  *buffers* must be a sequence "
"of :term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>`. Buffers are processed in "
"array order. Entire contents of the first buffer is written before "
"proceeding to the second, and so on."
msgstr ""
"將 *buffers* 的內容寫入檔案描述器 *fd* 的 *offset* 偏移量處，並保持檔案偏移量"
"不變。*buffers* 必須是\\ :term:`類位元組串物件 <bytes-like object>`\\ 的序"
"列。緩衝區會依陣列順序處理。在處理第二個緩衝區之前，會先寫入第一個緩衝區的全"
"部內容，依此類推。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1640
msgid ":data:`RWF_DSYNC`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_DSYNC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1641
msgid ":data:`RWF_SYNC`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_SYNC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1642
msgid ":data:`RWF_APPEND`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_APPEND`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1644
msgid ":data:`RWF_ATOMIC`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_ATOMIC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1646
msgid "Return the total number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "回傳實際寫入的位元組總數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1651
msgid "Combine the functionality of :func:`os.writev` and :func:`os.pwrite`."
msgstr "結合 :func:`os.writev` 與 :func:`os.pwrite` 的功能。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1662
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_DSYNC` :func:`os.open` flag. "
"This flag effect applies only to the data range written by the system call."
msgstr ""
"提供與 :func:`os.open` 的 :data:`O_DSYNC` 旗標等效、但以每次寫入為單位的功"
"能。此旗標的效果只會套用到該系統呼叫所寫入的資料範圍。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1672
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_SYNC` :func:`os.open` flag. "
"This flag effect applies only to the data range written by the system call."
msgstr ""
"提供與 :func:`os.open` 的 :data:`O_SYNC` 旗標等效、但以每次寫入為單位的功能。"
"此旗標的效果只會套用到該系統呼叫所寫入的資料範圍。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1682
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_APPEND` :func:`os.open` flag. "
"This flag is meaningful only for :func:`os.pwritev`, and its effect applies "
"only to the data range written by the system call. The *offset* argument "
"does not affect the write operation; the data is always appended to the end "
"of the file. However, if the *offset* argument is ``-1``, the current file "
"*offset* is updated."
msgstr ""
"提供與 :func:`os.open` 的 :data:`O_APPEND` 旗標等效、但以每次寫入為單位的功"
"能。此旗標只對 :func:`os.pwritev` 有意義，且其效果只會套用到該系統呼叫所寫入"
"的資料範圍。*offset* 引數不會影響寫入操作；資料一律會附加到檔案結尾。然而，如"
"果 *offset* 引數為 ``-1``，則會更新目前的檔案 *offset*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1696
msgid "Read at most *n* bytes from file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "從檔案描述器 *fd* 讀取最多 *n* 個位元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1703
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To read a \"file "
"object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or by :func:`popen` "
"or :func:`fdopen`, or :data:`sys.stdin`, use its :meth:`~io.TextIOBase.read` "
"or :meth:`~io.IOBase.readline` methods."
msgstr ""
"此函式用於低階 I/O，且必須套用在由 :func:`os.open` 或 :func:`pipe` 回傳的檔案"
"描述器上。若要讀取由內建函式 :func:`open`、:func:`popen` 或 :func:`fdopen` 回"
"傳的「檔案物件」，或是 :data:`sys.stdin`，請使用"
"其 :meth:`~io.TextIOBase.read` 或 :meth:`~io.IOBase.readline` 方法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1717
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* into a mutable :ref:`buffer object "
"<bufferobjects>` *buffer*."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *fd* 讀取資料到可變的\\ :ref:`緩衝區物件 <bufferobjects>` "
"*buffer* 中。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1720
msgid ""
"The *buffer* should be mutable and :term:`bytes-like <bytes-like object>`. "
"On success, returns the number of bytes read. Less bytes may be read than "
"the size of the buffer. The underlying system call will be retried when "
"interrupted by a signal, unless the signal handler raises an exception. "
"Other errors will not be retried and an error will be raised."
msgstr ""
"*buffer* 應該是可變的且為\\ :term:`類位元組串 <bytes-like object>`。成功時回"
"傳讀取的位元組數。讀取到的位元組可能少於緩衝區的大小。底層的系統呼叫被訊號中"
"斷時會重試，除非訊號處理程式引發了例外。其他錯誤則不會重試，而是直接引發錯"
"誤。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1726
msgid ""
"Returns 0 if *fd* is at end of file or if the provided *buffer* has length 0 "
"(which can be used to check for errors without reading data). Never returns "
"negative."
msgstr ""
"如果 *fd* 已到達檔案結尾，或提供的 *buffer* 長度為 0（可用來在不讀取資料的情"
"況下檢查錯誤），則回傳 0。永遠不會回傳負數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1732
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`os.pipe`.  To read a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open`, "
"or :data:`sys.stdin`, use its member functions, for "
"example :meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.readinto`, :meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.read`, "
"or :meth:`io.TextIOBase.read`"
msgstr ""
"此函式用於低階 I/O，且必須套用在由 :func:`os.open` 或 :func:`os.pipe` 回傳的"
"檔案描述器上。若要讀取由內建函式 :func:`open` 回傳的「檔案物件」"
"或 :data:`sys.stdin`，請使用其成員函式，例"
"如 :meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.readinto`、:meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.read` "
"或 :meth:`io.TextIOBase.read`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1745
msgid ""
"Copy *count* bytes from file descriptor *in_fd* to file descriptor *out_fd* "
"starting at *offset*. Return the number of bytes sent. When EOF is reached "
"return ``0``."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *in_fd* 的 *offset* 處開始，複製 *count* 個位元組到檔案描述器 "
"*out_fd*。回傳已傳送的位元組數。當到達 EOF 時回傳 ``0``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1749
msgid ""
"The first function notation is supported by all platforms that "
"define :func:`sendfile`."
msgstr "所有定義了 :func:`sendfile` 的平台都支援第一種函式寫法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1752
msgid ""
"On Linux, if *offset* is given as ``None``, the bytes are read from the "
"current position of *in_fd* and the position of *in_fd* is updated."
msgstr ""
"在 Linux 上，如果 *offset* 為 ``None``，則會從 *in_fd* 的目前位置讀取位元組，"
"並更新 *in_fd* 的位置。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1755
msgid ""
"The second case may be used on macOS and FreeBSD where *headers* and "
"*trailers* are arbitrary sequences of buffers that are written before and "
"after the data from *in_fd* is written. It returns the same as the first "
"case."
msgstr ""
"第二種情況可以在 macOS 和 FreeBSD 上使用，其中 *headers* 和 *trailers* 是任意"
"的緩衝區序列，會分別在寫入來自 *in_fd* 的資料之前與之後寫入。它的回傳值與第一"
"種情況相同。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1759
msgid ""
"On macOS and FreeBSD, a value of ``0`` for *count* specifies to send until "
"the end of *in_fd* is reached."
msgstr ""
"在 macOS 和 FreeBSD 上，*count* 的值為 ``0`` 時，表示持續傳送直到到達 "
"*in_fd* 的結尾。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1762
msgid ""
"All platforms support sockets as *out_fd* file descriptor, and some "
"platforms allow other types (e.g. regular file, pipe) as well."
msgstr ""
"所有平台都支援以 socket 作為 *out_fd* 檔案描述器，有些平台也允許其他類型（例"
"如一般檔案、管道）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1765
msgid ""
"Cross-platform applications should not use *headers*, *trailers* and *flags* "
"arguments."
msgstr "跨平台應用程式不應使用 *headers*、*trailers* 和 *flags* 引數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1772
msgid ""
"For a higher-level wrapper of :func:`sendfile`, "
"see :meth:`socket.socket.sendfile`."
msgstr ""
"關於 :func:`sendfile` 更高階的包裝函式，請參"
"閱 :meth:`socket.socket.sendfile`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1777
msgid "Parameters *out* and *in* was renamed to *out_fd* and *in_fd*."
msgstr "參數 *out* 和 *in* 已被重新命名為 *out_fd* 和 *in_fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1785
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`sendfile` function, if the implementation supports "
"them."
msgstr "如果實作有支援，這些是 :func:`sendfile` 函式的參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1794
msgid ""
"Parameter to the :func:`sendfile` function, if the implementation supports "
"it. The data won't be cached in the virtual memory and will be freed "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""
"如果實作有支援，這是 :func:`sendfile` 函式的參數。資料不會被快取在虛擬記憶體"
"中，並會在之後被釋放。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1804
msgid ""
"Set the blocking mode of the specified file descriptor. Set "
"the :data:`O_NONBLOCK` flag if blocking is ``False``, clear the flag "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"設定指定檔案描述器的阻塞模式。如果 blocking 為 ``False`` 則設"
"定 :data:`O_NONBLOCK` 旗標，否則清除該旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1807
msgid "See also :func:`get_blocking` and :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."
msgstr "另請參閱 :func:`get_blocking` 與 :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1824
msgid ""
"Transfer *count* bytes from file descriptor *src*, starting from offset "
"*offset_src*, to file descriptor *dst*, starting from offset *offset_dst*."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *src* 的偏移量 *offset_src* 開始，傳輸 *count* 個位元組到檔案描"
"述器 *dst* 的偏移量 *offset_dst* 處。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1827
msgid ""
"The splicing behaviour can be modified by specifying a *flags* value. Any of "
"the following variables may used, combined using bitwise OR (the ``|`` "
"operator):"
msgstr ""
"可以透過指定 *flags* 值來修改 splice 的行為。可以使用下列任何變數，並以位元 "
"OR（``|`` 運算子）組合："

#: ../../library/os.rst:1831
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_MOVE` is specified, the kernel is asked to move pages "
"instead of copying, but pages may still be copied if the kernel cannot move "
"the pages from the pipe."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 :const:`SPLICE_F_MOVE`，會要求核心移動分頁而不是複製，但如果核心無"
"法從管道中移動分頁，分頁仍可能會被複製。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1835
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_NONBLOCK` is specified, the kernel is asked to not block "
"on I/O. This makes the splice pipe operations nonblocking, but splice may "
"nevertheless block because the spliced file descriptors may block."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 :const:`SPLICE_F_NONBLOCK`，會要求核心不要在 I/O 上阻塞。這會讓 "
"splice 的管道操作成為非阻塞的，但由於被 splice 的檔案描述器可能會阻塞，"
"splice 仍有可能阻塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1840
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_MORE` is specified, it hints to the kernel that more "
"data will be coming in a subsequent splice."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 :const:`SPLICE_F_MORE`，會提示核心在後續的 splice 中將有更多資料傳"
"入。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1843
msgid ""
"At least one of the file descriptors must refer to a pipe. If *offset_src* "
"is ``None``, then *src* is read from the current position; respectively for "
"*offset_dst*. The offset associated to the file descriptor that refers to a "
"pipe must be ``None``. The files pointed to by *src* and *dst* must reside "
"in the same filesystem, otherwise an :exc:`OSError` is raised "
"with :attr:`~OSError.errno` set to :const:`errno.EXDEV`."
msgstr ""
"至少要有一個檔案描述器指向管道。如果 *offset_src* 為 ``None``，則會從目前位置"
"讀取 *src*；*offset_dst* 亦同，此時會從目前位置寫入 *dst*。與指向管道之檔案描"
"述器關聯的偏移量必須是 ``None``。*src* 和 *dst* 所指向的檔案必須位於同一個檔"
"案系統，否則會引發 :exc:`OSError`，且其 :attr:`~OSError.errno` 會被設"
"為 :const:`errno.EXDEV`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1850
msgid ""
"This copy is done without the additional cost of transferring data from the "
"kernel to user space and then back into the kernel. Additionally, some "
"filesystems could implement extra optimizations. The copy is done as if both "
"files are opened as binary."
msgstr ""
"此複製操作不會產生將資料從核心傳輸到使用者空間、再送回核心的額外成本。此外，"
"有些檔案系統可以實作額外的最佳化。複製時會如同兩個檔案皆以二進位模式開啟。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1855
msgid ""
"Upon successful completion, returns the number of bytes spliced to or from "
"the pipe. A return value of 0 means end of input. If *src* refers to a pipe, "
"then this means that there was no data to transfer, and it would not make "
"sense to block because there are no writers connected to the write end of "
"the pipe."
msgstr ""
"成功完成時，回傳 splice 進出管道的位元組數。回傳值為 0 表示輸入結束。如果 "
"*src* 指向管道，這表示沒有資料可傳輸，而且由於沒有寫入者連接到管道的寫入端，"
"阻塞也沒有意義。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1861
msgid "The :manpage:`splice(2)` man page."
msgstr ":manpage:`splice(2)` 使用手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1876
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* into a number of mutable :term:`bytes-like "
"objects <bytes-like object>` *buffers*. Transfer data into each buffer until "
"it is full and then move on to the next buffer in the sequence to hold the "
"rest of the data."
msgstr ""
"從檔案描述器 *fd* 讀取資料到多個可變的\\ :term:`類位元組串物件 <bytes-like "
"object>` *buffers* 中。資料會被傳入每個緩衝區直到填滿，再移到序列中的下一個緩"
"衝區來存放其餘資料。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1894
msgid ""
"Return the process group associated with the terminal given by *fd* (an open "
"file descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open`)."
msgstr ""
"回傳與 *fd*\\ （由 :func:`os.open` 回傳的已開啟檔案描述器）所指定之終端機關聯"
"的行程群組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1902
msgid ""
"Set the process group associated with the terminal given by *fd* (an open "
"file descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open`) to *pg*."
msgstr ""
"將與 *fd*\\ （由 :func:`os.open` 回傳的已開啟檔案描述器）所指定之終端機關聯的"
"行程群組設定為 *pg*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1910
msgid ""
"Return a string which specifies the terminal device associated with file "
"descriptor *fd*.  If *fd* is not associated with a terminal device, an "
"exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個字串，指定與檔案描述器 *fd* 關聯的終端機裝置。如果 *fd* 沒有與終端機"
"裝置關聯，則會引發例外。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1919
msgid ""
"Unlock the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the master pseudo-"
"terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The file "
"descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"解鎖從屬偽終端裝置，該裝置與檔案描述器 *fd* 所指的主偽終端裝置相關聯。失敗時"
"不會關閉檔案描述器 *fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1923
msgid "Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`unlockpt`."
msgstr "呼叫 C 標準函式庫函式 :c:func:`unlockpt`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1932
msgid "Write the bytestring in *str* to file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "將 *str* 中的位元組串寫入檔案描述器 *fd*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1938
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To write a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or "
"by :func:`popen` or :func:`fdopen`, or :data:`sys.stdout` "
"or :data:`sys.stderr`, use its :meth:`~io.TextIOBase.write` method."
msgstr ""
"此函式用於低階 I/O，且必須套用在由 :func:`os.open` 或 :func:`pipe` 回傳的檔案"
"描述器上。若要寫入由內建函式 :func:`open`、:func:`popen` 或 :func:`fdopen` 回"
"傳的「檔案物件」，或是 :data:`sys.stdout` 或 :data:`sys.stderr`，請使用"
"其 :meth:`~io.TextIOBase.write` 方法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1952
msgid ""
"Write the contents of *buffers* to file descriptor *fd*. *buffers* must be a "
"sequence of :term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>`. Buffers are "
"processed in array order. Entire contents of the first buffer is written "
"before proceeding to the second, and so on."
msgstr ""
"將 *buffers* 的內容寫入檔案描述器 *fd*。*buffers* 必須是\\ :term:`類位元組串"
"物件 <bytes-like object>`\\ 的序列。緩衝區會依陣列順序處理。在處理第二個緩衝"
"區之前，會先寫入第一個緩衝區的全部內容，依此類推。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1957
msgid "Returns the total number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "回傳實際寫入的位元組總數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1970
msgid "Querying the size of a terminal"
msgstr "查詢終端機的大小"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1976
msgid ""
"Return the size of the terminal window as ``(columns, lines)``, tuple of "
"type :class:`terminal_size`."
msgstr ""
"以 :class:`terminal_size` 型別的元組 ``(columns, lines)`` 回傳終端機視窗的大"
"小。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1979
msgid ""
"The optional argument ``fd`` (default ``STDOUT_FILENO``, or standard output) "
"specifies which file descriptor should be queried."
msgstr ""
"可選引數 ``fd``\\ （預設為 ``STDOUT_FILENO``，即標準輸出）指定要查詢哪個檔案"
"描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1982
msgid ""
"If the file descriptor is not connected to a terminal, an :exc:`OSError` is "
"raised."
msgstr "如果檔案描述器沒有連接到終端機，則會引發 :exc:`OSError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1985
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.get_terminal_size` is the high-level function which should "
"normally be used, ``os.get_terminal_size`` is the low-level implementation."
msgstr ""
":func:`shutil.get_terminal_size` 是一般應使用的高階函式，"
"``os.get_terminal_size`` 則是其低階實作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1993
msgid ""
"A subclass of tuple, holding ``(columns, lines)`` of the terminal window "
"size."
msgstr "元組的子類別，存放終端機視窗大小的 ``(columns, lines)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1997
msgid "Width of the terminal window in characters."
msgstr "終端機視窗的寬度（以字元為單位）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2001
msgid "Height of the terminal window in characters."
msgstr "終端機視窗的高度（以字元為單位）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2007
msgid "Inheritance of File Descriptors"
msgstr "檔案描述器的繼承"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2011
msgid ""
"A file descriptor has an \"inheritable\" flag which indicates if the file "
"descriptor can be inherited by child processes.  Since Python 3.4, file "
"descriptors created by Python are non-inheritable by default."
msgstr ""
"檔案描述器具有一個「可繼承」旗標，表示該檔案描述器是否可以被子行程繼承。自 "
"Python 3.4 起，由 Python 建立的檔案描述器預設為不可繼承。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2015
msgid ""
"On UNIX, non-inheritable file descriptors are closed in child processes at "
"the execution of a new program, other file descriptors are inherited. Note "
"that non-inheritable file descriptors are still *inherited* by child "
"processes on :func:`os.fork`."
msgstr ""
"在 UNIX 上，不可繼承的檔案描述器會在子行程執行新程式時被關閉，其他檔案描述器"
"則會被繼承。請注意，在 :func:`os.fork` 時，不可繼承的檔案描述器仍然會被子行程"
"\\ *繼承*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2019
msgid ""
"On Windows, non-inheritable handles and file descriptors are closed in child "
"processes, except for standard streams (file descriptors 0, 1 and 2: stdin, "
"stdout and stderr), which are always inherited.  Using :func:`spawn\\* "
"<spawnl>` functions, all inheritable handles and all inheritable file "
"descriptors are inherited. Using the :mod:`subprocess` module, all file "
"descriptors except standard streams are closed, and inheritable handles are "
"only inherited if the *close_fds* parameter is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，不可繼承的控制代碼 (handle) 與檔案描述器會在子行程中被關閉，但"
"標準串流（檔案描述器 0、1 和 2：stdin、stdout 和 stderr）除外，它們總是會被繼"
"承。使用 :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式時，所有可繼承的控制代碼和所有可繼承的"
"檔案描述器都會被繼承。使用 :mod:`subprocess` 模組時，除了標準串流以外的所有檔"
"案描述器都會被關閉，而且只有在 *close_fds* 參數為 ``False`` 時，可繼承的控制"
"代碼才會被繼承。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2027
msgid "On WebAssembly platforms, the file descriptor cannot be modified."
msgstr "在 WebAssembly 平台上，無法修改檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2031
msgid ""
"Get the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified file descriptor (a boolean)."
msgstr "取得指定檔案描述器的「可繼承」旗標（一個布林值）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2035
msgid "Set the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified file descriptor."
msgstr "設定指定檔案描述器的「可繼承」旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2039
msgid "Get the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified handle (a boolean)."
msgstr "取得指定控制代碼的「可繼承」旗標（一個布林值）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2045
msgid "Set the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified handle."
msgstr "設定指定控制代碼的「可繼承」旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2053
msgid "Files and Directories"
msgstr "檔案和目錄"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2055
msgid ""
"On some Unix platforms, many of these functions support one or more of these "
"features:"
msgstr "在某些 Unix 平台上，這些函式中有許多支援下列一項或多項功能："

#: ../../library/os.rst:2060
msgid ""
"**specifying a file descriptor:** Normally the *path* argument provided to "
"functions in the :mod:`!os` module must be a string specifying a file path.  "
"However, some functions now alternatively accept an open file descriptor for "
"their *path* argument. The function will then operate on the file referred "
"to by the descriptor. For POSIX systems, Python will call the variant of the "
"function prefixed with ``f`` (e.g. call ``fchdir`` instead of ``chdir``)."
msgstr ""
"**指定檔案描述器：**\\ 通常提供給 :mod:`!os` 模組中函式的 *path* 引數必須是指"
"定檔案路徑的字串。不過，有些函式現在也接受以已開啟的檔案描述器作為 *path* 引"
"數。此時函式會對該描述器所指的檔案進行操作。在 POSIX 系統上，Python 會呼叫該"
"函式加上 ``f`` 前綴的變體（例如呼叫 ``fchdir`` 而非 ``chdir``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2068
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *path* can be specified as a file descriptor "
"for a particular function on your platform using :data:`os.supports_fd`. If "
"this functionality is unavailable, using it will raise "
"a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"你可以使用 :data:`os.supports_fd` 檢查在你的平台上，特定函式的 *path* 是否可"
"以指定為檔案描述器。如果此功能無法使用，使用它會引"
"發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2073
msgid ""
"If the function also supports *dir_fd* or *follow_symlinks* arguments, it's "
"an error to specify one of those when supplying *path* as a file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"如果函式也支援 *dir_fd* 或 *follow_symlinks* 引數，那麼在以檔案描述器提供 "
"*path* 時，指定其中任何一個都是錯誤的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2078
msgid ""
"**paths relative to directory descriptors:** If *dir_fd* is not ``None``, it "
"should be a file descriptor referring to a directory, and the path to "
"operate on should be relative; path will then be relative to that "
"directory.  If the path is absolute, *dir_fd* is ignored.  For POSIX "
"systems, Python will call the variant of the function with an ``at`` suffix "
"and possibly prefixed with ``f`` (e.g. call ``faccessat`` instead of "
"``access``)."
msgstr ""
"**相對於目錄描述器的路徑：**\\ 如果 *dir_fd* 不是 ``None``，它應該是指向某個"
"目錄的檔案描述器，且要操作的路徑應為相對路徑；路徑將會相對於該目錄。如果路徑"
"是絕對路徑，則會忽略 *dir_fd*。在 POSIX 系統上，Python 會呼叫該函式加上 "
"``at`` 後綴、並可能加上 ``f`` 前綴的變體（例如呼叫 ``faccessat`` 而非 "
"``access``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2085
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *dir_fd* is supported for a particular function "
"on your platform using :data:`os.supports_dir_fd`.  If it's unavailable, "
"using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"你可以使用 :data:`os.supports_dir_fd` 檢查在你的平台上，特定函式是否支援 "
"*dir_fd*。如果無法使用，使用它會引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2091
msgid ""
"**not following symlinks:** If *follow_symlinks* is ``False``, and the last "
"element of the path to operate on is a symbolic link, the function will "
"operate on the symbolic link itself rather than the file pointed to by the "
"link.  For POSIX systems, Python will call the ``l...`` variant of the "
"function."
msgstr ""
"**不跟隨符號連結：**\\ 如果 *follow_symlinks* 為 ``False``，且要操作之路徑的"
"最後一個元素是符號連結，則函式會對符號連結本身進行操作，而不是對該連結所指向"
"的檔案。在 POSIX 系統上，Python 會呼叫該函式的 ``l...`` 變體。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2097
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *follow_symlinks* is supported for a particular "
"function on your platform using :data:`os.supports_follow_symlinks`. If it's "
"unavailable, using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"你可以使用 :data:`os.supports_follow_symlinks` 檢查在你的平台上，特定函式是否"
"支援 *follow_symlinks*。如果無法使用，使用它會引"
"發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2105
msgid ""
"Use the real uid/gid to test for access to *path*.  Note that most "
"operations will use the effective uid/gid, therefore this routine can be "
"used in a suid/sgid environment to test if the invoking user has the "
"specified access to *path*.  *mode* should be :const:`F_OK` to test the "
"existence of *path*, or it can be the inclusive OR of one or more "
"of :const:`R_OK`, :const:`W_OK`, and :const:`X_OK` to test permissions.  "
"Return :const:`True` if access is allowed, :const:`False` if not. See the "
"Unix man page :manpage:`access(2)` for more information."
msgstr ""
"使用真實 uid/gid 測試對 *path* 的存取權限。請注意，大多數操作會使用有效 uid/"
"gid，因此此常式可以在 suid/sgid 環境中用來測試呼叫的使用者是否擁有對 *path* "
"的指定存取權限。*mode* 應為 :const:`F_OK` 以測試 *path* 是否存在，或者可以"
"是 :const:`R_OK`、:const:`W_OK` 和 :const:`X_OK` 其中一個或多個的位元 OR 組"
"合，以測試權限。如果允許存取則回傳 :const:`True`，否則回傳 :const:`False`。更"
"多資訊請參閱 Unix 使用手冊 :manpage:`access(2)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2114
msgid ""
"This function can support specifying :ref:`paths relative to directory "
"descriptors <dir_fd>` and :ref:`not following symlinks <follow_symlinks>`."
msgstr ""
"此函式可以支援指定\\ :ref:`相對於目錄描述器的路徑 <dir_fd>`\\ 和\\ :ref:`不跟"
"隨符號連結 <follow_symlinks>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2117
msgid ""
"If *effective_ids* is ``True``, :func:`access` will perform its access "
"checks using the effective uid/gid instead of the real uid/gid. "
"*effective_ids* may not be supported on your platform; you can check whether "
"or not it is available using :data:`os.supports_effective_ids`.  If it is "
"unavailable, using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"如果 *effective_ids* 為 ``True``，:func:`access` 會使用有效 uid/gid 而非真實 "
"uid/gid 來進行存取檢查。你的平台可能不支援 *effective_ids*；你可以使"
"用 :data:`os.supports_effective_ids` 檢查它是否可用。如果無法使用，使用它會引"
"發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2125
msgid ""
"Using :func:`access` to check if a user is authorized to e.g. open a file "
"before actually doing so using :func:`open` creates a security hole, because "
"the user might exploit the short time interval between checking and opening "
"the file to manipulate it. It's preferable to use :term:`EAFP` techniques. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"在實際使用 :func:`open` 開啟檔案之前，先用 :func:`access` 檢查使用者是否有權"
"限進行開啟檔案等操作，會造成安全漏洞，因為使用者可能會利用檢查與開啟檔案之間"
"的短暫時間間隔來操弄該檔案。最好使用 :term:`EAFP` 技巧。例如： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2131
msgid ""
"if os.access(\"myfile\", os.R_OK):\n"
"    with open(\"myfile\") as fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()\n"
"return \"some default data\""
msgstr ""
"if os.access(\"myfile\", os.R_OK):\n"
"    with open(\"myfile\") as fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()\n"
"return \"some default data\""

#: ../../library/os.rst:2136
msgid "is better written as::"
msgstr "最好寫成： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2138
msgid ""
"try:\n"
"    fp = open(\"myfile\")\n"
"except PermissionError:\n"
"    return \"some default data\"\n"
"else:\n"
"    with fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()"
msgstr ""
"try:\n"
"    fp = open(\"myfile\")\n"
"except PermissionError:\n"
"    return \"some default data\"\n"
"else:\n"
"    with fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2148
msgid ""
"I/O operations may fail even when :func:`access` indicates that they would "
"succeed, particularly for operations on network filesystems which may have "
"permissions semantics beyond the usual POSIX permission-bit model."
msgstr ""
"即使 :func:`access` 表示 I/O 操作會成功，這些操作仍可能失敗，特別是對於網路檔"
"案系統上的操作，其權限語意可能超出一般 POSIX 權限位元模型的範圍。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2152
msgid "Added the *dir_fd*, *effective_ids*, and *follow_symlinks* parameters."
msgstr "新增 *dir_fd*、*effective_ids* 與 *follow_symlinks* 參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2164
msgid ""
"Values to pass as the *mode* parameter of :func:`access` to test the "
"existence, readability, writability and executability of *path*, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"作為 :func:`access` 之 *mode* 參數傳入的值，分別用來測試 *path* 是否存在、可"
"讀、可寫與可執行。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2173
