#: ../../library/os.rst:3767
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`os.statx` function.  Requests that the kernel return "
"up-to-date information even when doing so is expensive (for example, "
"requiring a round trip to the server for a file on a network filesystem)."
msgstr ""
":func:`os.statx` 函式的旗標。要求核心回傳最新的資訊，即使這麼做的成本很高（例"
"如對於網路檔案系統上的檔案，需要與伺服器進行一次往返）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3777
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`os.statx` function.  Requests that the kernel return "
"cached information if possible."
msgstr ":func:`os.statx` 函式的旗標。要求核心盡可能回傳快取的資訊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3786
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`os.statx` function.  This flag is defined as ``0``, so "
"it has no effect, but it can be used to explicitly indicate "
"neither :data:`AT_STATX_FORCE_SYNC` nor :data:`AT_STATX_DONT_SYNC` is being "
"passed. In the absence of the other two flags, the kernel will generally "
"return information as fresh as :func:`os.stat` would return."
msgstr ""
":func:`os.statx` 函式的旗標。此旗標定義為 ``0``，因此沒有效果，但可以用來明確"
"表示既未傳入 :data:`AT_STATX_FORCE_SYNC` 也未傳"
"入 :data:`AT_STATX_DONT_SYNC`。在沒有另外兩個旗標的情況下，核心通常會回傳"
"與 :func:`os.stat` 一樣新的資訊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3799
msgid ""
"If the final component of a path is an automount point, operate on the "
"automount point instead of performing the automount.  On "
"Linux, :func:`os.stat`, :func:`os.fstat` and :func:`os.lstat` always behave "
"this way."
msgstr ""
"如果路徑的最後一個組成部分是自動掛載點 (automount point)，則對該自動掛載點本"
"身進行操作，而不執行自動掛載。在 Linux 上，:func:`os.stat`、:func:`os.fstat` "
"和 :func:`os.lstat` 一律以這種方式運作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3811
msgid ""
"Perform a :manpage:`statvfs(3)` system call on the given path.  The return "
"value is a :class:`statvfs_result` whose attributes describe the filesystem "
"on the given path and correspond to the members of the :c:struct:`statvfs` "
"structure."
msgstr ""
"對給定的路徑執行 :manpage:`statvfs(3)` 系統呼叫。回傳值是一"
"個 :class:`statvfs_result`，其屬性描述了給定路徑上的檔案系統，並對應"
"於 :c:struct:`statvfs` 結構的成員。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3829
msgid ""
"Filesystem statistics returned by :func:`os.statvfs` "
"and :func:`os.fstatvfs`. See :manpage:`statvfs(3)` for more details."
msgstr ""
"由 :func:`os.statvfs` 與 :func:`os.fstatvfs` 回傳的檔案系統統計資訊。詳情請參"
"閱 :manpage:`statvfs(3)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3834
msgid "Block size."
msgstr "區塊大小。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3838
msgid "Fragment size."
msgstr "片段大小。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3842
msgid ""
"Number of :attr:`~statvfs_result.f_frsize` sized blocks the filesystem can "
"contain."
msgstr "檔案系統可容納、大小為 :attr:`~statvfs_result.f_frsize` 的區塊數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3847
msgid "Number of free blocks."
msgstr "可用區塊的數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3851
msgid "Number of free blocks for unprivileged users."
msgstr "非特權使用者可用的區塊數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3855
msgid "Number of file entries, inodes, the filesystem can contain."
msgstr "檔案系統可容納的檔案條目 (inode) 數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3859
msgid "Number of free files entries."
msgstr "可用的檔案條目數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3863
msgid "Number of free file entries for unprivileged users."
msgstr "非特權使用者可用的檔案條目數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3867
msgid ""
"Bit-mask of mount flags.  The following flags are "
"defined: :data:`ST_RDONLY`, :data:`ST_NOSUID`, :data:`ST_NODEV`, :data:`ST_NOEXEC`, :data:`ST_SYNCHRONOUS`, :data:`ST_MANDLOCK`, :data:`ST_WRITE`, :data:`ST_APPEND`, :data:`ST_IMMUTABLE`, :data:`ST_NOATIME`, :data:`ST_NODIRATIME`, "
"and :data:`ST_RELATIME`."
msgstr ""
"掛載旗標的位元遮罩。已定義以下旗"
"標：:data:`ST_RDONLY`、:data:`ST_NOSUID`、:data:`ST_NODEV`、:data:`ST_NOEXEC`、:data:`ST_SYNCHRONOUS`、:data:`ST_MANDLOCK`、:data:`ST_WRITE`、:data:`ST_APPEND`、:data:`ST_IMMUTABLE`、:data:`ST_NOATIME`、:data:`ST_NODIRATIME` "
"與 :data:`ST_RELATIME`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3875
msgid ""
"Filesystem max filename length. OS specific limitations such "
"as :ref:`Windows MAX_PATH <max-path>` and those described in "
"Linux :manpage:`pathname(7)` may exist."
msgstr ""
"檔案系統的最大檔案名稱長度。可能存在作業系統特定的限制，例如 :ref:`Windows "
"MAX_PATH <max-path>` 以及 Linux :manpage:`pathname(7)` 中所描述的限制。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3881
msgid "Filesystem ID."
msgstr "檔案系統 ID。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3886
msgid "The following flags are used in :attr:`statvfs_result.f_flag`."
msgstr "以下旗標用於 :attr:`statvfs_result.f_flag`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3890
msgid "Read-only filesystem."
msgstr "唯讀檔案系統。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3896
msgid "Setuid/setgid bits are disabled or not supported."
msgstr "Setuid/setgid 位元已停用或不受支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3902
msgid "Disallow access to device special files."
msgstr "不允許存取裝置特殊檔案。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3910
msgid "Disallow program execution."
msgstr "不允許執行程式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3918
msgid "Writes are synced at once."
msgstr "寫入會立即同步。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3926
msgid "Allow mandatory locks on an FS."
msgstr "允許在檔案系統上使用強制鎖 (mandatory lock)。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3934
msgid "Write on file/directory/symlink."
msgstr "在檔案/目錄/符號連結上寫入。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3942
msgid "Append-only file."
msgstr "僅能附加的檔案。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3950
msgid "Immutable file."
msgstr "不可變的檔案。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3958
msgid "Do not update access times."
msgstr "不更新存取時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3966
msgid "Do not update directory access times."
msgstr "不更新目錄存取時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3974
msgid "Update atime relative to mtime/ctime."
msgstr "相對於 mtime/ctime 更新 atime。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3983
msgid ""
"A :class:`set` object indicating which functions in the :mod:`!os` module "
"accept an open file descriptor for their *dir_fd* parameter. Different "
"platforms provide different features, and the underlying functionality "
"Python uses to implement the *dir_fd* parameter is not available on all "
"platforms Python supports.  For consistency's sake, functions that may "
"support *dir_fd* always allow specifying the parameter, but will throw an "
"exception if the functionality is used when it's not locally available. "
"(Specifying ``None`` for *dir_fd* is always supported on all platforms.)"
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`set` 物件，指出 :mod:`!os` 模組中有哪些函式的 *dir_fd* 參數接受"
"已開啟的檔案描述器。不同平台提供不同的功能，而 Python 用來實作 *dir_fd* 參數"
"的底層功能並非在 Python 支援的所有平台上都可用。為了一致性，可能支援 "
"*dir_fd* 的函式一律允許指定該參數，但若在本地不支援的情況下使用該功能，則會引"
"發例外。（在所有平台上，一律支援為 *dir_fd* 指定 ``None``。）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3993
msgid ""
"To check whether a particular function accepts an open file descriptor for "
"its *dir_fd* parameter, use the ``in`` operator on ``supports_dir_fd``. As "
"an example, this expression evaluates to ``True`` if :func:`os.stat` accepts "
"open file descriptors for *dir_fd* on the local platform::"
msgstr ""
"若要檢查特定函式的 *dir_fd* 參數是否接受已開啟的檔案描述器，請對 "
"``supports_dir_fd`` 使用 ``in`` 運算子。例如，如果 :func:`os.stat` 在本地平台"
"上的 *dir_fd* 接受已開啟的檔案描述器，則此運算式會求值為 ``True``： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:3998
msgid "os.stat in os.supports_dir_fd"
msgstr "os.stat in os.supports_dir_fd"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4000
msgid ""
"Currently *dir_fd* parameters only work on Unix platforms; none of them work "
"on Windows."
msgstr "目前 *dir_fd* 參數只能在 Unix 平台上運作；在 Windows 上都無法運作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4008
msgid ""
"A :class:`set` object indicating whether :func:`os.access` permits "
"specifying ``True`` for its *effective_ids* parameter on the local platform. "
"(Specifying ``False`` for *effective_ids* is always supported on all "
"platforms.)  If the local platform supports it, the collection will "
"contain :func:`os.access`; otherwise it will be empty."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`set` 物件，指出 :func:`os.access` 在本地平台上是否允許將其 "
"*effective_ids* 參數指定為 ``True``。（在所有平台上，一律支援將 "
"*effective_ids* 指定為 ``False``。）如果本地平台支援，此集合會包"
"含 :func:`os.access`；否則會是空的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4014
msgid ""
"This expression evaluates to ``True`` if :func:`os.access` supports "
"``effective_ids=True`` on the local platform::"
msgstr ""
"如果 :func:`os.access` 在本地平台上支援 ``effective_ids=True``，則此運算式會"
"求值為 ``True``： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4017
msgid "os.access in os.supports_effective_ids"
msgstr "os.access in os.supports_effective_ids"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4019
msgid ""
"Currently *effective_ids* is only supported on Unix platforms; it does not "
"work on Windows."
msgstr "目前只有 Unix 平台支援 *effective_ids*；它在 Windows 上無法運作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4027
msgid ""
"A :class:`set` object indicating which functions in the :mod:`!os` module "
"permit specifying their *path* parameter as an open file descriptor on the "
"local platform.  Different platforms provide different features, and the "
"underlying functionality Python uses to accept open file descriptors as "
"*path* arguments is not available on all platforms Python supports."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`set` 物件，指出 :mod:`!os` 模組中有哪些函式在本地平台上允許將其 "
"*path* 參數指定為已開啟的檔案描述器。不同平台提供不同的功能，而 Python 用來接"
"受已開啟檔案描述器作為 *path* 引數的底層功能並非在 Python 支援的所有平台上都"
"可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4034
msgid ""
"To determine whether a particular function permits specifying an open file "
"descriptor for its *path* parameter, use the ``in`` operator on "
"``supports_fd``. As an example, this expression evaluates to ``True`` "
"if :func:`os.chdir` accepts open file descriptors for *path* on your local "
"platform::"
msgstr ""
"若要判斷特定函式是否允許將其 *path* 參數指定為已開啟的檔案描述器，請對 "
"``supports_fd`` 使用 ``in`` 運算子。例如，如果 :func:`os.chdir` 在你的本地平"
"台上接受已開啟的檔案描述器作為 *path*，則此運算式會求值為 ``True``： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4040
msgid "os.chdir in os.supports_fd"
msgstr "os.chdir in os.supports_fd"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4047
msgid ""
"A :class:`set` object indicating which functions in the :mod:`!os` module "
"accept ``False`` for their *follow_symlinks* parameter on the local "
"platform. Different platforms provide different features, and the underlying "
"functionality Python uses to implement *follow_symlinks* is not available on "
"all platforms Python supports.  For consistency's sake, functions that may "
"support *follow_symlinks* always allow specifying the parameter, but will "
"throw an exception if the functionality is used when it's not locally "
"available.  (Specifying ``True`` for *follow_symlinks* is always supported "
"on all platforms.)"
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`set` 物件，指出 :mod:`!os` 模組中有哪些函式在本地平台上的 "
"*follow_symlinks* 參數接受 ``False``。不同平台提供不同的功能，而 Python 用來"
"實作 *follow_symlinks* 的底層功能並非在 Python 支援的所有平台上都可用。為了一"
"致性，可能支援 *follow_symlinks* 的函式一律允許指定該參數，但若在本地不支援的"
"情況下使用該功能，則會引發例外。（在所有平台上，一律支援為 *follow_symlinks* "
"指定 ``True``。）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4057
msgid ""
"To check whether a particular function accepts ``False`` for its "
"*follow_symlinks* parameter, use the ``in`` operator on "
"``supports_follow_symlinks``.  As an example, this expression evaluates to "
"``True`` if you may specify ``follow_symlinks=False`` when "
"calling :func:`os.stat` on the local platform::"
msgstr ""
"若要檢查特定函式的 *follow_symlinks* 參數是否接受 ``False``，請對 "
"``supports_follow_symlinks`` 使用 ``in`` 運算子。例如，如果你在本地平台上呼"
"叫 :func:`os.stat` 時可以指定 ``follow_symlinks=False``，則此運算式會求值為 "
"``True``： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4063
msgid "os.stat in os.supports_follow_symlinks"
msgstr "os.stat in os.supports_follow_symlinks"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4070
msgid "Create a symbolic link pointing to *src* named *dst*."
msgstr "建立一個指向 *src*、名為 *dst* 的符號連結。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4072
msgid ""
"The *src* parameter refers to the target of the link (the file or directory "
"being linked to), and *dst* is the name of the link being created."
msgstr ""
"*src* 參數指的是連結的目標（被連結的檔案或目錄），而 *dst* 是要建立的連結名"
"稱。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4075
msgid ""
"On Windows, a symlink represents either a file or a directory, and does not "
"morph to the target dynamically.  If the target is present, the type of the "
"symlink will be created to match. Otherwise, the symlink will be created as "
"a directory if *target_is_directory* is ``True`` or a file symlink (the "
"default) otherwise.  On non-Windows platforms, *target_is_directory* is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，符號連結代表的是檔案或目錄其中之一，且不會動態地隨目標變化。如"
"果目標存在，會建立與其類型相符的符號連結。否則，如果 *target_is_directory* "
"為 ``True``，會建立目錄符號連結，否則建立檔案符號連結（預設）。在非 Windows "
"平台上，*target_is_directory* 會被忽略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4086
msgid ""
"On newer versions of Windows 10, unprivileged accounts can create symlinks "
"if Developer Mode is enabled. When Developer Mode is not available/enabled, "
"the *SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege* privilege is required, or the process "
"must be run as an administrator."
msgstr ""
"在較新版本的 Windows 10 上，如果啟用了開發人員模式 (Developer Mode)，非特權帳"
"號可以建立符號連結。當開發人員模式不可用或未啟用時，需要 "
"*SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege* 權限，或者必須以系統管理員身分執行該行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4092
msgid ""
":exc:`OSError` is raised when the function is called by an unprivileged user."
msgstr "當非特權使用者呼叫此函式時，會引發 :exc:`OSError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4095
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.symlink`` with arguments "
"``src``, ``dst``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``src``、``dst``、``dir_fd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``os.symlink``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4105
msgid ""
"Added the *dir_fd* parameter, and now allow *target_is_directory* on non-"
"Windows platforms."
msgstr ""
"新增 *dir_fd* 參數，且現在允許在非 Windows 平台上使用 *target_is_directory*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4112
msgid "Added support for unelevated symlinks on Windows with Developer Mode."
msgstr "新增在 Windows 開發人員模式下對未提升權限之符號連結的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4118
msgid "Force write of everything to disk."
msgstr "強制將所有內容寫入磁碟。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4127
msgid ""
"Truncate the file corresponding to *path*, so that it is at most *length* "
"bytes in size."
msgstr "截斷 *path* 所對應的檔案，使其大小最多為 *length* 個位元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4132
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.truncate`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``length``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``length`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.truncate``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4147
msgid ""
"Remove (delete) the file *path*.  This function is semantically identical "
"to :func:`remove`; the ``unlink`` name is its traditional Unix name.  Please "
"see the documentation for :func:`remove` for further information."
msgstr ""
"移除（刪除）檔案 *path*。此函式在語意上與 :func:`remove` 相同；``unlink`` 這"
"個名稱是它在 Unix 中的傳統名稱。更多資訊請參閱 :func:`remove` 的文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4163
msgid "Set the access and modified times of the file specified by *path*."
msgstr "設定 *path* 所指定之檔案的存取時間與修改時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4165
msgid ""
":func:`utime` takes two optional parameters, *times* and *ns*. These specify "
"the times set on *path* and are used as follows:"
msgstr ""
":func:`utime` 接受兩個可選參數 *times* 與 *ns*。它們指定要在 *path* 上設定的"
"時間，用法如下："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4168
msgid ""
"If *ns* is specified, it must be a 2-tuple of the form ``(atime_ns, "
"mtime_ns)`` where each member is an int expressing nanoseconds."
msgstr ""
"如果有指定 *ns*，它必須是 ``(atime_ns, mtime_ns)`` 形式的 2 元組，其中每個成"
"員都是以奈秒表示的 int。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4171
msgid ""
"If *times* is not ``None``, it must be a 2-tuple of the form ``(atime, "
"mtime)`` where each member is a real number expressing seconds, rounded down "
"to nanoseconds."
msgstr ""
"如果 *times* 不是 ``None``，它必須是 ``(atime, mtime)`` 形式的 2 元組，其中每"
"個成員都是以秒表示的實數，並向下捨入至奈秒。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4175
msgid ""
"If *times* is ``None`` and *ns* is unspecified, this is equivalent to "
"specifying ``ns=(atime_ns, mtime_ns)`` where both times are the current time."
msgstr ""
"如果 *times* 為 ``None`` 且未指定 *ns*，這等同於指定 ``ns=(atime_ns, "
"mtime_ns)``，其中兩個時間都是目前時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4179
msgid "It is an error to specify tuples for both *times* and *ns*."
msgstr "同時為 *times* 與 *ns* 指定元組是錯誤的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4181
msgid ""
"Note that the exact times you set here may not be returned by a "
"subsequent :func:`~os.stat` call, depending on the resolution with which "
"your operating system records access and modification times; "
"see :func:`~os.stat`. The best way to preserve exact times is to use the "
"*st_atime_ns* and *st_mtime_ns* fields from the :func:`os.stat` result "
"object with the *ns* parameter to :func:`utime`."
msgstr ""
"請注意，你在此設定的確切時間可能不會由後續的 :func:`~os.stat` 呼叫回傳，這取"
"決於你的作業系統記錄存取與修改時間的解析度；請參閱 :func:`~os.stat`。保留確切"
"時間的最佳方式，是將 :func:`os.stat` 結果物件中的 *st_atime_ns* 與 "
"*st_mtime_ns* 欄位搭配 :func:`utime` 的 *ns* 參數使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4192
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.utime`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``times``, ``ns``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``times``、``ns``、``dir_fd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``os.utime``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4194
msgid ""
"Added support for specifying *path* as an open file descriptor, and the "
"*dir_fd*, *follow_symlinks*, and *ns* parameters."
msgstr ""
"新增將 *path* 指定為已開啟檔案描述器的支援，以及 *dir_fd*、*follow_symlinks* "
"與 *ns* 參數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4201
msgid "Accepts any real numbers as *times*, not only integers or floats."
msgstr "*times* 接受任何實數，而不僅限於整數或浮點數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4211
msgid ""
"Generate the file names in a directory tree by walking the tree either top-"
"down or bottom-up. For each directory in the tree rooted at directory *top* "
"(including *top* itself), it yields a 3-tuple ``(dirpath, dirnames, "
"filenames)``."
msgstr ""
"透過由上而下或由下而上走訪目錄樹，來產生樹中的檔案名稱。對於以目錄 *top* 為根"
"的樹中的每個目錄（包括 *top* 本身），它會產生一個 3 元組 ``(dirpath, "
"dirnames, filenames)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4216
msgid ""
"*dirpath* is a string, the path to the directory.  *dirnames* is a list of "
"the names of the subdirectories in *dirpath* (including symlinks to "
"directories, and excluding ``'.'`` and ``'..'``). *filenames* is a list of "
"the names of the non-directory files in *dirpath*. Note that the names in "
"the lists contain no path components.  To get a full path (which begins with "
"*top*) to a file or directory in *dirpath*, do ``os.path.join(dirpath, "
"name)``.  Whether or not the lists are sorted depends on the file system.  "
"If a file is removed from or added to the *dirpath* directory during "
"generating the lists, whether a name for that file be included is "
"unspecified."
msgstr ""
"*dirpath* 是一個字串，為該目錄的路徑。*dirnames* 是 *dirpath* 中子目錄名稱的"
"串列（包括指向目錄的符號連結，但不包括 ``'.'`` 與 ``'..'``）。*filenames* 是 "
"*dirpath* 中非目錄檔案名稱的串列。請注意，串列中的名稱不包含路徑組成部分。若"
"要取得 *dirpath* 中某個檔案或目錄的完整路徑（以 *top* 開頭），請執行 "
"``os.path.join(dirpath, name)``。串列是否經過排序取決於檔案系統。如果在產生串"
"列的過程中，有檔案從 *dirpath* 目錄中被移除或被新增到其中，則是否會包含該檔案"
"的名稱並未指定。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4227
msgid ""
"If optional argument *topdown* is ``True`` or not specified, the triple for "
"a directory is generated before the triples for any of its subdirectories "
"(directories are generated top-down).  If *topdown* is ``False``, the triple "
"for a directory is generated after the triples for all of its subdirectories "
"(directories are generated bottom-up). No matter the value of *topdown*, the "
"list of subdirectories is retrieved before the tuples for the directory and "
"its subdirectories are generated."
msgstr ""
"如果可選引數 *topdown* 為 ``True`` 或未指定，則目錄的三元組會在其任何子目錄的"
"三元組之前產生（目錄由上而下產生）。如果 *topdown* 為 ``False``，則目錄的三元"
"組會在其所有子目錄的三元組之後產生（目錄由下而上產生）。無論 *topdown* 的值為"
"何，子目錄串列都會在產生該目錄及其子目錄的元組之前取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4235
msgid ""
"When *topdown* is ``True``, the caller can modify the *dirnames* list in-"
"place (perhaps using :keyword:`del` or slice assignment), and :func:`walk` "
"will only recurse into the subdirectories whose names remain in *dirnames*; "
"this can be used to prune the search, impose a specific order of visiting, "
"or even to inform :func:`walk` about directories the caller creates or "
"renames before it resumes :func:`walk` again.  Modifying *dirnames* when "
"*topdown* is ``False`` has no effect on the behavior of the walk, because in "
"bottom-up mode the directories in *dirnames* are generated before *dirpath* "
"itself is generated."
msgstr ""
"當 *topdown* 為 ``True`` 時，呼叫者可以原地修改 *dirnames* 串列（例如使"
"用 :keyword:`del` 或切片賦值），而 :func:`walk` 只會遞迴進入名稱仍保留在 "
"*dirnames* 中的子目錄；這可以用來修剪搜尋範圍、強制指定特定的走訪順序，甚至可"
"以在呼叫者再次恢復 :func:`walk` 之前，把呼叫者自己建立或重新命名的目錄告"
"知 :func:`walk`。當 *topdown* 為 ``False`` 時，修改 *dirnames* 對走訪行為沒有"
"影響，因為在由下而上模式中，*dirnames* 中的目錄會在 *dirpath* 本身產生之前就"
"已產生。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4244
msgid ""
"By default, errors from the :func:`scandir` call are ignored.  If optional "
"argument *onerror* is specified, it should be a function; it will be called "
"with one argument, an :exc:`OSError` instance.  It can report the error to "
"continue with the walk, or raise the exception to abort the walk.  Note that "
"the filename is available as the ``filename`` attribute of the exception "
"object."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，來自 :func:`scandir` 呼叫的錯誤會被忽略。如果有指定可選引數 "
"*onerror*，它應該是一個函式；呼叫它時會傳入一個引數，即一個 :exc:`OSError` 實"
"例。它可以回報錯誤後繼續走訪，或引發例外來中止走訪。請注意，檔案名稱可以透過"
"例外物件的 ``filename`` 屬性取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4250
msgid ""
"By default, :func:`walk` will not walk down into symbolic links that resolve "
"to directories. Set *followlinks* to ``True`` to visit directories pointed "
"to by symlinks, on systems that support them."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，:func:`walk` 不會走訪進入解析為目錄的符號連結。在支援符號連結的系"
"統上，將 *followlinks* 設為 ``True`` 即可走訪符號連結所指向的目錄。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4256
msgid ""
"Be aware that setting *followlinks* to ``True`` can lead to infinite "
"recursion if a link points to a parent directory of itself. :func:`walk` "
"does not keep track of the directories it visited already."
msgstr ""
"請注意，如果連結指向其自身的父目錄，將 *followlinks* 設為 ``True`` 可能會導致"
"無限遞迴。:func:`walk` 不會記錄它已經走訪過的目錄。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4262
msgid ""
"If you pass a relative pathname, don't change the current working directory "
"between resumptions of :func:`walk`.  :func:`walk` never changes the current "
"directory, and assumes that its caller doesn't either."
msgstr ""
"如果你傳入相對路徑名稱，請勿在 :func:`walk` 兩次恢復執行之間更改目前工作目"
"錄。:func:`walk` 永遠不會更改目前目錄，並假設其呼叫者也不會。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4266 ../../library/os.rst:4328
msgid ""
"This example displays the number of bytes taken by non-directory files in "
"each directory under the starting directory, except that it doesn't look "
"under any ``__pycache__`` subdirectory::"
msgstr ""
"此範例會顯示起始目錄下每個目錄中非目錄檔案所佔用的位元組數，但不會查看任何 "
"``__pycache__`` 子目錄： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4270
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"from os.path import join, getsize\n"
"for root, dirs, files in os.walk('python/Lib/xml'):\n"
"    print(root, \"consumes\", end=\" \")\n"
"    print(sum(getsize(join(root, name)) for name in files), end=\" \")\n"
"    print(\"bytes in\", len(files), \"non-directory files\")\n"
"    if '__pycache__' in dirs:\n"
"        dirs.remove('__pycache__')  # don't visit __pycache__ directories"
msgstr ""
"import os\n"
"from os.path import join, getsize\n"
"for root, dirs, files in os.walk('python/Lib/xml'):\n"
"    print(root, \"consumes\", end=\" \")\n"
"    print(sum(getsize(join(root, name)) for name in files), end=\" \")\n"
"    print(\"bytes in\", len(files), \"non-directory files\")\n"
"    if '__pycache__' in dirs:\n"
"        dirs.remove('__pycache__')  # 不要走訪 __pycache__ 目錄"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4279
msgid ""
"In the next example (simple implementation of :func:`shutil.rmtree`), "
"walking the tree bottom-up is essential, :func:`rmdir` doesn't allow "
"deleting a directory before the directory is empty::"
msgstr ""
"在下一個範例中（:func:`shutil.rmtree` 的簡單實作），由下而上走訪目錄樹是必要"
"的，因為 :func:`rmdir` 不允許在目錄清空之前刪除該目錄： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4283
msgid ""
"# Delete everything reachable from the directory named in \"top\",\n"
"# assuming there are no symbolic links.\n"
"# CAUTION:  This is dangerous!  For example, if top == '/', it\n"
"# could delete all your disk files.\n"
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files in os.walk(top, topdown=False):\n"
"    for name in files:\n"
"        os.remove(os.path.join(root, name))\n"
"    for name in dirs:\n"
"        os.rmdir(os.path.join(root, name))\n"
"os.rmdir(top)"
msgstr ""
"# 刪除從 \"top\" 所指名的目錄可到達的所有內容，\n"
"# 假設其中沒有符號連結。\n"
"# 注意：這很危險！例如，如果 top == '/'，\n"
"# 它可能會刪除你所有的磁碟檔案。\n"
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files in os.walk(top, topdown=False):\n"
"    for name in files:\n"
"        os.remove(os.path.join(root, name))\n"
"    for name in dirs:\n"
"        os.rmdir(os.path.join(root, name))\n"
"os.rmdir(top)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4295
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.walk`` with arguments "
"``top``, ``topdown``, ``onerror``, ``followlinks``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``top``、``topdown``、``onerror``、``followlinks`` 的"
"\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.walk``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4297
msgid ""
"This function now calls :func:`os.scandir` instead of :func:`os.listdir`, "
"making it faster by reducing the number of calls to :func:`os.stat`."
msgstr ""
"此函式現在會呼叫 :func:`os.scandir` 而不是 :func:`os.listdir`，藉由減少呼"
"叫 :func:`os.stat` 的次數使其更快。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4311
msgid ""
"This behaves exactly like :func:`walk`, except that it yields a 4-tuple "
"``(dirpath, dirnames, filenames, dirfd)``, and it supports ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"此函式的行為與 :func:`walk` 完全相同，差別在於它會產生一個 4 元組 "
"``(dirpath, dirnames, filenames, dirfd)``，並且支援 ``dir_fd``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4314
msgid ""
"*dirpath*, *dirnames* and *filenames* are identical to :func:`walk` output, "
"and *dirfd* is a file descriptor referring to the directory *dirpath*."
msgstr ""
"*dirpath*、*dirnames* 與 *filenames* 與 :func:`walk` 的輸出相同，而 *dirfd* "
"是指向目錄 *dirpath* 的檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4317
msgid ""
"This function always supports :ref:`paths relative to directory descriptors "
"<dir_fd>` and :ref:`not following symlinks <follow_symlinks>`.  Note however "
"that, unlike other functions, the :func:`fwalk` default value for "
"*follow_symlinks* is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"此函式一律支援\\ :ref:`相對於目錄描述器的路徑 <dir_fd>`\\ 與\\ :ref:`不跟隨符"
"號連結 <follow_symlinks>`。但請注意，與其他函式不同，:func:`fwalk` 的 "
"*follow_symlinks* 預設值為 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4324
msgid ""
"Since :func:`fwalk` yields file descriptors, those are only valid until the "
"next iteration step, so you should duplicate them (e.g. with :func:`dup`) if "
"you want to keep them longer."
msgstr ""
"由於 :func:`fwalk` 會產生檔案描述器，而這些檔案描述器只在下一個疊代步驟之前有"
"效，因此如果你想保留它們更久，應該複製它們（例如使用 :func:`dup`）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4332
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files, rootfd in os.fwalk('python/Lib/xml'):\n"
"    print(root, \"consumes\", end=\" \")\n"
"    print(sum([os.stat(name, dir_fd=rootfd).st_size for name in files]),\n"
"          end=\" \")\n"
"    print(\"bytes in\", len(files), \"non-directory files\")\n"
"    if '__pycache__' in dirs:\n"
"        dirs.remove('__pycache__')  # don't visit __pycache__ directories"
msgstr ""
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files, rootfd in os.fwalk('python/Lib/xml'):\n"
"    print(root, \"consumes\", end=\" \")\n"
"    print(sum([os.stat(name, dir_fd=rootfd).st_size for name in files]),\n"
"          end=\" \")\n"
"    print(\"bytes in\", len(files), \"non-directory files\")\n"
"    if '__pycache__' in dirs:\n"
"        dirs.remove('__pycache__')  # 不要走訪 __pycache__ 目錄"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4341
msgid ""
"In the next example, walking the tree bottom-up is essential: :func:`rmdir` "
"doesn't allow deleting a directory before the directory is empty::"
msgstr ""
"在下一個範例中，由下而上走訪目錄樹是必要的：:func:`rmdir` 不允許在目錄清空之"
"前刪除該目錄： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4345
msgid ""
"# Delete everything reachable from the directory named in \"top\",\n"
"# assuming there are no symbolic links.\n"
"# CAUTION:  This is dangerous!  For example, if top == '/', it\n"
"# could delete all your disk files.\n"
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files, rootfd in os.fwalk(top, topdown=False):\n"
"    for name in files:\n"
"        os.unlink(name, dir_fd=rootfd)\n"
"    for name in dirs:\n"
"        os.rmdir(name, dir_fd=rootfd)"
msgstr ""
"# 刪除從 \"top\" 所指名的目錄可到達的所有內容，\n"
"# 假設其中沒有符號連結。\n"
"# 注意：這很危險！例如，如果 top == '/'，\n"
"# 它可能會刪除你所有的磁碟檔案。\n"
"import os\n"
"for root, dirs, files, rootfd in os.fwalk(top, topdown=False):\n"
"    for name in files:\n"
"        os.unlink(name, dir_fd=rootfd)\n"
"    for name in dirs:\n"
"        os.rmdir(name, dir_fd=rootfd)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4356
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.fwalk`` with arguments "
"``top``, ``topdown``, ``onerror``, ``follow_symlinks``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``top``、``topdown``、``onerror``、``follow_symlinks``、"
"``dir_fd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.fwalk``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4365
msgid "Added support for :class:`bytes` paths."
msgstr "新增對 :class:`bytes` 路徑的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4371
msgid ""
"Create an anonymous file and return a file descriptor that refers to it. "
"*flags* must be one of the ``os.MFD_*`` constants available on the system "
"(or a bitwise ORed combination of them).  By default, the new file "
"descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"建立一個匿名檔案，並回傳指向它的檔案描述器。*flags* 必須是系統上可用的 "
"``os.MFD_*`` 常數之一（或它們以位元 OR 組合的結果）。預設情況下，新的檔案描述"
"器為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4376
msgid ""
"The name supplied in *name* is used as a filename and will be displayed as "
"the target of the corresponding symbolic link in the directory ``/proc/self/"
"fd/``. The displayed name is always prefixed with ``memfd:`` and serves only "
"for debugging purposes. Names do not affect the behavior of the file "
"descriptor, and as such multiple files can have the same name without any "
"side effects."
msgstr ""
"*name* 中提供的名稱會被用作檔案名稱，並會顯示為 ``/proc/self/fd/`` 目錄中對應"
"符號連結的目標。顯示的名稱一律帶有 ``memfd:`` 前綴，且僅供除錯之用。名稱不會"
"影響檔案描述器的行為，因此多個檔案可以使用相同的名稱而不會產生任何副作用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4406
msgid "These flags can be passed to :func:`memfd_create`."
msgstr "這些旗標可以傳給 :func:`memfd_create`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4410
msgid "The ``MFD_HUGE*`` flags are only available since Linux 4.14."
msgstr "``MFD_HUGE*`` 旗標僅在 Linux 4.14 以上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4417
msgid ""
"Create and return an event file descriptor. The file descriptors supports "
"raw :func:`read` and :func:`write` with a buffer size of "
"8, :func:`~select.select`, :func:`~select.poll` and similar. See man "
"page :manpage:`eventfd(2)` for more information.  By default, the new file "
"descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"建立並回傳一個事件檔案描述器。該檔案描述器支援緩衝區大小為 8 的原"
"始 :func:`read` "
"與 :func:`write`、:func:`~select.select`、:func:`~select.poll` 以及類似操作。"
"更多資訊請參閱使用手冊 :manpage:`eventfd(2)`。預設情況下，新的檔案描述器為"
"\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4423
msgid ""
"*initval* is the initial value of the event counter. The initial value must "
"be a 32 bit unsigned integer. Please note that the initial value is limited "
"to a 32 bit unsigned int although the event counter is an unsigned 64 bit "
"integer with a maximum value of 2\\ :sup:`64`\\ -\\ 2."
msgstr ""
"*initval* 是事件計數器的初始值。初始值必須是 32 位元無符號整數。請注意，雖然"
"事件計數器是最大值為 2\\ :sup:`64`\\ -\\ 2 的 64 位元無符號整數，但初始值仍限"
"制為 32 位元無符號 int。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4428
msgid ""
"*flags* can be constructed from :const:`EFD_CLOEXEC`, :const:`EFD_NONBLOCK`, "
"and :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE`."
msgstr ""
"*flags* 可以由 :const:`EFD_CLOEXEC`、:const:`EFD_NONBLOCK` "
"與 :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE` 組成。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4431
msgid ""
"If :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE` is specified and the event counter is non-"
"zero, :func:`eventfd_read` returns 1 and decrements the counter by one."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE` 且事件計數器不為零，:func:`eventfd_read` 會"
"回傳 1 並將計數器減一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4434
msgid ""
"If :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE` is not specified and the event counter is non-"
"zero, :func:`eventfd_read` returns the current event counter value and "
"resets the counter to zero."
msgstr ""
"如果未指定 :const:`EFD_SEMAPHORE` 且事件計數器不為零，:func:`eventfd_read` 會"
"回傳目前的事件計數器值，並將計數器重設為零。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4438
msgid ""
"If the event counter is zero and :const:`EFD_NONBLOCK` is not "
"specified, :func:`eventfd_read` blocks."
msgstr ""
"如果事件計數器為零且未指定 :const:`EFD_NONBLOCK`，:func:`eventfd_read` 會阻"
"塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4441
msgid ""
":func:`eventfd_write` increments the event counter. Write blocks if the "
"write operation would increment the counter to a value larger than "
"2\\ :sup:`64`\\ -\\ 2."
msgstr ""
":func:`eventfd_write` 會遞增事件計數器。如果寫入操作會使計數器遞增到大於 "
"2\\ :sup:`64`\\ -\\ 2 的值，則寫入會阻塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4447
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"\n"
"# semaphore with start value '1'\n"
"fd = os.eventfd(1, os.EFD_SEMAPHORE | os.EFD_CLOEXEC)\n"
"try:\n"
"    # acquire semaphore\n"
"    v = os.eventfd_read(fd)\n"
"    try:\n"
"        do_work()\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        # release semaphore\n"
"        os.eventfd_write(fd, v)\n"
"finally:\n"
"    os.close(fd)"
msgstr ""
"import os\n"
"\n"
"# 初始值為 '1' 的號誌\n"
"fd = os.eventfd(1, os.EFD_SEMAPHORE | os.EFD_CLOEXEC)\n"
"try:\n"
"    # 取得號誌\n"
"    v = os.eventfd_read(fd)\n"
"    try:\n"
"        do_work()\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        # 釋放號誌\n"
"        os.eventfd_write(fd, v)\n"
"finally:\n"
"    os.close(fd)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4468
msgid ""
"Read value from an :func:`eventfd` file descriptor and return a 64 bit "
"unsigned int. The function does not verify that *fd* is an :func:`eventfd`."
msgstr ""
"從 :func:`eventfd` 檔案描述器讀取值，並回傳 64 位元無符號 int。此函式不會驗"
"證 *fd* 是否為 :func:`eventfd`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4477
msgid ""
"Add value to an :func:`eventfd` file descriptor. *value* must be a 64 bit "
"unsigned int. The function does not verify that *fd* is an :func:`eventfd`."
msgstr ""
"將值加到 :func:`eventfd` 檔案描述器。*value* 必須是 64 位元無符號 int。此函式"
"不會驗證 *fd* 是否為 :func:`eventfd`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4486
msgid "Set close-on-exec flag for new :func:`eventfd` file descriptor."
msgstr "為新的 :func:`eventfd` 檔案描述器設定 close-on-exec 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4494
msgid ""
"Set :const:`O_NONBLOCK` status flag for new :func:`eventfd` file descriptor."
msgstr "設定新的 :func:`eventfd` 檔案描述器的 :const:`O_NONBLOCK` 狀態旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4503
msgid ""
"Provide semaphore-like semantics for reads from an :func:`eventfd` file "
"descriptor. On read the internal counter is decremented by one."
msgstr ""
"為從 :func:`eventfd` 檔案描述器進行的讀取提供類似號誌 (semaphore) 的語意。讀"
"取時，內部計數器會減一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4514
msgid "Timer File Descriptors"
msgstr "計時器檔案描述器"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4518
msgid ""
"These functions provide support for Linux's *timer file descriptor* API. "
"Naturally, they are all only available on Linux."
msgstr ""
"這些函式提供對 Linux *計時器檔案描述器* (timer file descriptor) API 的支援。"
"當然，它們都只能在 Linux 上使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4523
msgid "Create and return a timer file descriptor (*timerfd*)."
msgstr "建立並回傳一個計時器檔案描述器 (*timerfd*)。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4525
msgid "The file descriptor returned by :func:`timerfd_create` supports:"
msgstr ":func:`timerfd_create` 回傳的檔案描述器支援："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4527
msgid ":func:`read`"
msgstr ":func:`read`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4528
msgid ":func:`~select.select`"
msgstr ":func:`~select.select`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4529
msgid ":func:`~select.poll`"
msgstr ":func:`~select.poll`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4531
msgid ""
"The file descriptor's :func:`read` method can be called with a buffer size "
"of 8. If the timer has already expired one or more times, :func:`read` "
"returns the number of expirations with the host's endianness, which may be "
"converted to an :class:`int` by ``int.from_bytes(x, "
"byteorder=sys.byteorder)``."
msgstr ""
"該檔案描述器的 :func:`read` 方法可以用 8 作為緩衝區大小來呼叫。如果計時器已經"
"到期一次或多次，:func:`read` 會以主機的位元組順序回傳到期次數，可以透過 "
"``int.from_bytes(x, byteorder=sys.byteorder)`` 將其轉換為 :class:`int`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4536
msgid ""
":func:`~select.select` and :func:`~select.poll` can be used to wait until "
"timer expires and the file descriptor is readable."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 :func:`~select.select` 與 :func:`~select.poll` 來等待計時器到期且檔"
"案描述器變為可讀取。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4539
msgid ""
"*clockid* must be a valid :ref:`clock ID <time-clock-id-constants>`, as "
"defined in the :py:mod:`time` module:"
msgstr ""
"*clockid* 必須是有效的\\ :ref:`時鐘 ID <time-clock-id-constants>`，"
"如 :py:mod:`time` 模組中所定義："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4542
msgid ":const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`"
msgstr ":const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4543
msgid ":const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC`"
msgstr ":const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4544
msgid ":const:`time.CLOCK_BOOTTIME` (Since Linux 3.15 for timerfd_create)"
msgstr ""
":const:`time.CLOCK_BOOTTIME`\\ （自 Linux 3.15 起適用於 timerfd_create）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4546
msgid ""
"If *clockid* is :const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`, a settable system-wide real-"
"time clock is used. If the system clock is changed, the timer setting needs "
"to be updated. To cancel the timer when the system clock is changed, "
"see :const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET`."
msgstr ""
"如果 *clockid* 為 :const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`，則會使用可設定的系統層級即時"
"時鐘。如果系統時鐘被更改，則需要更新計時器設定。若要在系統時鐘被更改時取消計"
"時器，請參閱 :const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4551
msgid ""
"If *clockid* is :const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC`, a non-settable monotonically "
"increasing clock is used. Even if the system clock is changed, the timer "
"setting will not be affected."
msgstr ""
"如果 *clockid* 為 :const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC`，則會使用不可設定、單調遞增的"
"時鐘。即使系統時鐘被更改，計時器設定也不會受到影響。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4555
msgid ""
"If *clockid* is :const:`time.CLOCK_BOOTTIME`, it is the same "
"as :const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC` except it includes any time that the system "
"is suspended."
msgstr ""
"如果 *clockid* 為 :const:`time.CLOCK_BOOTTIME`，則"
"與 :const:`time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC` 相同，差別在於它包含系統休眠 (suspend) 期間"
"的所有時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4559
msgid ""
"The file descriptor's behaviour can be modified by specifying a *flags* "
"value. Any of the following variables may be used, combined using bitwise OR "
"(the ``|`` operator):"
msgstr ""
"可以透過指定 *flags* 值來修改檔案描述器的行為。可以使用以下任何變數，並以位"
"元 OR（``|`` 運算子）組合："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4563
msgid ":const:`TFD_NONBLOCK`"
msgstr ":const:`TFD_NONBLOCK`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4564
msgid ":const:`TFD_CLOEXEC`"
msgstr ":const:`TFD_CLOEXEC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4566
msgid ""
"If :const:`TFD_NONBLOCK` is not set as a flag, :func:`read` blocks until the "
"timer expires. If it is set as a flag, :func:`read` doesn't block, but if "
"there hasn't been an expiration since the last call to read, :func:`read` "
"raises :class:`OSError` with ``errno`` set to :const:`errno.EAGAIN`."
msgstr ""
"如果未設定 :const:`TFD_NONBLOCK` 旗標，:func:`read` 會阻塞直到計時器到期。如"
"果有設定該旗標，:func:`read` 不會阻塞，但如果自上次呼叫 read 以來沒有發生到"
"期，:func:`read` 會引發 :class:`OSError`，且 ``errno`` 會被設"
"為 :const:`errno.EAGAIN`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4572
msgid ":const:`TFD_CLOEXEC` is always set by Python automatically."
msgstr ":const:`TFD_CLOEXEC` 總是由 Python 自動設定。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4574
msgid ""
"The file descriptor must be closed with :func:`os.close` when it is no "
"longer needed, or else the file descriptor will be leaked."
msgstr ""
"當不再需要該檔案描述器時，必須使用 :func:`os.close` 將其關閉，否則該檔案描述"
"器會洩漏。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4577
msgid "The :manpage:`timerfd_create(2)` man page."
msgstr ":manpage:`timerfd_create(2)` 使用手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4586
msgid ""
"Alter a timer file descriptor's internal timer. This function operates the "
"same interval timer as :func:`timerfd_settime_ns`."
msgstr ""
"修改計時器檔案描述器的內部計時器。此函式與 :func:`timerfd_settime_ns` 操作的"
"是同一個間隔計時器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4589
msgid "*fd* must be a valid timer file descriptor."
msgstr "*fd* 必須是有效的計時器檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4591
msgid ""
"The timer's behaviour can be modified by specifying a *flags* value. Any of "
"the following variables may be used, combined using bitwise OR (the ``|`` "
"operator):"
msgstr ""
"可以透過指定 *flags* 值來修改計時器的行為。可以使用以下任何變數，並以位元 OR"
"（``|`` 運算子）組合："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4595
msgid ":const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME`"
msgstr ":const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4596
msgid ":const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET`"
msgstr ":const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4598
msgid ""
"The timer is disabled by setting *initial* to zero (``0``). If *initial* is "
"greater than zero, the timer is enabled. If *initial* is less than zero, it "
"raises an :class:`OSError` exception with ``errno`` set "
"to :const:`errno.EINVAL`."
msgstr ""
"將 *initial* 設為零 (``0``) 會停用計時器。如果 *initial* 大於零，則會啟用計時"
"器。如果 *initial* 小於零，則會引發 :class:`OSError` 例外，且 ``errno`` 會被"
"設為 :const:`errno.EINVAL`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4603
msgid "By default the timer will fire when *initial* seconds have elapsed."
msgstr "預設情況下，計時器會在經過 *initial* 秒後觸發。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4605
msgid ""
"However, if the :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` flag is set, the timer will fire "
"when the timer's clock (set by *clockid* in :func:`timerfd_create`) reaches "
"*initial* seconds."
msgstr ""
"然而，如果設定了 :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` 旗標，計時器會在計時器的時鐘"
"（由 :func:`timerfd_create` 中的 *clockid* 設定）達到 *initial* 秒時觸發。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4609
msgid ""
"The timer's interval is set by the *interval* real number. If *interval* is "
"zero, the timer only fires once, on the initial expiration. If *interval* is "
"greater than zero, the timer fires every time *interval* seconds have "
"elapsed since the previous expiration. If *interval* is less than zero, it "
"raises :class:`OSError` with ``errno`` set to :const:`errno.EINVAL`."
msgstr ""
"計時器的間隔由實數 *interval* 設定。如果 *interval* 為零，計時器只會在初次到"
"期時觸發一次。如果 *interval* 大於零，計時器會在每次距離上次到期經過 "
"*interval* 秒時觸發。如果 *interval* 小於零，則會引發 :class:`OSError`，且 "
"``errno`` 會被設為 :const:`errno.EINVAL`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4616
msgid ""
"If the :const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET` flag is set along "
"with :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` and the clock for this timer "
"is :const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`, the timer is marked as cancelable if the "
"real-time clock is changed discontinuously. Reading the descriptor is "
"aborted with the error :const:`errno.ECANCELED`."
msgstr ""
"如果 :const:`TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET` 旗標與 :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` 一起"
"設定，且此計時器的時鐘為 :const:`time.CLOCK_REALTIME`，則當即時時鐘發生不連續"
"的變更時，計時器會被標記為可取消。讀取該描述器時會以錯"
"誤 :const:`errno.ECANCELED` 中止。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4622
msgid ""
"Linux manages system clock as UTC. A daylight-savings time transition is "
"done by changing time offset only and doesn't cause discontinuous system "
"clock change."
msgstr ""
"Linux 以 UTC 管理系統時鐘。日光節約時間的轉換僅透過更改時間偏移量來完成，不會"
"造成系統時鐘的不連續變更。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4626
msgid ""
"Discontinuous system clock change will be caused by the following events:"
msgstr "以下事件會造成系統時鐘的不連續變更："

#: ../../library/os.rst:4628
msgid "``settimeofday``"
msgstr "``settimeofday``"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4629
msgid "``clock_settime``"
msgstr "``clock_settime``"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4630
msgid "set the system date and time by ``date`` command"
msgstr "透過 ``date`` 命令設定系統日期與時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4632
msgid ""
"Return a two-item tuple of (``next_expiration``, ``interval``) from the "
"previous timer state, before this function executed."
msgstr ""
"回傳此函式執行前的計時器狀態，形式為二元組 (``next_expiration``, "
"``interval``)。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4637
msgid ""
":manpage:`timerfd_create(2)`, :manpage:`timerfd_settime(2)`, :manpage:`settimeofday(2)`, :manpage:`clock_settime(2)`, "
"and :manpage:`date(1)`."
msgstr ""
":manpage:`timerfd_create(2)`、:manpage:`timerfd_settime(2)`、:manpage:`settimeofday(2)`、:manpage:`clock_settime(2)` "
"與 :manpage:`date(1)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4648
msgid ""
"Similar to :func:`timerfd_settime`, but use time as nanoseconds. This "
"function operates the same interval timer as :func:`timerfd_settime`."
msgstr ""
"與 :func:`timerfd_settime` 類似，但以奈秒為單位使用時間。此函式"
"與 :func:`timerfd_settime` 操作的是同一個間隔計時器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4658
msgid "Return a two-item tuple of floats (``next_expiration``, ``interval``)."
msgstr "回傳一個由浮點數組成的二元組 (``next_expiration``, ``interval``)。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4660
msgid ""
"``next_expiration`` denotes the relative time until the timer next fires, "
"regardless of if the :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` flag is set."
msgstr ""
"``next_expiration`` 表示距離計時器下次觸發的相對時間，無論是否設定"
"了 :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4663
msgid ""
"``interval`` denotes the timer's interval. If zero, the timer will only fire "
"once, after ``next_expiration`` seconds have elapsed."
msgstr ""
"``interval`` 表示計時器的間隔。如果為零，計時器只會在經過 "
"``next_expiration`` 秒後觸發一次。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4667
msgid ":manpage:`timerfd_gettime(2)`"
msgstr ":manpage:`timerfd_gettime(2)`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4676
msgid "Similar to :func:`timerfd_gettime`, but return time as nanoseconds."
msgstr "與 :func:`timerfd_gettime` 類似，但以奈秒為單位回傳時間。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4684
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`timerfd_create` function, which sets "
"the :const:`O_NONBLOCK` status flag for the new timer file descriptor. "
"If :const:`TFD_NONBLOCK` is not set as a flag, :func:`read` blocks."
msgstr ""
":func:`timerfd_create` 函式的旗標，會為新的計時器檔案描述器設"
"定 :const:`O_NONBLOCK` 狀態旗標。如果未設定 :const:`TFD_NONBLOCK` 旗"
"標，:func:`read` 會阻塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4694
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`timerfd_create` function, If :const:`TFD_CLOEXEC` is "
"set as a flag, set close-on-exec flag for new file descriptor."
msgstr ""
":func:`timerfd_create` 函式的旗標。如果設定了 :const:`TFD_CLOEXEC` 旗標，則會"
"為新的檔案描述器設定 close-on-exec 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4704
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`timerfd_settime` and :func:`timerfd_settime_ns` "
"functions. If this flag is set, *initial* is interpreted as an absolute "
"value on the timer's clock (in UTC seconds or nanoseconds since the Unix "
"Epoch)."
msgstr ""
":func:`timerfd_settime` 與 :func:`timerfd_settime_ns` 函式的旗標。如果設定了"
"此旗標，*initial* 會被解讀為計時器時鐘上的絕對值（自 Unix 紀元起算的 UTC 秒數"
"或奈秒數）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4714
msgid ""
"A flag for the :func:`timerfd_settime` and :func:`timerfd_settime_ns` "
"functions along with :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME`. The timer is cancelled when "
"the time of the underlying clock changes discontinuously."
msgstr ""
":func:`timerfd_settime` 與 :func:`timerfd_settime_ns` 函式的旗標，需"
"與 :const:`TFD_TIMER_ABSTIME` 一起使用。當底層時鐘的時間發生不連續變更時，計"
"時器會被取消。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4725
msgid "Linux extended attributes"
msgstr "Linux 延伸屬性 (extended attributes)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4729
msgid "These functions are all available on Linux only."
msgstr "這些函式都只能在 Linux 上使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4733
msgid ""
"Return the value of the extended filesystem attribute *attribute* for "
"*path*. *attribute* can be bytes or str (directly or indirectly through "
"the :class:`PathLike` interface). If it is str, it is encoded with the "
"filesystem encoding."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *path* 的延伸檔案系統屬性 *attribute* 的值。*attribute* 可以是 bytes 或 "
"str（直接或間接透過 :class:`PathLike` 介面）。如果是 str，則會以檔案系統編碼"
"進行編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4741
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.getxattr`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``attribute``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``attribute`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.getxattr``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4743 ../../library/os.rst:4779
#: ../../library/os.rst:4804
msgid "Accepts a :term:`path-like object` for *path* and *attribute*."
msgstr "*path* 與 *attribute* 接受\\ :term:`類路徑物件 <path-like object>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4749
msgid ""
"Return a list of the extended filesystem attributes on *path*.  The "
"attributes in the list are represented as strings decoded with the "
"filesystem encoding.  If *path* is ``None``, :func:`listxattr` will examine "
"the current directory."
msgstr ""
"回傳 *path* 上的延伸檔案系統屬性串列。串列中的屬性以使用檔案系統編碼解碼後的"
"字串表示。如果 *path* 為 ``None``，:func:`listxattr` 會檢查目前目錄。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4757
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.listxattr`` with argument "
"``path``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.listxattr``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4762
msgid ""
"``os.listxattr(-1)`` now fails with ``OSError(errno.EBADF)`` rather than "
"listing extended attributes of the current directory."
msgstr ""
"``os.listxattr(-1)`` 現在會以 ``OSError(errno.EBADF)`` 失敗，而不是列出目前目"
"錄的延伸屬性。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4769
msgid ""
"Removes the extended filesystem attribute *attribute* from *path*. "
"*attribute* should be bytes or str (directly or indirectly through "
"the :class:`PathLike` interface). If it is a string, it is encoded with "
"the :term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`."
msgstr ""
"從 *path* 中移除延伸檔案系統屬性 *attribute*。*attribute* 應為 bytes 或 str"
"（直接或間接透過 :class:`PathLike` 介面）。如果是字串，則會以\\ :term:`檔案系"
"統編碼和錯誤處理函式 <filesystem encoding and error handler>`\\ 進行編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4777
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.removexattr`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``attribute``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``attribute`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.removexattr``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4785
msgid ""
"Set the extended filesystem attribute *attribute* on *path* to *value*. "
"*attribute* must be a bytes or str with no embedded NULs (directly or "
"indirectly through the :class:`PathLike` interface). If it is a str, it is "
"encoded with the :term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`.  *flags* may "
"be :data:`XATTR_REPLACE` or :data:`XATTR_CREATE`. If :data:`XATTR_REPLACE` "
"is given and the attribute does not exist, ``ENODATA`` will be raised. "
"If :data:`XATTR_CREATE` is given and the attribute already exists, the "
"attribute will not be created and ``EEXISTS`` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"將 *path* 上的延伸檔案系統屬性 *attribute* 設為 *value*。*attribute* 必須是不"
"含內嵌 NUL 的 bytes 或 str（直接或間接透過 :class:`PathLike` 介面）。如果是 "
"str，則會以\\ :term:`檔案系統編碼和錯誤處理函式 <filesystem encoding and "
"error handler>`\\ 進行編碼。*flags* 可以是 :data:`XATTR_REPLACE` "
"或 :data:`XATTR_CREATE`。如果給定 :data:`XATTR_REPLACE` 且該屬性不存在，則會"
"引發 ``ENODATA``。如果給定 :data:`XATTR_CREATE` 且該屬性已存在，則不會建立該"
"屬性，並會引發 ``EEXISTS``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4799
msgid ""
"A bug in Linux kernel versions less than 2.6.39 caused the flags argument to "
"be ignored on some filesystems."
msgstr ""
"低於 2.6.39 的 Linux 核心版本中有一個錯誤，導致某些檔案系統會忽略 flags 引"
"數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4802
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.setxattr`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``attribute``, ``value``, ``flags``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``attribute``、``value``、``flags`` 的\\ :ref:`稽"
"核事件 <auditing>` ``os.setxattr``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4810
msgid ""
"The maximum size the value of an extended attribute can be. Currently, this "
"is 64 KiB on Linux."
msgstr "延伸屬性值的最大大小。目前在 Linux 上為 64 KiB。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4816
msgid ""
"This is a possible value for the flags argument in :func:`setxattr`. It "
"indicates the operation must create an attribute."
msgstr ""
"這是 :func:`setxattr` 中 flags 引數的可能值。它表示該操作必須建立屬性。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4822
msgid ""
"This is a possible value for the flags argument in :func:`setxattr`. It "
"indicates the operation must replace an existing attribute."
msgstr ""
"這是 :func:`setxattr` 中 flags 引數的可能值。它表示該操作必須取代現有的屬性。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4829
msgid "Process Management"
msgstr "行程管理"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4831
msgid "These functions may be used to create and manage processes."
msgstr "這些函式可用於建立和管理行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4833
msgid ""
"The various :func:`exec\\* <execl>` functions take a list of arguments for "
"the new program loaded into the process.  In each case, the first of these "
"arguments is passed to the new program as its own name rather than as an "
"argument a user may have typed on a command line.  For the C programmer, "
"this is the ``argv[0]`` passed to a program's :c:func:`main`.  For example, "
"``os.execv('/bin/echo', ['foo', 'bar'])`` will only print ``bar`` on "
"standard output; ``foo`` will seem to be ignored."
msgstr ""
"各種 :func:`exec\\* <execl>` 函式接受一個引數串列，用於載入到行程中的新程式。"
"在每種情況下，這些引數中的第一個會作為新程式本身的名稱傳給它，而不是作為使用"
"者可能在命令列上輸入的引數。對 C 程式設計師而言，這就是傳給程"
"式 :c:func:`main` 的 ``argv[0]``。例如，``os.execv('/bin/echo', ['foo', "
"'bar'])`` 只會在標準輸出上印出 ``bar``；``foo`` 看起來會被忽略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4844
msgid ""
"Generate a :const:`~signal.SIGABRT` signal to the current process.  On Unix, "
"the default behavior is to produce a core dump; on Windows, the process "
"immediately returns an exit code of ``3``.  Be aware that calling this "
"function will not call the Python signal handler registered "
"for :const:`~signal.SIGABRT` with :func:`signal.signal`."
msgstr ""
"對目前行程產生 :const:`~signal.SIGABRT` 訊號。在 Unix 上，預設行為是產生核心"
"傾印 (core dump)；在 Windows 上，行程會立即回傳結束代碼 ``3``。請注意，呼叫此"
"函式不會呼叫透過 :func:`signal.signal` 為 :const:`~signal.SIGABRT` 註冊的 "
"Python 訊號處理程式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4853
msgid "Add a path to the DLL search path."
msgstr "將路徑新增到 DLL 搜尋路徑。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4855
msgid ""
"This search path is used when resolving dependencies for imported extension "
"modules (the module itself is resolved through :data:`sys.path`), and also "
"by :mod:`ctypes`."
msgstr ""
"此搜尋路徑用於解析已引入之擴充模組的相依性（模組本身是透過 :data:`sys.path` "
"解析的），也會被 :mod:`ctypes` 使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4859
msgid ""
"Remove the directory by calling **close()** on the returned object or using "
"it in a :keyword:`with` statement."
msgstr ""
"透過對回傳的物件呼叫 **close()**，或在 :keyword:`with` 陳述式中使用它，來將該"
"目錄從 DLL 搜尋路徑中移除。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4862
msgid ""
"See the `Microsoft documentation <https://msdn.microsoft.com/"
"44228cf2-6306-466c-8f16-f513cd3ba8b5>`_ for more information about how DLLs "
"are loaded."
msgstr ""
"關於 DLL 如何載入的更多資訊，請參閱 `Microsoft 文件 <https://"
"msdn.microsoft.com/44228cf2-6306-466c-8f16-f513cd3ba8b5>`_。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4866
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.add_dll_directory`` with "
"argument ``path``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.add_dll_directory``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4870
msgid ""
"Previous versions of CPython would resolve DLLs using the default behavior "
"for the current process. This led to inconsistencies, such as only sometimes "
"searching :envvar:`PATH` or the current working directory, and OS functions "
"such as ``AddDllDirectory`` having no effect."
msgstr ""
"先前版本的 CPython 會使用目前行程的預設行為來解析 DLL。這導致了不一致的情況，"
"例如有時會搜尋、有時又不會搜尋 :envvar:`PATH` 或目前工作目錄，以及像 "
"``AddDllDirectory`` 這樣的作業系統函式沒有作用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4877
msgid ""
"In 3.8, the two primary ways DLLs are loaded now explicitly override the "
"process-wide behavior to ensure consistency. See the :ref:`porting notes "
"<bpo-36085-whatsnew>` for information on updating libraries."
msgstr ""
"在 3.8 中，DLL 載入的兩種主要方式現在會明確覆寫整個行程的行為，以確保一致性。"
"關於更新函式庫的資訊，請參閱\\ :ref:`移植說明 <bpo-36085-whatsnew>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4892
msgid ""
"These functions all execute a new program, replacing the current process; "
"they do not return.  On Unix, the new executable is loaded into the current "
"process, and will have the same process id as the caller.  Errors will be "
"reported as :exc:`OSError` exceptions."
msgstr ""
"這些函式都會執行一個新程式，並取代目前的行程；它們不會回傳。在 Unix 上，新的"
"可執行檔會被載入到目前的行程中，並且會擁有與呼叫者相同的行程 ID。錯誤會"
"以 :exc:`OSError` 例外的形式回報。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4897
msgid ""
"The current process is replaced immediately. Open file objects and "
"descriptors are not flushed, so if there may be data buffered on these open "
"files, you should flush them using :func:`~io.IOBase.flush` "
"or :func:`os.fsync` before calling an :func:`exec\\* <execl>` function."
msgstr ""
"目前的行程會被立即取代。已開啟的檔案物件與描述器不會被清空 (flush)，因此如果"
"這些已開啟的檔案中可能有緩衝的資料，你應該在呼叫 :func:`exec\\* <execl>` 函式"
"之前，使用 :func:`~io.IOBase.flush` 或 :func:`os.fsync` 將其清空。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4903
msgid ""
"The \"l\" and \"v\" variants of the :func:`exec\\* <execl>` functions differ "
"in how command-line arguments are passed.  The \"l\" variants are perhaps "
"the easiest to work with if the number of parameters is fixed when the code "
"is written; the individual parameters simply become additional parameters to "
"the :func:`!execl\\*` functions.  The \"v\" variants are good when the "
"number of parameters is variable, with the arguments being passed in a list "
"or tuple as the *args* parameter.  In either case, the arguments to the "
"child process should start with the name of the command being run, but this "
"is not enforced."
msgstr ""
":func:`exec\\* <execl>` 函式的「l」與「v」變體的差別在於命令列引數的傳遞方"
"式。如果在撰寫程式碼時參數的數量是固定的，「l」變體或許是最容易使用的；個別參"
"數只需成為 :func:`!execl\\*` 函式的額外參數即可。當參數數量可變時，「v」變體"
"就很合適，引數會以串列或元組的形式作為 *args* 參數傳入。無論哪種情況，傳給子"
"行程的引數都應該以正在執行的命令名稱開頭，但這並非強制要求。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4912
msgid ""
"The variants which include a \"p\" near the end "
"(:func:`execlp`, :func:`execlpe`, :func:`execvp`, and :func:`execvpe`) will "
"use the :envvar:`PATH` environment variable to locate the program *file*.  "
"When the environment is being replaced (using one of the :func:`exec\\*e "
"<execl>` variants, discussed in the next paragraph), the new environment is "
"used as the source of the :envvar:`PATH` variable. The other "
"variants, :func:`execl`, :func:`execle`, :func:`execv`, and :func:`execve`, "
"will not use the :envvar:`PATH` variable to locate the executable; *path* "
"must contain an appropriate absolute or relative path. Relative paths must "
"include at least one slash, even on Windows, as plain names will not be "
"resolved."
msgstr ""
"名稱結尾附近包含「p」的變體（:func:`execlp`、:func:`execlpe`、:func:`execvp` "
"與 :func:`execvpe`）會使用 :envvar:`PATH` 環境變數來尋找程式 *file*。當環境被"
"取代時（使用下一段所討論的 :func:`exec\\*e <execl>` 變體之一），新環境會被用"
"作 :envvar:`PATH` 變數的來源。其他變"
"體 :func:`execl`、:func:`execle`、:func:`execv` 與 :func:`execve` 不會使"
"用 :envvar:`PATH` 變數來尋找可執行檔；*path* 必須包含適當的絕對或相對路徑。相"
"對路徑必須至少包含一個斜線，即使在 Windows 上也是如此，因為單純的名稱不會被解"
"析。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4923
msgid ""
"For :func:`execle`, :func:`execlpe`, :func:`execve`, and :func:`execvpe` "
"(note that these all end in \"e\"), the *env* parameter must be a mapping "
"which is used to define the environment variables for the new process (these "
"are used instead of the current process' environment); the "
"functions :func:`execl`, :func:`execlp`, :func:`execv`, and :func:`execvp` "
"all cause the new process to inherit the environment of the current process."
msgstr ""
"對於 :func:`execle`、:func:`execlpe`、:func:`execve` 與 :func:`execvpe`\\ "
"（請注意這些名稱都以「e」結尾），*env* 參數必須是一個對映，用來定義新行程的環"
"境變數（這些變數會用來代替目前行程的環境）；"
"而 :func:`execl`、:func:`execlp`、:func:`execv` 與 :func:`execvp` 函式都會使"
"新行程繼承目前行程的環境。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4930
msgid ""
"For :func:`execve` on some platforms, *path* may also be specified as an "
"open file descriptor.  This functionality may not be supported on your "
"platform; you can check whether or not it is available "
"using :data:`os.supports_fd`. If it is unavailable, using it will raise "
"a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"對於某些平台上的 :func:`execve`，*path* 也可以指定為已開啟的檔案描述器。你的"
"平台可能不支援此功能；你可以使用 :data:`os.supports_fd` 來檢查它是否可用。如"
"果不可用，使用它將會引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4935
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.exec`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``args``, ``env``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``args``、``env`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.exec``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4939
msgid ""
"Added support for specifying *path* as an open file descriptor "
"for :func:`execve`."
msgstr "新增為 :func:`execve` 將 *path* 指定為已開啟檔案描述器的支援。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4948
msgid ""
"Exit the process with status *n*, without calling cleanup handlers, flushing "
"stdio buffers, etc."
msgstr "以狀態 *n* 結束行程，而不呼叫清理處理函式、不清空 stdio 緩衝區等。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4953
msgid ""
"The standard way to exit is :func:`sys.exit(n) <sys.exit>`.  :func:`!_exit` "
"should normally only be used in the child process after a :func:`fork`."
msgstr ""
"結束的標準方式是 :func:`sys.exit(n) <sys.exit>`。:func:`!_exit` 通常只應"
"在 :func:`fork` 之後的子行程中使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4956
msgid ""
"The following exit codes are defined and can be used with :func:`_exit`, "
"although they are not required.  These are typically used for system "
"programs written in Python, such as a mail server's external command "
"delivery program."
msgstr ""
"以下結束代碼已有定義，可以與 :func:`_exit` 一起使用，但並非必要。這些通常用於"
"以 Python 撰寫的系統程式，例如郵件伺服器的外部命令遞送程式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4962
msgid ""
"Some of these may not be available on all Unix platforms, since there is "
"some variation.  These constants are defined where they are defined by the "
"underlying platform."
msgstr ""
"由於存在一些差異，其中某些可能並非在所有 Unix 平台上都可用。這些常數只會在底"
"層平台有定義的情況下才會被定義。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4969
msgid ""
"Exit code that means no error occurred. May be taken from the defined value "
"of ``EXIT_SUCCESS`` on some platforms. Generally has a value of zero."
msgstr ""
"表示沒有發生錯誤的結束代碼。在某些平台上，可能取自 ``EXIT_SUCCESS`` 的定義"
"值。其值通常為零。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4977
msgid ""
"Exit code that means the command was used incorrectly, such as when the "
"wrong number of arguments are given."
msgstr "表示命令使用方式不正確的結束代碼，例如給定了錯誤數量的引數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4985
msgid "Exit code that means the input data was incorrect."
msgstr "表示輸入資料不正確的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4992
msgid "Exit code that means an input file did not exist or was not readable."
msgstr "表示輸入檔案不存在或無法讀取的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:4999
msgid "Exit code that means a specified user did not exist."
msgstr "表示指定的使用者不存在的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5006
msgid "Exit code that means a specified host did not exist."
msgstr "表示指定的主機不存在的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5013
msgid "Exit code that means that a required service is unavailable."
msgstr "表示所需服務無法使用的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5020
msgid "Exit code that means an internal software error was detected."
msgstr "表示偵測到內部軟體錯誤的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5027
msgid ""
"Exit code that means an operating system error was detected, such as the "
"inability to fork or create a pipe."
msgstr "表示偵測到作業系統錯誤的結束代碼，例如無法 fork 或建立管道。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5035
msgid ""
"Exit code that means some system file did not exist, could not be opened, or "
"had some other kind of error."
msgstr "表示某些系統檔案不存在、無法開啟，或發生其他類型錯誤的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5043
msgid "Exit code that means a user specified output file could not be created."
msgstr "表示使用者指定的輸出檔案無法建立的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5050
msgid ""
"Exit code that means that an error occurred while doing I/O on some file."
msgstr "表示對某個檔案進行 I/O 時發生錯誤的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5057
msgid ""
"Exit code that means a temporary failure occurred.  This indicates something "
"that may not really be an error, such as a network connection that couldn't "
"be made during a retryable operation."
msgstr ""
"表示發生暫時性失敗的結束代碼。這表示某些情況可能並不是真正的錯誤，例如在可重"
"試的操作期間無法建立網路連線。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5066
msgid ""
"Exit code that means that a protocol exchange was illegal, invalid, or not "
"understood."
msgstr "表示協定交換不合法、無效或無法理解的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5074
msgid ""
"Exit code that means that there were insufficient permissions to perform the "
"operation (but not intended for file system problems)."
msgstr "表示權限不足以執行該操作的結束代碼（但並非用於檔案系統問題）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5082
msgid "Exit code that means that some kind of configuration error occurred."
msgstr "表示發生某種組態錯誤的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5089
msgid "Exit code that means something like \"an entry was not found\"."
msgstr "表示類似「找不到條目」之情況的結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5096
msgid ""
"Fork a child process.  Return ``0`` in the child and the child's process id "
"in the parent.  If an error occurs :exc:`OSError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Fork 出一個子行程。在子行程中回傳 ``0``，在父行程中回傳子行程的行程 ID。如果"
"發生錯誤，會引發 :exc:`OSError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5099
msgid ""
"Note that some platforms including FreeBSD <= 6.3 and Cygwin have known "
"issues when using ``fork()`` from a thread."
msgstr ""
"請注意，某些平台（包括 FreeBSD <= 6.3 和 Cygwin）在從執行緒中使用 ``fork()`` "
"時存在已知問題。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5102
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.fork`` with no arguments."
msgstr "引發一個不附帶引數的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.fork``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5106
msgid ""
"If you use TLS sockets in an application calling ``fork()``, see the warning "
"in the :mod:`ssl` documentation."
msgstr ""
"如果你在呼叫 ``fork()`` 的應用程式中使用 TLS socket，請參閱 :mod:`ssl` 文件中"
"的警告。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5111 ../../library/os.rst:5157
msgid ""
"On macOS the use of this function is unsafe when mixed with using higher-"
"level system APIs, and that includes using :mod:`urllib.request`."
msgstr ""
"在 macOS 上，將此函式與較高階的系統 API 混用是不安全的，這也包括使"
"用 :mod:`urllib.request`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5114
msgid ""
"Calling ``fork()`` in a subinterpreter is no longer supported "
"(:exc:`RuntimeError` is raised)."
msgstr ""
"已不再支援在子直譯器中呼叫 ``fork()``\\ （會引發 :exc:`RuntimeError`）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5118
msgid ""
"If Python is able to detect that your process has multiple "
"threads, :func:`os.fork` now raises a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`."
msgstr ""
"如果 Python 能夠偵測到你的行程有多個執行緒，:func:`os.fork` 現在會引"
"發 :exc:`DeprecationWarning`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5122
msgid ""
"We chose to surface this as a warning, when detectable, to better inform "
"developers of a design problem that the POSIX platform specifically notes as "
"not supported. Even in code that *appears* to work, it has never been safe "
"to mix threading with :func:`os.fork` on POSIX platforms. The CPython "
"runtime itself has always made API calls that are not safe for use in the "
"child process when threads existed in the parent (such as ``malloc`` and "
"``free``)."
msgstr ""
"我們選擇在可偵測時以警告的形式呈現此問題，以便讓開發者更清楚地知道這是一個設"
"計上的問題，而 POSIX 平台也特別註明這種用法不受支援。即使是\\ *看似*\\ 能正常"
"運作的程式碼，在 POSIX 平台上將執行緒與 :func:`os.fork` 混用也從來都不安全。"
"當父行程中存在執行緒時，CPython runtime 本身一直都會進行一些在子行程中使用並"
"不安全的 API 呼叫（例如 ``malloc`` 與 ``free``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5131
msgid ""
"Users of macOS or users of libc or malloc implementations other than those "
"typically found in glibc to date are among those already more likely to "
"experience deadlocks running such code."
msgstr ""
"macOS 的使用者，以及所使用的 libc 或 malloc 實作不同於目前 glibc 中常見實作的"
"使用者，原本就屬於較容易在執行這類程式碼時遇到死鎖的族群。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5135
msgid ""
"See `this discussion on fork being incompatible with threads <https://"
"discuss.python.org/t/33555>`_ for technical details of why we're surfacing "
"this longstanding platform compatibility problem to developers."
msgstr ""
"關於我們為何要向開發者揭示這個長期存在的平台相容性問題，其技術細節請參閱\\ `"
"這篇關於 fork 與執行緒不相容的討論 <https://discuss.python.org/t/33555>`_。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5145
msgid ""
"Fork a child process, using a new pseudo-terminal as the child's controlling "
"terminal. Return a pair of ``(pid, fd)``, where *pid* is ``0`` in the child, "
"the new child's process id in the parent, and *fd* is the file descriptor of "
"the master end of the pseudo-terminal.  For a more portable approach, use "
"the :mod:`pty` module.  If an error occurs :exc:`OSError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Fork 出一個子行程，並使用新的偽終端作為子行程的控制終端機。回傳一對 ``(pid, "
"fd)``，其中 *pid* 在子行程中為 ``0``、在父行程中為新子行程的行程 ID，而 *fd* "
"是偽終端主端的檔案描述器。若需要更具可移植性的做法，請使用 :mod:`pty` 模組。"
"如果發生錯誤，會引發 :exc:`OSError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5151
msgid ""
"The returned file descriptor *fd* is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr "回傳的檔案描述器 *fd* 為\\ :ref:`不可繼承 <fd_inheritance>`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5153
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.forkpty`` with no arguments."
msgstr "引發一個不附帶引數的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.forkpty``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5160
msgid ""
"Calling ``forkpty()`` in a subinterpreter is no longer supported "
"(:exc:`RuntimeError` is raised)."
msgstr ""
"已不再支援在子直譯器中呼叫 ``forkpty()``\\ （會引發 :exc:`RuntimeError`）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5164
msgid ""
"If Python is able to detect that your process has multiple threads, this now "
"raises a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. See the longer explanation "
"on :func:`os.fork`."
msgstr ""
"如果 Python 能夠偵測到你的行程有多個執行緒，此函式現在會引"
"發 :exc:`DeprecationWarning`。請參閱 :func:`os.fork` 中更詳細的說明。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5169
msgid "The returned file descriptor is now made non-inheritable."
msgstr "回傳的檔案描述器現在會被設為不可繼承。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5181
msgid ""
"Send signal *sig* to the process *pid*.  Constants for the specific signals "
"available on the host platform are defined in the :mod:`signal` module."
msgstr ""
"將訊號 *sig* 傳送給行程 *pid*。主機平台上可用的各個訊號常數定義"
"於 :mod:`signal` 模組中。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5184
msgid ""
"Windows: The :const:`signal.CTRL_C_EVENT` "
"and :const:`signal.CTRL_BREAK_EVENT` signals are special signals which can "
"only be sent to console processes which share a common console window, e.g., "
"some subprocesses. Any other value for *sig* will cause the process to be "
"unconditionally killed by the TerminateProcess API, and the exit code will "
"be set to *sig*."
msgstr ""
"Windows：:const:`signal.CTRL_C_EVENT` 與 :const:`signal.CTRL_BREAK_EVENT` 訊"
"號是特殊訊號，只能傳送給共用同一個主控台視窗的主控台行程，例如某些子行程。"
"*sig* 為任何其他值時，都會使該行程被 TerminateProcess API 無條件終止，且結束"
"代碼會被設為 *sig*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5191
msgid "See also :func:`signal.pthread_kill`."
msgstr "另請參閱 :func:`signal.pthread_kill`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5193
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.kill`` with arguments "
"``pid``, ``sig``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``pid``、``sig`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.kill``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5207
msgid "Send the signal *sig* to the process group *pgid*."
msgstr "將訊號 *sig* 傳送給行程群組 *pgid*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5209
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.killpg`` with arguments "
"``pgid``, ``sig``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``pgid``、``sig`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.killpg``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5216
msgid ""
"Add *increment* to the process's \"niceness\".  Return the new niceness."
msgstr "將行程的「nice 值」(niceness) 加上 *increment*。回傳新的 nice 值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5223
msgid ""
"Return a file descriptor referring to the process *pid* with *flags* set. "
"This descriptor can be used to perform process management without races and "
"signals."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個參照行程 *pid* 並設定了 *flags* 的檔案描述器。此描述器可用於進行行程"
"管理，而不會有競爭條件與訊號的問題。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5227
msgid "See the :manpage:`pidfd_open(2)` man page for more details."
msgstr "更多細節請見 :manpage:`pidfd_open(2)` 使用手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5234
msgid ""
"This flag indicates that the file descriptor will be non-blocking. If the "
"process referred to by the file descriptor has not yet terminated, then an "
"attempt to wait on the file descriptor using :manpage:`waitid(2)` will "
"immediately return the error :const:`~errno.EAGAIN` rather than blocking."
msgstr ""
"此旗標表示該檔案描述器為非阻塞。如果該檔案描述器所參照的行程尚未終止，那麼嘗"
"試使用 :manpage:`waitid(2)` 等待該檔案描述器時，會立即回傳錯"
"誤 :const:`~errno.EAGAIN`，而不是阻塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5245
msgid ""
"Lock program segments into memory.  The value of *op* (defined in ``<sys/"
"lock.h>``) determines which segments are locked."
msgstr ""
"將程式區段鎖定在記憶體中。*op* 的值（定義於 ``<sys/lock.h>``）決定要鎖定哪些"
"區段。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5253
msgid ""
"Open a pipe to or from command *cmd*. The return value is an open file "
"object connected to the pipe, which can be read or written depending on "
"whether *mode* is ``'r'`` (default) or ``'w'``. The *buffering* argument "
"have the same meaning as the corresponding argument to the built-"
"in :func:`open` function. The returned file object reads or writes text "
"strings rather than bytes."
msgstr ""
"開啟一個通往命令 *cmd* 或來自命令 *cmd* 的管道。回傳值是一個連接到該管道的已"
"開啟檔案物件，依據 *mode* 是 ``'r'``\\ （預設）或 ``'w'``，可對其進行讀取或寫"
"入。*buffering* 引數的意義與內建函式 :func:`open` 中對應的引數相同。回傳的檔"
"案物件讀寫的是文字字串而非位元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5261
msgid ""
"The ``close`` method returns :const:`None` if the subprocess exited "
"successfully, or the subprocess's return code if there was an error. On "
"POSIX systems, if the return code is positive it represents the return value "
"of the process left-shifted by one byte.  If the return code is negative, "
"the process was terminated by the signal given by the negated value of the "
"return code.  (For example, the return value might be ``- signal.SIGKILL`` "
"if the subprocess was killed.)  On Windows systems, the return value "
"contains the signed integer return code from the child process."
msgstr ""
"如果子行程成功結束，``close`` 方法會回傳 :const:`None`；如果發生錯誤，則回傳"
"子行程的回傳碼。在 POSIX 系統上，如果回傳碼為正數，它代表行程的回傳值左移一個"
"位元組。如果回傳碼為負數，代表行程被訊號終止，該訊號即為回傳碼取負值。（例"
"如，若子行程被強制終止，回傳值可能是 ``- signal.SIGKILL``。）在 Windows 系統"
"上，回傳值包含子行程的有號整數回傳碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5271
msgid ""
"On Unix, :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` can be used to convert the ``close`` "
"method result (exit status) into an exit code if it is not ``None``. On "
"Windows, the ``close`` method result is directly the exit code (or ``None``)."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，若 ``close`` 方法的結果（結束狀態）不是 ``None``，可以使"
"用 :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` 將其轉換為結束代碼。在 Windows 上，"
"``close`` 方法的結果直接就是結束代碼（或 ``None``）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5276
msgid ""
"This is implemented using :class:`subprocess.Popen`; see that class's "
"documentation for more powerful ways to manage and communicate with "
"subprocesses."
msgstr ""
"此函式是使用 :class:`subprocess.Popen` 實作的；若需要更強大的方式來管理子行程"
"並與之溝通，請參閱該類別的文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5283
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Python UTF-8 Mode <utf8-mode>` affects encodings used for *cmd* "
"and pipe contents."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Python UTF-8 模式 <utf8-mode>`\\ 會影響 *cmd* 與管道內容所使用的編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5286
msgid ""
":func:`popen` is a simple wrapper around :class:`subprocess.Popen`. "
"Use :class:`subprocess.Popen` or :func:`subprocess.run` to control options "
"like encodings."
msgstr ""
":func:`popen` 是 :class:`subprocess.Popen` 的簡單包裝函式。若要控制編碼等選"
"項，請使用 :class:`subprocess.Popen` 或 :func:`subprocess.run`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5290 ../../library/os.rst:5519
msgid "The :mod:`subprocess` module is recommended instead."
msgstr "建議改用 :mod:`subprocess` 模組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5298
msgid "Wraps the :c:func:`!posix_spawn` C library API for use from Python."
msgstr "包裝 C 函式庫 API :c:func:`!posix_spawn` 以供 Python 使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5300
msgid ""
"Most users should use :func:`subprocess.run` instead of :func:`posix_spawn`."
msgstr "大多數使用者應該使用 :func:`subprocess.run` 而非 :func:`posix_spawn`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5302
msgid ""
"The positional-only arguments *path*, *args*, and *env* are similar "
"to :func:`execve`. *env* is allowed to be ``None``, in which case current "
"process' environment is used."
msgstr ""
"僅限位置引數 *path*、*args* 與 *env* 和 :func:`execve` 的對應引數類似。*env* "
"可以是 ``None``，此時會使用目前行程的環境。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5306
msgid ""
"The *path* parameter is the path to the executable file.  The *path* should "
"contain a directory.  Use :func:`posix_spawnp` to pass an executable file "
"without directory."
msgstr ""
"*path* 參數是可執行檔的路徑。*path* 應包含目錄。若要傳入不含目錄的可執行檔，"
"請使用 :func:`posix_spawnp`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5310
msgid ""
"The *file_actions* argument may be a sequence of tuples describing actions "
"to take on specific file descriptors in the child process between the C "
"library implementation's :c:func:`fork` and :c:func:`exec` steps. The first "
"item in each tuple must be one of the three type indicator listed below "
"describing the remaining tuple elements:"
msgstr ""
"*file_actions* 引數可以是一個由元組組成的序列，描述在 C 函式庫實作"
"的 :c:func:`fork` 與 :c:func:`exec` 步驟之間，要在子行程中對特定檔案描述器執"
"行的動作。每個元組的第一個項目必須是下列三種型別指示符之一，用來描述該元組其"
"餘的元素："

#: ../../library/os.rst:5318
msgid "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_OPEN``, *fd*, *path*, *flags*, *mode*)"
msgstr "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_OPEN``, *fd*, *path*, *flags*, *mode*)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5320
msgid "Performs ``os.dup2(os.open(path, flags, mode), fd)``."
msgstr "執行 ``os.dup2(os.open(path, flags, mode), fd)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5324
msgid "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSE``, *fd*)"
msgstr "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSE``, *fd*)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5326
msgid "Performs ``os.close(fd)``."
msgstr "執行 ``os.close(fd)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5330
msgid "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_DUP2``, *fd*, *new_fd*)"
msgstr "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_DUP2``, *fd*, *new_fd*)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5332
msgid "Performs ``os.dup2(fd, new_fd)``."
msgstr "執行 ``os.dup2(fd, new_fd)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5336
msgid "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM``, *fd*)"
msgstr "(``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM``, *fd*)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5338
msgid "Performs ``os.closerange(fd, INF)``."
msgstr "執行 ``os.closerange(fd, INF)``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5340
msgid ""
"These tuples correspond to the C library :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen`, :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose`, :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2`, and :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np` API calls used to prepare for "
"the :c:func:`!posix_spawn` call itself."
msgstr ""
"這些元組對應到 C 函式庫的 :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addopen`、:c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addclose`、:c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2` 與 :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np` API 呼叫，這些呼叫用於為 :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn` 呼叫本身做準備。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5347
msgid ""
"The *setpgroup* argument will set the process group of the child to the "
"value specified. If the value specified is 0, the child's process group ID "
"will be made the same as its process ID. If the value of *setpgroup* is not "
"set, the child will inherit the parent's process group ID. This argument "
"corresponds to the C library :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP` flag."
msgstr ""
"*setpgroup* 引數會將子行程的行程群組設為指定的值。如果指定的值為 0，子行程的"
"行程群組 ID 會與其行程 ID 相同。如果未設定 *setpgroup* 的值，子行程會繼承父行"
"程的行程群組 ID。此引數對應到 C 函式庫的 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP` 旗"
"標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5353
msgid ""
"If the *resetids* argument is ``True`` it will reset the effective UID and "
"GID of the child to the real UID and GID of the parent process. If the "
"argument is ``False``, then the child retains the effective UID and GID of "
"the parent. In either case, if the set-user-ID and set-group-ID permission "
"bits are enabled on the executable file, their effect will override the "
"setting of the effective UID and GID. This argument corresponds to the C "
"library :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_RESETIDS` flag."
msgstr ""
"如果 *resetids* 引數為 ``True``，它會將子行程的有效 UID 與 GID 重設為父行程的"
"真實 UID 與 GID。如果該引數為 ``False``，子行程會保留父行程的有效 UID 與 "
"GID。無論是哪種情況，如果可執行檔上啟用了 set-user-ID 與 set-group-ID 權限位"
"元，它們的效果都會覆寫有效 UID 與 GID 的設定。此引數對應到 C 函式庫"
"的 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_RESETIDS` 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5361
msgid ""
"If the *setsid* argument is ``True``, it will create a new session ID for "
"``posix_spawn``. *setsid* requires :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID` "
"or :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID_NP` flag. "
"Otherwise, :exc:`NotImplementedError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"如果 *setsid* 引數為 ``True``，它會為 ``posix_spawn`` 建立新的 session ID。"
"*setsid* 需要 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID` 或 :c:macro:`!"
"POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID_NP` 旗標，否則會引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5366
msgid ""
"The *setsigmask* argument will set the signal mask to the signal set "
"specified. If the parameter is not used, then the child inherits the "
"parent's signal mask. This argument corresponds to the C library :c:macro:`!"
"POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK` flag."
msgstr ""
"*setsigmask* 引數會將訊號遮罩設為指定的訊號集合。如果未使用此參數，子行程會繼"
"承父行程的訊號遮罩。此引數對應到 C 函式庫的 :c:macro:`!"
"POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK` 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5371
msgid ""
"The *setsigdef* argument will reset the disposition of all signals in the "
"set specified. This argument corresponds to the C library :c:macro:`!"
"POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF` flag."
msgstr ""
"*setsigdef* 引數會將指定集合中所有訊號的處置方式重設為預設值。此引數對應到 C "
"函式庫的 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF` 旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5375
msgid ""
"The *scheduler* argument must be a tuple containing the (optional) scheduler "
"policy and an instance of :class:`sched_param` with the scheduler "
"parameters. A value of ``None`` in the place of the scheduler policy "
"indicates that is not being provided. This argument is a combination of the "
"C library :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDPARAM` and :c:macro:`!"
"POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDULER` flags."
msgstr ""
"*scheduler* 引數必須是一個元組，包含（可選的）排程器策略，以及一個帶有排程器"
"參數的 :class:`sched_param` 實例。在排程器策略的位置上放 ``None`` 表示未提供"
"該策略。此引數是 C 函式庫 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDPARAM` "
"與 :c:macro:`!POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDULER` 旗標的組合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5382 ../../library/os.rst:5403
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.posix_spawn`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``argv``, ``env``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``argv``、``env`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.posix_spawn``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5386
msgid ""
"*env* parameter accepts ``None``. ``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM`` is available "
"on platforms where :c:func:`!posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np` "
"exists."
msgstr ""
"*env* 參數接受 ``None``。在有 :c:func:`!"
"posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np` 的平台上可以使用 "
"``os.POSIX_SPAWN_CLOSEFROM``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5397
msgid "Wraps the :c:func:`!posix_spawnp` C library API for use from Python."
msgstr "包裝 C 函式庫 API :c:func:`!posix_spawnp` 以供 Python 使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5399
msgid ""
"Similar to :func:`posix_spawn` except that the system searches for the "
"*executable* file in the list of directories specified by the :envvar:`PATH` "
"environment variable (in the same way as for ``execvp(3)``)."
msgstr ""
"與 :func:`posix_spawn` 類似，差別在於系統會在 :envvar:`PATH` 環境變數所指定的"
"目錄串列中搜尋 *executable* 檔案（方式與 ``execvp(3)`` 相同）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5409
msgid "See :func:`posix_spawn` documentation."
msgstr "見 :func:`posix_spawn` 文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5415
msgid ""
"Register callables to be executed when a new child process is forked "
"using :func:`os.fork` or similar process cloning APIs. The parameters are "
"optional and keyword-only. Each specifies a different call point."
msgstr ""
"註冊可呼叫物件，在使用 :func:`os.fork` 或類似的行程複製 API fork 出新的子行程"
"時執行。這些參數皆為可選且僅限關鍵字。每個參數各自指定一個不同的呼叫時機點。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5420
msgid "*before* is a function called before forking a child process."
msgstr "*before* 是在 fork 子行程之前呼叫的函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5421
msgid ""
"*after_in_parent* is a function called from the parent process after forking "
"a child process."
msgstr "*after_in_parent* 是在 fork 子行程之後，從父行程呼叫的函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5423
msgid "*after_in_child* is a function called from the child process."
msgstr "*after_in_child* 是從子行程呼叫的函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5425
msgid ""
"These calls are only made if control is expected to return to the Python "
"interpreter.  A typical :mod:`subprocess` launch will not trigger them as "
"the child is not going to re-enter the interpreter."
msgstr ""
"只有在預期控制權會回到 Python 直譯器時，才會進行這些呼叫。典型"
"的 :mod:`subprocess` 啟動不會觸發它們，因為子行程不會再進入直譯器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5429
msgid ""
"Functions registered for execution before forking are called in reverse "
"registration order.  Functions registered for execution after forking "
"(either in the parent or in the child) are called in registration order."
msgstr ""
"註冊在 fork 之前執行的函式會以與註冊順序相反的順序呼叫。註冊在 fork 之後執行"
"的函式（無論是在父行程或子行程中）會依註冊順序呼叫。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5434
msgid ""
"Note that :c:func:`fork` calls made by third-party C code may not call those "
"functions, unless it explicitly "
"calls :c:func:`PyOS_BeforeFork`, :c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Parent` "
"and :c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Child`."
msgstr ""
"請注意，第三方 C 程式碼所進行的 :c:func:`fork` 呼叫可能不會呼叫這些函式，除非"
"它明確呼叫了 :c:func:`PyOS_BeforeFork`、:c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Parent` "
"與 :c:func:`PyOS_AfterFork_Child`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5438
msgid "There is no way to unregister a function."
msgstr "沒有辦法取消註冊函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5454
msgid "Execute the program *file* in a new process."
msgstr "在新行程中執行程式 *file*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5456
msgid ""
"(Note that the :mod:`subprocess` module provides more powerful facilities "
"for spawning new processes and retrieving their results; using that module "
"is preferable to using these functions.  Check especially "
"the :ref:`subprocess-replacements` section.)"
msgstr ""
"（請注意，:mod:`subprocess` 模組提供了更強大的機制來衍生新行程並取得其結果；"
"使用該模組會比使用這些函式更好。特別請參閱\\ :ref:`subprocess-"
"replacements`\\ 章節。）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5461
msgid ""
"If *mode* is :const:`P_NOWAIT`, this function returns the process id of the "
"new process; if *mode* is :const:`P_WAIT`, returns the process's exit code "
"if it exits normally, or ``-signal``, where *signal* is the signal that "
"killed the process.  On Windows, the process id will actually be the process "
"handle, so can be used with the :func:`waitpid` function."
msgstr ""
"如果 *mode* 為 :const:`P_NOWAIT`，此函式會回傳新行程的行程 ID；如果 *mode* "
"為 :const:`P_WAIT`，若行程正常結束則回傳其結束代碼，否則回傳 ``-signal``，其"
"中 *signal* 是終止該行程的訊號。在 Windows 上，行程 ID 實際上會是行程控制代"
"碼，因此可以與 :func:`waitpid` 函式一起使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5467
msgid ""
"Note on VxWorks, this function doesn't return ``-signal`` when the new "
"process is killed. Instead it raises OSError exception."
msgstr ""
"請注意，在 VxWorks 上，當新行程被終止時，此函式不會回傳 ``-signal``，而是會引"
"發 OSError 例外。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5470
msgid ""
"The \"l\" and \"v\" variants of the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` functions "
"differ in how command-line arguments are passed.  The \"l\" variants are "
"perhaps the easiest to work with if the number of parameters is fixed when "
"the code is written; the individual parameters simply become additional "
"parameters to the :func:`!spawnl\\*` functions.  The \"v\" variants are good "
"when the number of parameters is variable, with the arguments being passed "
"in a list or tuple as the *args* parameter.  In either case, the arguments "
"to the child process must start with the name of the command being run."
msgstr ""
":func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式的「l」與「v」變體在命令列引數的傳遞方式上有所"
"不同。如果在撰寫程式碼時參數的數量是固定的，「l」變體大概是最容易使用的；各個"
"參數只要成為 :func:`!spawnl\\*` 函式的額外參數即可。「v」變體則適合參數數量不"
"固定的情況，引數會以串列或元組的形式作為 *args* 參數傳入。無論哪種情況，傳給"
"子行程的引數都必須以所執行的命令名稱開頭。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5479
msgid ""
"The variants which include a second \"p\" near the end "
"(:func:`spawnlp`, :func:`spawnlpe`, :func:`spawnvp`, and :func:`spawnvpe`) "
"will use the :envvar:`PATH` environment variable to locate the program "
"*file*.  When the environment is being replaced (using one of "
"the :func:`spawn\\*e <spawnl>` variants, discussed in the next paragraph), "
"the new environment is used as the source of the :envvar:`PATH` variable.  "
"The other variants, :func:`spawnl`, :func:`spawnle`, :func:`spawnv`, "
"and :func:`spawnve`, will not use the :envvar:`PATH` variable to locate the "
"executable; *file* must contain an appropriate absolute or relative path."
msgstr ""
"名稱結尾附近包含第二個「p」的變體"
"（:func:`spawnlp`、:func:`spawnlpe`、:func:`spawnvp` 與 :func:`spawnvpe`）會"
"使用 :envvar:`PATH` 環境變數來尋找程式 *file*。當環境被取代時（使用下一段所討"
"論的 :func:`spawn\\*e <spawnl>` 變體之一），新環境會被用作 :envvar:`PATH` 變"
"數的來源。其他變體 :func:`spawnl`、:func:`spawnle`、:func:`spawnv` "
"與 :func:`spawnve` 不會使用 :envvar:`PATH` 變數來尋找可執行檔；*file* 必須包"
"含適當的絕對或相對路徑。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5489
msgid ""
"For :func:`spawnle`, :func:`spawnlpe`, :func:`spawnve`, and :func:`spawnvpe` "
"(note that these all end in \"e\"), the *env* parameter must be a mapping "
"which is used to define the environment variables for the new process (they "
"are used instead of the current process' environment); the "
"functions :func:`spawnl`, :func:`spawnlp`, :func:`spawnv`, "
"and :func:`spawnvp` all cause the new process to inherit the environment of "
"the current process.  Note that keys and values in the *env* dictionary must "
"be strings; invalid keys or values will cause the function to fail, with a "
"return value of ``127``."
msgstr ""
"對於 :func:`spawnle`、:func:`spawnlpe`、:func:`spawnve` "
"與 :func:`spawnvpe`\\ （請注意這些函式的名稱都以「e」結尾），*env* 參數必須是"
"一個對映，用來定義新行程的環境變數（它們會用來代替目前行程的環境）；"
"而 :func:`spawnl`、:func:`spawnlp`、:func:`spawnv` 與 :func:`spawnvp` 函式都"
"會讓新行程繼承目前行程的環境。請注意，*env* 字典中的鍵與值都必須是字串；無效"
"的鍵或值會導致函式失敗，並回傳 ``127``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5498
msgid ""
"As an example, the following calls to :func:`spawnlp` and :func:`spawnvpe` "
"are equivalent::"
msgstr ""
"舉例來說，以下對 :func:`spawnlp` 與 :func:`spawnvpe` 的呼叫是等價的： ::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5501
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"os.spawnlp(os.P_WAIT, 'cp', 'cp', 'index.html', '/dev/null')\n"
"\n"
"L = ['cp', 'index.html', '/dev/null']\n"
"os.spawnvpe(os.P_WAIT, 'cp', L, os.environ)"
msgstr ""
"import os\n"
"os.spawnlp(os.P_WAIT, 'cp', 'cp', 'index.html', '/dev/null')\n"
"\n"
"L = ['cp', 'index.html', '/dev/null']\n"
"os.spawnvpe(os.P_WAIT, 'cp', L, os.environ)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5507
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.spawn`` with arguments "
"``mode``, ``file``, ``args``, ``env``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``mode``、``file``、``args``、``env`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``os.spawn``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5511
msgid ""
":func:`spawnlp`, :func:`spawnlpe`, :func:`spawnvp` and :func:`spawnvpe` are "
"not available on Windows.  :func:`spawnle` and :func:`spawnve` are not "
"thread-safe on Windows; we advise you to use the :mod:`subprocess` module "
"instead."
msgstr ""
":func:`spawnlp`、:func:`spawnlpe`、:func:`spawnvp` 與 :func:`spawnvpe` 在 "
"Windows 上無法使用。:func:`spawnle` 與 :func:`spawnve` 在 Windows 上不是執行"
"緒安全的；我們建議你改用 :mod:`subprocess` 模組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5526
msgid ""
"Possible values for the *mode* parameter to the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` "
"family of functions.  If either of these values is given, "
"the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` functions will return as soon as the new "
"process has been created, with the process id as the return value."
msgstr ""
":func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 系列函式的 *mode* 參數的可能值。如果給定這兩個值中"
"的任一個，:func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式會在新行程建立後立即回傳，並以行程 "
"ID 作為回傳值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5536
msgid ""
"Possible value for the *mode* parameter to the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` "
"family of functions.  If this is given as *mode*, the :func:`spawn\\* "
"<spawnl>` functions will not return until the new process has run to "
"completion and will return the exit code of the process the run is "
"successful, or ``-signal`` if a signal kills the process."
msgstr ""
":func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 系列函式的 *mode* 參數的可能值。如果將此值作為 "
"*mode* 傳入，:func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式要等到新行程執行完畢才會回傳；若執"
"行成功則回傳該行程的結束代碼，若行程被訊號終止則回傳 ``-signal``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5548
msgid ""
"Possible values for the *mode* parameter to the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` "
"family of functions.  These are less portable than those listed "
"above. :const:`P_DETACH` is similar to :const:`P_NOWAIT`, but the new "
"process is detached from the console of the calling process. "
"If :const:`P_OVERLAY` is used, the current process will be replaced; "
"the :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` function will not return."
msgstr ""
":func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 系列函式的 *mode* 參數的可能值。這些值的可移植性比"
"上面列出的值差。:const:`P_DETACH` 與 :const:`P_NOWAIT` 類似，但新行程會與呼叫"
"端行程的主控台分離。如果使用 :const:`P_OVERLAY`，目前的行程將被取"
"代；:func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式不會回傳。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5559
msgid "Start a file with its associated application."
msgstr "以檔案所關聯的應用程式來開啟該檔案。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5561
msgid ""
"When *operation* is not specified, this acts like double-clicking the file "
"in Windows Explorer, or giving the file name as an argument to "
"the :program:`start` command from the interactive command shell: the file is "
"opened with whatever application (if any) its extension is associated."
msgstr ""
"當未指定 *operation* 時，此函式的行為就像在 Windows 檔案總管 (Windows "
"Explorer) 中按兩下該檔案，或在互動式命令 shell 中將檔案名稱作"
"為 :program:`start` 命令的引數：檔案會以其副檔名所關聯的應用程式（如果有的"
"話）開啟。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5566
msgid ""
"When another *operation* is given, it must be a \"command verb\" that "
"specifies what should be done with the file. Common verbs documented by "
"Microsoft are ``'open'``, ``'print'`` and  ``'edit'`` (to be used on files) "
"as well as ``'explore'`` and ``'find'`` (to be used on directories)."
msgstr ""
"當給定其他 *operation* 時，它必須是一個「命令動詞」，用來指定要對該檔案做什"
"麼。Microsoft 文件中記載的常見動詞有 ``'open'``、``'print'`` 與 ``'edit'``\\ "
"（用於檔案），以及 ``'explore'`` 與 ``'find'``\\ （用於目錄）。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5571
msgid ""
"When launching an application, specify *arguments* to be passed as a single "
"string. This argument may have no effect when using this function to launch "
"a document."
msgstr ""
"啟動應用程式時，請將要傳入的 *arguments* 指定為單一字串。使用此函式開啟文件"
"時，此引數可能不會有任何效果。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5575
msgid ""
"The default working directory is inherited, but may be overridden by the "
"*cwd* argument. This should be an absolute path. A relative *path* will be "
"resolved against this argument."
msgstr ""
"預設的工作目錄是繼承而來的，但可以用 *cwd* 引數覆寫。此引數應為絕對路徑。相對"
"的 *path* 會以此引數為基準來解析。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5579
msgid ""
"Use *show_cmd* to override the default window style. Whether this has any "
"effect will depend on the application being launched. Values are integers as "
"supported by the Win32 :c:func:`!ShellExecute` function."
msgstr ""
"使用 *show_cmd* 來覆寫預設的視窗樣式。這是否有任何效果取決於所啟動的應用程"
"式。其值為 Win32 :c:func:`!ShellExecute` 函式所支援的整數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5583
msgid ""
":func:`startfile` returns as soon as the associated application is launched. "
"There is no option to wait for the application to close, and no way to "
"retrieve the application's exit status.  The *path* parameter is relative to "
"the current directory or *cwd*.  If you want to use an absolute path, make "
"sure the first character is not a slash (``'/'``)  Use :mod:`pathlib` or "
"the :func:`os.path.normpath` function to ensure that paths are properly "
"encoded for Win32."
msgstr ""
":func:`startfile` 會在關聯的應用程式啟動後立即回傳。沒有選項可以等待應用程式"
"關閉，也沒有辦法取得應用程式的結束狀態。*path* 參數是相對於目前目錄或 *cwd* "
"的路徑。如果你想使用絕對路徑，請確保第一個字元不是斜線 (``'/'``)。請使"
"用 :mod:`pathlib` 或 :func:`os.path.normpath` 函式來確保路徑已針對 Win32 正確"
"編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5591
msgid ""
"To reduce interpreter startup overhead, the Win32 :c:func:`!ShellExecute` "
"function is not resolved until this function is first called.  If the "
"function cannot be resolved, :exc:`NotImplementedError` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"為了減少直譯器啟動的額外負擔，Win32 :c:func:`!ShellExecute` 函式要等到此函式"
"第一次被呼叫時才會被解析。如果無法解析該函式，將引"
"發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5595
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.startfile`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``operation``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``operation`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``os.startfile``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5597
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.startfile/2`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``operation``, ``arguments``, ``cwd``, ``show_cmd``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``path``、``operation``、``arguments``、``cwd``、"
"``show_cmd`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.startfile/2``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5601
msgid ""
"Added the *arguments*, *cwd* and *show_cmd* arguments, and the "
"``os.startfile/2`` audit event."
msgstr ""
"新增 *arguments*、*cwd* 與 *show_cmd* 引數，以及 ``os.startfile/2`` 稽核事"
"件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5608
msgid ""
"Execute the command (a string) in a subshell.  This is implemented by "
"calling the Standard C function :c:func:`system`, and has the same "
"limitations. Changes to :data:`sys.stdin`, etc. are not reflected in the "
"environment of the executed command. If *command* generates any output, it "
"will be sent to the interpreter standard output stream. The C standard does "
"not specify the meaning of the return value of the C function, so the return "
"value of the Python function is system-dependent."
msgstr ""
"在子 shell 中執行命令（一個字串）。此函式是透過呼叫標準 C 函"
"式 :c:func:`system` 來實作的，並具有相同的限制。對 :data:`sys.stdin` 等的變更"
"不會反映在所執行命令的環境中。如果 *command* 產生任何輸出，它會被送到直譯器的"
"標準輸出串流。C 標準並未規定 C 函式回傳值的意義，因此 Python 函式的回傳值取決"
"於系統。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5616
msgid ""
"On Unix, the return value is the exit status of the process encoded in the "
"format specified for :func:`wait`."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，回傳值是該行程的結束狀態，並以 :func:`wait` 所指定的格式編碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5619
msgid ""
"On Windows, the return value is that returned by the system shell after "
"running *command*.  The shell is given by the Windows environment "
"variable :envvar:`COMSPEC`: it is usually :program:`cmd.exe`, which returns "
"the exit status of the command run; on systems using a non-native shell, "
"consult your shell documentation."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，回傳值是系統 shell 執行 *command* 後所回傳的值。shell 由 "
"Windows 環境變數 :envvar:`COMSPEC` 指定：它通常是 :program:`cmd.exe`，會回傳"
"所執行命令的結束狀態；在使用非原生 shell 的系統上，請參閱你的 shell 文件。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5625
msgid ""
"The :mod:`subprocess` module provides more powerful facilities for spawning "
"new processes and retrieving their results; using that module is recommended "
"to using this function.  See the :ref:`subprocess-replacements` section in "
"the :mod:`subprocess` documentation for some helpful recipes."
msgstr ""
":mod:`subprocess` 模組提供了更強大的機制來衍生新行程並取得其結果；建議使用該"
"模組而非此函式。請參閱 :mod:`subprocess` 文件中的\\ :ref:`subprocess-"
"replacements`\\ 章節，以取得一些實用的做法。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5630
msgid ""
"On Unix, :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` can be used to convert the result "
"(exit status) into an exit code. On Windows, the result is directly the exit "
"code."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，可以使用 :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` 將結果（結束狀態）轉換為"
"結束代碼。在 Windows 上，結果直接就是結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5634
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.system`` with argument "
"``command``."
msgstr ""
"引發一個附帶引數 ``command`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``os.system``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5641
msgid ""
"Returns the current global process times. The return value is an object with "
"five attributes:"
msgstr "回傳目前的全域行程時間。回傳值是一個具有五個屬性的物件："

#: ../../library/os.rst:5644
msgid ":attr:`!user` - user time"
msgstr ":attr:`!user` - 使用者時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5645
msgid ":attr:`!system` - system time"
msgstr ":attr:`!system` - 系統時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5646
msgid ":attr:`!children_user` - user time of all child processes"
msgstr ":attr:`!children_user` - 所有子行程的使用者時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5647
msgid ":attr:`!children_system` - system time of all child processes"
msgstr ":attr:`!children_system` - 所有子行程的系統時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5648
msgid ":attr:`!elapsed` - elapsed real time since a fixed point in the past"
msgstr ":attr:`!elapsed` - 自過去某個固定時間點起經過的實際時間"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5650
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility, this object also behaves like a five-tuple "
"containing :attr:`!user`, :attr:`!system`, :attr:`!children_user`, :attr:`!"
"children_system`, and :attr:`!elapsed` in that order."
msgstr ""
"為了向後相容，此物件的行為也像一個依序包含 :attr:`!user`、:attr:`!"
"system`、:attr:`!children_user`、:attr:`!children_system` 與 :attr:`!"
"elapsed` 的五元組。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5654
msgid ""
"See the Unix manual page :manpage:`times(2)` and `times(3) <https://"
"man.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?time(3)>`_ manual page on Unix or `the "
"GetProcessTimes MSDN <https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/win32/api/"
"processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-getprocesstimes>`_ on Windows. On "
"Windows, only :attr:`!user` and :attr:`!system` are known; the other "
"attributes are zero."
msgstr ""
"請參閱 Unix 使用手冊 :manpage:`times(2)` 與 Unix 上的 `times(3) <https://"
"man.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?time(3)>`_ 使用手冊，或 Windows 上的 "
"`GetProcessTimes MSDN 文件 <https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/win32/api/"
"processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-getprocesstimes>`_。在 Windows 上，只"
"有 :attr:`!user` 與 :attr:`!system` 是已知的；其他屬性皆為零。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5668
msgid ""
"Wait for completion of a child process, and return a tuple containing its "
"pid and exit status indication: a 16-bit number, whose low byte is the "
"signal number that killed the process, and whose high byte is the exit "
"status (if the signal number is zero); the high bit of the low byte is set "
"if a core file was produced."
msgstr ""
"等待子行程完成，並回傳一個包含其 pid 與結束狀態指示的元組：結束狀態指示是一"
"個 16 位元的數字，其低位元組是終止該行程的訊號編號，高位元組則是結束狀態（如"
"果訊號編號為零）；如果產生了核心檔案 (core file)，低位元組的最高位元會被設"
"定。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5674
msgid ""
"If there are no children that could be waited for, :exc:`ChildProcessError` "
"is raised."
msgstr "如果沒有可以等待的子行程，會引發 :exc:`ChildProcessError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5677 ../../library/os.rst:5752
msgid ""
":func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` can be used to convert the exit status into "
"an exit code."
msgstr "可以使用 :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` 將結束狀態轉換為結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5684
msgid ""
"The other :func:`!wait*` functions documented below can be used to wait for "
"the completion of a specific child process and have more "
"options. :func:`waitpid` is the only one also available on Windows."
msgstr ""
"下面記載的其他 :func:`!wait*` 函式可用來等待特定子行程完成，並且有更多選"
"項。:func:`waitpid` 是其中唯一在 Windows 上也可以使用的函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5691
msgid "Wait for the completion of a child process."
msgstr "等待子行程完成。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5693
msgid ""
"*idtype* can be :data:`P_PID`, :data:`P_PGID`, :data:`P_ALL`, or (on "
"Linux) :data:`P_PIDFD`. The interpretation of *id* depends on it; see their "
"individual descriptions."
msgstr ""
"*idtype* 可以是 :data:`P_PID`、:data:`P_PGID`、:data:`P_ALL` 或（在 Linux "
"上）\\ :data:`P_PIDFD`。*id* 的解讀方式取決於它；請參閱各自的說明。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5696
msgid ""
"*options* is an OR combination of flags.  At least one "
"of :data:`WEXITED`, :data:`WSTOPPED` or :data:`WCONTINUED` is "
"required; :data:`WNOHANG` and :data:`WNOWAIT` are additional optional flags."
msgstr ""
"*options* 是旗標的 OR 組合。至少需要 :data:`WEXITED`、:data:`WSTOPPED` "
"或 :data:`WCONTINUED` 其中之一；:data:`WNOHANG` 與 :data:`WNOWAIT` 則是額外的"
"可選旗標。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5700
msgid ""
"The return value is an object representing the data contained in "
"the :c:type:`siginfo_t` structure with the following attributes:"
msgstr ""
"回傳值是一個物件，代表 :c:type:`siginfo_t` 結構中所包含的資料，並具有以下屬"
"性："

#: ../../library/os.rst:5703
msgid ":attr:`!si_pid` (process ID)"
msgstr ":attr:`!si_pid`\\ （行程 ID）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5704
msgid ":attr:`!si_uid` (real user ID of the child)"
msgstr ":attr:`!si_uid`\\ （子行程的真實使用者 ID）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5705
msgid ":attr:`!si_signo` (always :const:`~signal.SIGCHLD`)"
msgstr ":attr:`!si_signo`\\ （一律為 :const:`~signal.SIGCHLD`）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5706
msgid ""
":attr:`!si_status` (the exit status or signal number, depending on :attr:`!"
"si_code`)"
msgstr ":attr:`!si_status`\\ （結束狀態或訊號編號，取決於 :attr:`!si_code`）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5707
msgid ":attr:`!si_code` (see :data:`CLD_EXITED` for possible values)"
msgstr ":attr:`!si_code`\\ （可能的值請參閱 :data:`CLD_EXITED`）"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5709
msgid ""
"If :data:`WNOHANG` is specified and there are no matching children in the "
"requested state, ``None`` is returned. Otherwise, if there are no matching "
"children that could be waited for, :exc:`ChildProcessError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 :data:`WNOHANG`，且在所要求的狀態中沒有相符的子行程，則回傳 "
"``None``。否則，如果沒有可以等待的相符子行程，會引"
"發 :exc:`ChildProcessError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5718
msgid "This function is now available on macOS as well."
msgstr "此函式現在在 macOS 上也可以使用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5724
msgid "The details of this function differ on Unix and Windows."
msgstr "此函式的細節在 Unix 與 Windows 上有所不同。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5726
msgid ""
"On Unix: Wait for completion of a child process given by process id *pid*, "
"and return a tuple containing its process id and exit status indication "
"(encoded as for :func:`wait`).  The semantics of the call are affected by "
"the value of the integer *options*, which should be ``0`` for normal "
"operation."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上：等待由行程 ID *pid* 所指定的子行程完成，並回傳一個包含其行程 ID "
"與結束狀態指示（編碼方式同 :func:`wait`）的元組。此呼叫的語意會受到整數 "
"*options* 的值影響，一般操作時應為 ``0``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5731
msgid ""
"If *pid* is greater than ``0``, :func:`waitpid` requests status information "
"for that specific process.  If *pid* is ``0``, the request is for the status "
"of any child in the process group of the current process.  If *pid* is "
"``-1``, the request pertains to any child of the current process.  If *pid* "
"is less than ``-1``, status is requested for any process in the process "
"group ``-pid`` (the absolute value of *pid*)."
msgstr ""
"如果 *pid* 大於 ``0``，:func:`waitpid` 會請求該特定行程的狀態資訊。如果 "
"*pid* 為 ``0``，則請求目前行程所屬行程群組中任何子行程的狀態。如果 *pid* 為 "
"``-1``，則請求目前行程的任何子行程。如果 *pid* 小於 ``-1``，則請求行程群組 "
"``-pid``\\ （即 *pid* 的絕對值）中任何行程的狀態。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5738
msgid ""
"*options* is an OR combination of flags.  If it contains :data:`WNOHANG` and "
"there are no matching children in the requested state, ``(0, 0)`` is "
"returned.  Otherwise, if there are no matching children that could be waited "
"for, :exc:`ChildProcessError` is raised.  Other options that can be used "
"are :data:`WUNTRACED` and :data:`WCONTINUED`."
msgstr ""
"*options* 是旗標的 OR 組合。如果其中包含 :data:`WNOHANG`，且在所要求的狀態中"
"沒有相符的子行程，則回傳 ``(0, 0)``。否則，如果沒有可以等待的相符子行程，會引"
"發 :exc:`ChildProcessError`。其他可以使用的選項有 :data:`WUNTRACED` "
"與 :data:`WCONTINUED`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5744
msgid ""
"On Windows: Wait for completion of a process given by process handle *pid*, "
"and return a tuple containing *pid*, and its exit status shifted left by 8 "
"bits (shifting makes cross-platform use of the function easier). A *pid* "
"less than or equal to ``0`` has no special meaning on Windows, and raises an "
"exception. The value of integer *options* has no effect. *pid* can refer to "
"any process whose id is known, not necessarily a child process. "
"The :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` functions called with :const:`P_NOWAIT` return "
"suitable process handles."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上：等待由行程控制代碼 *pid* 所指定的行程完成，並回傳一個包含 "
"*pid* 及其左移 8 位元之結束狀態的元組（位移讓此函式更容易跨平台使用）。小於或"
"等於 ``0`` 的 *pid* 在 Windows 上沒有特殊意義，並會引發例外。整數 *options* "
"的值沒有作用。*pid* 可以參照任何已知其 ID 的行程，不一定要是子行程。"
"以 :const:`P_NOWAIT` 呼叫的 :func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` 函式會回傳合適的行程控"
"制代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5765
msgid ""
"Similar to :func:`waitpid`, except no process id argument is given and a 3-"
"element tuple containing the child's process id, exit status indication, and "
"resource usage information is returned.  Refer to :func:`resource.getrusage` "
"for details on resource usage information.  The *options* argument is the "
"same as that provided to :func:`waitpid` and :func:`wait4`."
msgstr ""
"與 :func:`waitpid` 類似，差別在於不需提供行程 ID 引數，並會回傳一個包含子行程"
"的行程 ID、結束狀態指示與資源使用資訊的三元組。資源使用資訊的詳細內容請參"
"閱 :func:`resource.getrusage`。*options* 引數與提供給 :func:`waitpid` "
"和 :func:`wait4` 的相同。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5772 ../../library/os.rst:5786
msgid ""
":func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` can be used to convert the exit status into "
"an exitcode."
msgstr "可以使用 :func:`waitstatus_to_exitcode` 將結束狀態轉換為結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5780
msgid ""
"Similar to :func:`waitpid`, except a 3-element tuple, containing the child's "
"process id, exit status indication, and resource usage information is "
"returned.  Refer to :func:`resource.getrusage` for details on resource usage "
"information.  The arguments to :func:`wait4` are the same as those provided "
"to :func:`waitpid`."
msgstr ""
"與 :func:`waitpid` 類似，差別在於會回傳一個包含子行程的行程 ID、結束狀態指示"
"與資源使用資訊的三元組。資源使用資訊的詳細內容請參"
"閱 :func:`resource.getrusage`。:func:`wait4` 的引數與提供給 :func:`waitpid` "
"的相同。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5797
msgid ""
"These are the possible values for *idtype* in :func:`waitid`. They affect "
"how *id* is interpreted:"
msgstr ""
"這些是 :func:`waitid` 中 *idtype* 的可能值。它們會影響 *id* 的解讀方式："

#: ../../library/os.rst:5800
msgid ":data:`!P_PID` - wait for the child whose PID is *id*."
msgstr ":data:`!P_PID` - 等待 PID 為 *id* 的子行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5801
msgid ":data:`!P_PGID` - wait for any child whose progress group ID is *id*."
msgstr ":data:`!P_PGID` - 等待行程群組 ID 為 *id* 的任何子行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5802
msgid ":data:`!P_ALL` - wait for any child; *id* is ignored."
msgstr ":data:`!P_ALL` - 等待任何子行程；*id* 會被忽略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5803
msgid ""
":data:`!P_PIDFD` - wait for the child identified by the file descriptor *id* "
"(a process file descriptor created with :func:`pidfd_open`)."
msgstr ""
":data:`!P_PIDFD` - 等待由檔案描述器 *id*\\ （以 :func:`pidfd_open` 建立的行程"
"檔案描述器）所識別的子行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5808
msgid ":data:`!P_PIDFD` is only available on Linux >= 5.4."
msgstr ":data:`!P_PIDFD` 僅在 Linux >= 5.4 上可用。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5811
msgid "The :data:`!P_PIDFD` constant."
msgstr ":data:`!P_PIDFD` 常數。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5817
msgid ""
"This *options* flag for :func:`waitpid`, :func:`wait3`, :func:`wait4`, "
"and :func:`waitid` causes child processes to be reported if they have been "
"continued from a job control stop since they were last reported."
msgstr ""
"這是 :func:`waitpid`、:func:`wait3`、:func:`wait4` 與 :func:`waitid` 的 "
"*options* 旗標，會使自上次回報以來已從工作控制 (job control) 停止狀態中繼續執"
"行的子行程被回報。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5826
msgid ""
"This *options* flag for :func:`waitid` causes child processes that have "
"terminated to be reported."
msgstr "這是 :func:`waitid` 的 *options* 旗標，會使已終止的子行程被回報。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5829
msgid ""
"The other ``wait*`` functions always report children that have terminated, "
"so this option is not available for them."
msgstr "其他 ``wait*`` 函式一律會回報已終止的子行程，因此此選項不適用於它們。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5839
msgid ""
"This *options* flag for :func:`waitid` causes child processes that have been "
"stopped by the delivery of a signal to be reported."
msgstr ""
"這是 :func:`waitid` 的 *options* 旗標，會使因收到訊號而停止的子行程被回報。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5842 ../../library/os.rst:5874
msgid "This option is not available for the other ``wait*`` functions."
msgstr "此選項不適用於其他 ``wait*`` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5851
msgid ""
"This *options* flag for :func:`waitpid`, :func:`wait3`, and :func:`wait4` "
"causes child processes to also be reported if they have been stopped but "
"their current state has not been reported since they were stopped."
msgstr ""
"這是 :func:`waitpid`、:func:`wait3` 與 :func:`wait4` 的 *options* 旗標，會使"
"已停止、但自停止以來其目前狀態尚未被回報的子行程也被回報。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5855
msgid "This option is not available for :func:`waitid`."
msgstr "此選項不適用於 :func:`waitid`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5862
msgid ""
"This *options* flag causes :func:`waitpid`, :func:`wait3`, :func:`wait4`, "
"and :func:`waitid` to return right away if no child process status is "
"available immediately."
msgstr ""
"此 *options* 旗標會使 :func:`waitpid`、:func:`wait3`、:func:`wait4` "
"與 :func:`waitid` 在沒有立即可用的子行程狀態時馬上回傳。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5871
msgid ""
"This *options* flag causes :func:`waitid` to leave the child in a waitable "
"state, so that a later :func:`!wait*` call can be used to retrieve the child "
"status information again."
msgstr ""
"此 *options* 旗標會使 :func:`waitid` 讓子行程維持在可等待狀態，以便之後能再"
"用 :func:`!wait*` 呼叫取得子行程的狀態資訊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5886
msgid ""
"These are the possible values for :attr:`!si_code` in the result returned "
"by :func:`waitid`."
msgstr "這些是 :func:`waitid` 所回傳結果中 :attr:`!si_code` 的可能值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5893
msgid "Added :data:`CLD_KILLED` and :data:`CLD_STOPPED` values."
msgstr "新增 :data:`CLD_KILLED` 和 :data:`CLD_STOPPED` 值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5899
msgid "Convert a wait status to an exit code."
msgstr "將等待狀態轉換為結束代碼。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5901
msgid "On Unix:"
msgstr "在 Unix 上："

#: ../../library/os.rst:5903
msgid ""
"If the process exited normally (if ``WIFEXITED(status)`` is true), return "
"the process exit status (return ``WEXITSTATUS(status)``): result greater "
"than or equal to 0."
msgstr ""
"如果行程正常結束（如果 ``WIFEXITED(status)`` 為真），則回傳行程的結束狀態（回"
"傳 ``WEXITSTATUS(status)``）：結果大於或等於 0。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5906
msgid ""
"If the process was terminated by a signal (if ``WIFSIGNALED(status)`` is "
"true), return ``-signum`` where *signum* is the number of the signal that "
"caused the process to terminate (return ``-WTERMSIG(status)``): result less "
"than 0."
msgstr ""
"如果行程被訊號終止（如果 ``WIFSIGNALED(status)`` 為真），則回傳 ``-signum``，"
"其中 *signum* 是導致行程終止的訊號編號（回傳 ``-WTERMSIG(status)``）：結果小"
"於 0。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5910
msgid "Otherwise, raise a :exc:`ValueError`."
msgstr "否則，引發 :exc:`ValueError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5912
msgid "On Windows, return *status* shifted right by 8 bits."
msgstr "在 Windows 上，回傳 *status* 右移 8 位元後的值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5914
msgid ""
"On Unix, if the process is being traced or if :func:`waitpid` was called "
"with :data:`WUNTRACED` option, the caller must first check if "
"``WIFSTOPPED(status)`` is true. This function must not be called if "
"``WIFSTOPPED(status)`` is true."
msgstr ""
"在 Unix 上，如果行程正在被追蹤，或是以 :data:`WUNTRACED` 選項呼叫"
"了 :func:`waitpid`，呼叫者必須先檢查 ``WIFSTOPPED(status)`` 是否為真。如果 "
"``WIFSTOPPED(status)`` 為真，則不得呼叫此函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5921
msgid ""
":func:`WIFEXITED`, :func:`WEXITSTATUS`, :func:`WIFSIGNALED`, :func:`WTERMSIG`, :func:`WIFSTOPPED`, :func:`WSTOPSIG` "
"functions."
msgstr ""
":func:`WIFEXITED`、:func:`WEXITSTATUS`、:func:`WIFSIGNALED`、:func:`WTERMSIG`、:func:`WIFSTOPPED`、:func:`WSTOPSIG` "
"函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5929
msgid ""
"The following functions take a process status code as returned "
"by :func:`system`, :func:`wait`, or :func:`waitpid` as a parameter.  They "
"may be used to determine the disposition of a process."
msgstr ""
"以下函式接受由 :func:`system`、:func:`wait` 或 :func:`waitpid` 回傳的行程狀態"
"碼作為參數。它們可用來判斷行程處於何種狀態。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5935
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if a core dump was generated for the process, otherwise "
"return ``False``."
msgstr "如果該行程產生了核心傾印，則回傳 ``True``，否則回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5938 ../../library/os.rst:6004
msgid "This function should be employed only if :func:`WIFSIGNALED` is true."
msgstr "只有在 :func:`WIFSIGNALED` 為真時才應使用此函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5945
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if a stopped child has been resumed by delivery "
"of :const:`~signal.SIGCONT` (if the process has been continued from a job "
"control stop), otherwise return ``False``."
msgstr ""
"如果已停止的子行程因收到 :const:`~signal.SIGCONT` 而恢復執行（如果該行程已從"
"工作控制停止狀態中繼續執行），則回傳 ``True``，否則回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5949
msgid "See :data:`WCONTINUED` option."
msgstr "參閱 :data:`WCONTINUED` 選項。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5956
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the process was stopped by delivery of a signal, "
"otherwise return ``False``."
msgstr "如果該行程因收到訊號而停止，則回傳 ``True``，否則回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5959
msgid ""
":func:`WIFSTOPPED` only returns ``True`` if the :func:`waitpid` call was "
"done using :data:`WUNTRACED` option or when the process is being traced "
"(see :manpage:`ptrace(2)`)."
msgstr ""
"只有在以 :data:`WUNTRACED` 選項呼叫 :func:`waitpid`，或該行程正在被追蹤時（請"
"參閱 :manpage:`ptrace(2)`），:func:`WIFSTOPPED` 才會回傳 ``True``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5967
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the process was terminated by a signal, otherwise return "
"``False``."
msgstr "如果該行程被訊號終止，則回傳 ``True``，否則回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5975
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the process exited terminated normally, that is, by "
"calling ``exit()`` or ``_exit()``, or by returning from ``main()``; "
"otherwise return ``False``."
msgstr ""
"如果該行程正常結束，也就是透過呼叫 ``exit()`` 或 ``_exit()``，或是從 "
"``main()`` 回傳而結束，則回傳 ``True``；否則回傳 ``False``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5984
msgid "Return the process exit status."
msgstr "回傳行程的結束狀態。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5986
msgid "This function should be employed only if :func:`WIFEXITED` is true."
msgstr "只有在 :func:`WIFEXITED` 為真時才應使用此函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5993
msgid "Return the signal which caused the process to stop."
msgstr "回傳導致行程停止的訊號。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:5995
msgid "This function should be employed only if :func:`WIFSTOPPED` is true."
msgstr "只有在 :func:`WIFSTOPPED` 為真時才應使用此函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6002
msgid "Return the number of the signal that caused the process to terminate."
msgstr "回傳導致行程終止的訊號編號。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6010
msgid "Interface to the scheduler"
msgstr "排程器介面"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6012
msgid ""
"These functions control how a process is allocated CPU time by the operating "
"system. They are only available on some Unix platforms. For more detailed "
"information, consult your Unix manpages."
msgstr ""
"這些函式控制作業系統如何為行程分配 CPU 時間。它們僅在部分 Unix 平台上可用。更"
"詳細的資訊請參閱你的 Unix 使用手冊。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6018
msgid ""
"The following scheduling policies are exposed if they are supported by the "
"operating system."
msgstr "若作業系統支援，會提供以下排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6025
msgid "The default scheduling policy."
msgstr "預設的排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6029
msgid ""
"Scheduling policy for CPU-intensive processes that tries to preserve "
"interactivity on the rest of the computer."
msgstr "適用於 CPU 密集型行程的排程策略，會試圖維持電腦其餘部分的互動性。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6034
msgid "Scheduling policy for tasks with deadline constraints."
msgstr "適用於有截止期限限制之任務的排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6040
msgid "Scheduling policy for extremely low priority background tasks."
msgstr "適用於優先權極低之背景任務的排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6044
msgid "Alias for :data:`SCHED_OTHER`."
msgstr ":data:`SCHED_OTHER` 的別名。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6050
msgid "Scheduling policy for sporadic server programs."
msgstr "適用於零星伺服器 (sporadic server) 程式的排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6054
msgid "A First In First Out scheduling policy."
msgstr "先進先出排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6058
msgid "A round-robin scheduling policy."
msgstr "輪轉排程策略。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6062
msgid ""
"This flag can be OR'ed with any other scheduling policy. When a process with "
"this flag set forks, its child's scheduling policy and priority are reset to "
"the default."
msgstr ""
"此旗標可以與任何其他排程策略進行 OR 運算。當設定了此旗標的行程進行 fork 時，"
"其子行程的排程策略與優先權會被重設為預設值。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6069
msgid ""
"This class represents tunable scheduling parameters used "
"in :func:`sched_setparam`, :func:`sched_setscheduler`, "
"and :func:`sched_getparam`. It is immutable."
msgstr ""
"此類別代表 :func:`sched_setparam`、:func:`sched_setscheduler` "
"與 :func:`sched_getparam` 中所使用的可調整排程參數。它是不可變的。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6073
msgid "At the moment, there is only one possible parameter:"
msgstr "目前只有一個可能的參數："

#: ../../library/os.rst:6077
msgid "The scheduling priority for a scheduling policy."
msgstr "排程策略的排程優先權。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6082
msgid ""
"Get the minimum priority value for *policy*. *policy* is one of the "
"scheduling policy constants above."
msgstr "取得 *policy* 的最小優先權值。*policy* 是上述排程策略常數之一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6088
msgid ""
"Get the maximum priority value for *policy*. *policy* is one of the "
"scheduling policy constants above."
msgstr "取得 *policy* 的最大優先權值。*policy* 是上述排程策略常數之一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6094
msgid ""
"Set the scheduling policy for the process with PID *pid*. A *pid* of 0 means "
"the calling process. *policy* is one of the scheduling policy constants "
"above. *param* is a :class:`sched_param` instance."
msgstr ""
"設定 PID 為 *pid* 之行程的排程策略。*pid* 為 0 表示呼叫端行程。*policy* 是上"
"述排程策略常數之一。*param* 是一個 :class:`sched_param` 實例。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6101
msgid ""
"Return the scheduling policy for the process with PID *pid*. A *pid* of 0 "
"means the calling process. The result is one of the scheduling policy "
"constants above."
msgstr ""
"回傳 PID 為 *pid* 之行程的排程策略。*pid* 為 0 表示呼叫端行程。結果是上述排程"
"策略常數之一。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6108
msgid ""
"Set the scheduling parameters for the process with PID *pid*. A *pid* of 0 "
"means the calling process. *param* is a :class:`sched_param` instance."
msgstr ""
"設定 PID 為 *pid* 之行程的排程參數。*pid* 為 0 表示呼叫端行程。*param* 是一"
"個 :class:`sched_param` 實例。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6114
msgid ""
"Return the scheduling parameters as a :class:`sched_param` instance for the "
"process with PID *pid*. A *pid* of 0 means the calling process."
msgstr ""
"以 :class:`sched_param` 實例的形式回傳 PID 為 *pid* 之行程的排程參數。*pid* "
"為 0 表示呼叫端行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6120
msgid ""
"Return the round-robin quantum in seconds for the process with PID *pid*. A "
"*pid* of 0 means the calling process."
msgstr ""
"回傳 PID 為 *pid* 之行程的輪轉時間配額 (round-robin quantum)，以秒為單位。"
"*pid* 為 0 表示呼叫端行程。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6126
msgid ""
"Voluntarily relinquish the CPU. See :manpage:`sched_yield(2)` for details."
msgstr "自願讓出 CPU。詳細資訊請參閱 :manpage:`sched_yield(2)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6131
msgid ""
"Restrict the process with PID *pid* (or the current process if zero) to a "
"set of CPUs.  *mask* is an iterable of integers representing the set of CPUs "
"to which the process should be restricted."
msgstr ""
"將 PID 為 *pid* 的行程（若為零則為目前行程）限制在一組 CPU 上。*mask* 是一個"
"由整數組成的可疊代物件，代表該行程應被限制使用的 CPU 集合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6138
msgid "Return the set of CPUs the process with PID *pid* is restricted to."
msgstr "回傳 PID 為 *pid* 之行程被限制使用的 CPU 集合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6140
msgid ""
"If *pid* is zero, return the set of CPUs the calling thread of the current "
"process is restricted to."
msgstr "如果 *pid* 為零，則回傳目前行程的呼叫端執行緒被限制使用的 CPU 集合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6143
msgid "See also the :func:`process_cpu_count` function."
msgstr "也請見 :func:`process_cpu_count` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6149
msgid "Miscellaneous System Information"
msgstr "其他系統資訊"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6154
msgid ""
"Return string-valued system configuration values. *name* specifies the "
"configuration value to retrieve; it may be a string which is the name of a "
"defined system value; these names are specified in a number of standards "
"(POSIX, Unix 95, Unix 98, and others).  Some platforms define additional "
"names as well. The names known to the host operating system are given as the "
"keys of the ``confstr_names`` dictionary.  For configuration variables not "
"included in that mapping, passing an integer for *name* is also accepted."
msgstr ""
"回傳字串值的系統設定值。*name* 指定要取得的設定值；它可以是一個字串，為某個已"
"定義系統值的名稱；這些名稱由許多標準（POSIX、Unix 95、Unix 98 等）所規定。有"
"些平台還會定義額外的名稱。主機作業系統已知的名稱以 ``confstr_names`` 字典的鍵"
"提供。對於未包含在該對映中的設定變數，也可以傳入整數作為 *name*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6162
msgid ""
"If the configuration value specified by *name* isn't defined, ``None`` is "
"returned."
msgstr "如果 *name* 所指定的設定值未被定義，則回傳 ``None``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6165
msgid ""
"If *name* is a string and is not known, :exc:`ValueError` is raised.  If a "
"specific value for *name* is not supported by the host system, even if it is "
"included in ``confstr_names``, an :exc:`OSError` is raised "
"with :const:`errno.EINVAL` for the error number."
msgstr ""
"如果 *name* 是字串但未知，會引發 :exc:`ValueError`。如果主機系統不支援 "
"*name* 的特定值，即使它包含在 ``confstr_names`` 中，也會引發 :exc:`OSError`，"
"其錯誤編號為 :const:`errno.EINVAL`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6175
msgid ""
"Dictionary mapping names accepted by :func:`confstr` to the integer values "
"defined for those names by the host operating system. This can be used to "
"determine the set of names known to the system."
msgstr ""
"將 :func:`confstr` 所接受的名稱對映到主機作業系統為這些名稱所定義之整數值的字"
"典。可用來判斷系統已知的名稱集合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6184
msgid ""
"Return the number of logical CPUs in the **system**. Returns ``None`` if "
"undetermined."
msgstr "回傳\\ **系統**\\ 中邏輯 CPU 的數量。如果無法確定則回傳 ``None``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6187
msgid ""
"The :func:`process_cpu_count` function can be used to get the number of "
"logical CPUs usable by the calling thread of the **current process**."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 :func:`process_cpu_count` 函式來取得\\ **目前行程**\\ 的呼叫端執行緒"
"可使用的邏輯 CPU 數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6192
msgid ""
"If :option:`-X cpu_count <-X>` is given or :envvar:`PYTHON_CPU_COUNT` is "
"set, :func:`cpu_count` returns the override value *n*."
msgstr ""
"如果給定了 :option:`-X cpu_count <-X>` 或設定"
"了 :envvar:`PYTHON_CPU_COUNT`，:func:`cpu_count` 會回傳覆寫值 *n*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6199
msgid ""
"Return the number of processes in the system run queue averaged over the "
"last 1, 5, and 15 minutes or raises :exc:`OSError` if the load average was "
"unobtainable."
msgstr ""
"回傳系統執行佇列 (run queue) 中過去 1、5 與 15 分鐘的平均行程數量；如果無法取"
"得平均負載 (load average)，則引發 :exc:`OSError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6208
msgid ""
"Get the number of logical CPUs usable by the calling thread of the **current "
"process**. Returns ``None`` if undetermined. It can be less "
"than :func:`cpu_count` depending on the CPU affinity."
msgstr ""
"取得\\ **目前行程**\\ 的呼叫端執行緒可使用的邏輯 CPU 數量。如果無法確定則回"
"傳 ``None``。依據 CPU 親和性 (CPU affinity)，它可能會小於 :func:`cpu_count`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6212
msgid ""
"The :func:`cpu_count` function can be used to get the number of logical CPUs "
"in the **system**."
msgstr "可以使用 :func:`cpu_count` 函式來取得\\ **系統**\\ 中邏輯 CPU 的數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6215
msgid ""
"If :option:`-X cpu_count <-X>` is given or :envvar:`PYTHON_CPU_COUNT` is "
"set, :func:`process_cpu_count` returns the override value *n*."
msgstr ""
"如果給定了 :option:`-X cpu_count <-X>` 或設定"
"了 :envvar:`PYTHON_CPU_COUNT`，:func:`process_cpu_count` 會回傳覆寫值 *n*。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6218
msgid "See also the :func:`sched_getaffinity` function."
msgstr "也請見 :func:`sched_getaffinity` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6225
msgid ""
"Return integer-valued system configuration values. If the configuration "
"value specified by *name* isn't defined, ``-1`` is returned.  The comments "
"regarding the *name* parameter for :func:`confstr` apply here as well; the "
"dictionary that provides information on the known names is given by "
"``sysconf_names``."
msgstr ""
"回傳整數值的系統設定值。如果 *name* 所指定的設定值未被定義，則回傳 ``-1``。關"
"於 :func:`confstr` 的 *name* 參數的說明在此同樣適用；提供已知名稱資訊的字典"
"為 ``sysconf_names``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6235
msgid ""
"Dictionary mapping names accepted by :func:`sysconf` to the integer values "
"defined for those names by the host operating system. This can be used to "
"determine the set of names known to the system."
msgstr ""
"將 :func:`sysconf` 所接受的名稱對映到主機作業系統為這些名稱所定義之整數值的字"
"典。可用來判斷系統已知的名稱集合。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6241
msgid "Add ``'SC_MINSIGSTKSZ'`` name."
msgstr "新增 ``'SC_MINSIGSTKSZ'`` 名稱。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6244
msgid ""
"The following data values are used to support path manipulation operations.  "
"These are defined for all platforms."
msgstr "以下資料值用於支援路徑操作。它們在所有平台上皆有定義。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6247
msgid ""
"Higher-level operations on pathnames are defined in the :mod:`os.path` "
"module."
msgstr "對路徑名稱進行的高階操作定義於 :mod:`os.path` 模組中。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6253
msgid ""
"The constant string used by the operating system to refer to the current "
"directory. This is ``'.'`` for Windows and POSIX. Also available "
"via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"作業系統用來表示目前目錄的常數字串。在 Windows 與 POSIX 上為 ``'.'``。也可以"
"透過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6261
msgid ""
"The constant string used by the operating system to refer to the parent "
"directory. This is ``'..'`` for Windows and POSIX. Also available "
"via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"作業系統用來表示父目錄的常數字串。在 Windows 與 POSIX 上為 ``'..'``。也可以透"
"過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6270
msgid ""
"The character used by the operating system to separate pathname components. "
"This is ``'/'`` for POSIX and ``'\\\\'`` for Windows.  Note that knowing "
"this is not sufficient to be able to parse or concatenate pathnames --- "
"use :func:`os.path.split` and :func:`os.path.join` --- but it is "
"occasionally useful. Also available via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"作業系統用來分隔路徑名稱各組成部分的字元。在 POSIX 上為 ``'/'``，在 Windows "
"上為 ``'\\\\'``。請注意，僅知道這一點並不足以剖析或串接路徑名稱 --- 請使"
"用 :func:`os.path.split` 與 :func:`os.path.join` --- 但它偶爾還是很有用。也可"
"以透過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6280
msgid ""
"An alternative character used by the operating system to separate pathname "
"components, or ``None`` if only one separator character exists.  This is set "
"to ``'/'`` on Windows systems where ``sep`` is a backslash. Also available "
"via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"作業系統用來分隔路徑名稱各組成部分的替代字元；如果只有一個分隔字元則為 "
"``None``。在 ``sep`` 為反斜線的 Windows 系統上，此值設為 ``'/'``。也可以透"
"過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6289
msgid ""
"The character which separates the base filename from the extension; for "
"example, the ``'.'`` in :file:`os.py`. Also available via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"用來分隔基本檔案名稱與副檔名的字元；例如 :file:`os.py` 中的 ``'.'``。也可以透"
"過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6297
msgid ""
"The character conventionally used by the operating system to separate search "
"path components (as in :envvar:`PATH`), such as ``':'`` for POSIX or ``';'`` "
"for Windows. Also available via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"作業系統慣用來分隔搜尋路徑各組成部分（如 :envvar:`PATH` 中）的字元，例如 "
"POSIX 上的 ``':'`` 或 Windows 上的 ``';'``。也可以透過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6304
msgid ""
"The default search path used by :func:`exec\\*p\\* <execl>` "
"and :func:`spawn\\*p\\* <spawnl>` if the environment doesn't have a "
"``'PATH'`` key. Also available via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"當環境中沒有 ``'PATH'`` 鍵時，:func:`exec\\*p\\* <execl>` "
"與 :func:`spawn\\*p\\* <spawnl>` 所使用的預設搜尋路徑。也可以透"
"過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6311
msgid ""
"The string used to separate (or, rather, terminate) lines on the current "
"platform.  This may be a single character, such as ``'\\n'`` for POSIX, or "
"multiple characters, for example, ``'\\r\\n'`` for Windows. Do not use "
"*os.linesep* as a line terminator when writing files opened in text mode "
"(the default); use a single ``'\\n'`` instead, on all platforms."
msgstr ""
"目前平台上用來分隔（或者說，終止）各行的字串。這可能是單一字元，例如 POSIX 上"
"的 ``'\\n'``，也可能是多個字元，例如 Windows 上的 ``'\\r\\n'``。寫入以文字模"
"式（預設）開啟的檔案時，請不要使用 *os.linesep* 作為行結束符號；請在所有平台"
"上都改用單一的 ``'\\n'``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6320
msgid ""
"The file path of the null device. For example: ``'/dev/null'`` for POSIX, "
"``'nul'`` for Windows.  Also available via :mod:`os.path`."
msgstr ""
"空裝置 (null device) 的檔案路徑。例如：POSIX 上為 ``'/dev/null'``，Windows 上"
"為 ``'nul'``。也可以透過 :mod:`os.path` 取得。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6331
msgid ""
"Flags for use with the :func:`~sys.setdlopenflags` "
"and :func:`~sys.getdlopenflags` functions.  See the Unix manual "
"page :manpage:`dlopen(3)` for what the different flags mean."
msgstr ""
"用於 :func:`~sys.setdlopenflags` 與 :func:`~sys.getdlopenflags` 函式的旗標。"
"各旗標的意義請參閱 Unix 使用手冊 :manpage:`dlopen(3)`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6339
msgid "Random numbers"
msgstr "亂數"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6344
msgid ""
"Get up to *size* random bytes. The function can return less bytes than "
"requested."
msgstr ""
"取得最多 *size* 個隨機位元組。此函式回傳的位元組數可能少於所請求的數量。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6347
msgid ""
"These bytes can be used to seed user-space random number generators or for "
"cryptographic purposes."
msgstr "這些位元組可用於為使用者空間 的亂數產生器提供種子，或用於加密用途。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6350
msgid ""
"``getrandom()`` relies on entropy gathered from device drivers and other "
"sources of environmental noise. Unnecessarily reading large quantities of "
"data will have a negative impact on  other users  of the ``/dev/random`` and "
"``/dev/urandom`` devices."
msgstr ""
"``getrandom()`` 依賴從裝置驅動程式和其他環境雜訊來源所收集的熵 (entropy)。不"
"必要地讀取大量資料，會對 ``/dev/random`` 與 ``/dev/urandom`` 裝置的其他使用者"
"造成負面影響。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6355
msgid ""
"The flags argument is a bit mask that can contain zero or more of the "
"following values ORed together: :py:const:`os.GRND_RANDOM` "
"and :py:data:`GRND_NONBLOCK`."
msgstr ""
"flags 引數是一個位元遮罩，可以包含零個或多個以下值以 OR 組合而"
"成：:py:const:`os.GRND_RANDOM` 與 :py:data:`GRND_NONBLOCK`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6359
msgid ""
"See also the `Linux getrandom() manual page <https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man2/getrandom.2.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"另請參閱 `Linux getrandom() 使用手冊 <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/"
"getrandom.2.html>`_。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6368
msgid ""
"Return a bytestring of *size* random bytes suitable for cryptographic use."
msgstr "回傳一個由 *size* 個適用於加密用途之隨機位元組所組成的位元組串。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6370
msgid ""
"This function returns random bytes from an OS-specific randomness source.  "
"The returned data should be unpredictable enough for cryptographic "
"applications, though its exact quality depends on the OS implementation."
msgstr ""
"此函式從作業系統特定的隨機來源回傳隨機位元組。回傳的資料對於加密應用來說應該"
"足夠不可預測，但其確切品質取決於作業系統的實作。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6374
msgid ""
"On Linux, if the ``getrandom()`` syscall is available, it is used in "
"blocking mode: block until the system urandom entropy pool is initialized "
"(128 bits of entropy are collected by the kernel). See the :pep:`524` for "
"the rationale. On Linux, the :func:`getrandom` function can be used to get "
"random bytes in non-blocking mode (using the :data:`GRND_NONBLOCK` flag) or "
"to poll until the system urandom entropy pool is initialized."
msgstr ""
"在 Linux 上，如果可以使用 ``getrandom()`` 系統呼叫，則會以阻塞模式使用它：阻"
"塞直到系統的 urandom 熵池 (entropy pool) 初始化完成（核心已收集了 128 位元的"
"熵）。其理由請參閱 :pep:`524`。在 Linux 上，可以使用 :func:`getrandom` 函式以"
"非阻塞模式取得隨機位元組（使用 :data:`GRND_NONBLOCK` 旗標），或輪詢直到系統"
"的 urandom 熵池初始化完成。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6381
msgid ""
"On other Unix-like systems, the C ``getrandom()`` function is used if it is "
"available, otherwise the C ``getentropy()`` function."
msgstr ""
"在其他類 Unix 系統上，如果 C 的 ``getrandom()`` 函式可用就會使用它，否則使用 "
"C 的 ``getentropy()`` 函式。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6384
msgid ""
"If none of these functions can be used, random bytes are read from the ``/"
"dev/urandom`` device. If the ``/dev/urandom`` device is not available or not "
"readable, the :exc:`NotImplementedError` exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"如果這些函式都無法使用，則會從 ``/dev/urandom`` 裝置讀取隨機位元組。如果 ``/"
"dev/urandom`` 裝置無法使用或無法讀取，則會引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError` 例"
"外。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6388
msgid "On Windows, it will use ``BCryptGenRandom()``."
msgstr "在 Windows 上，它會使用 ``BCryptGenRandom()``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6391
msgid ""
"The :mod:`secrets` module provides higher level functions. For an easy-to-"
"use interface to the random number generator provided by your platform, "
"please see :class:`random.SystemRandom`."
msgstr ""
":mod:`secrets` 模組提供了更高階的函式。若需要一個易於使用、可存取你的平台所提"
"供之亂數產生器的介面，請參閱 :class:`random.SystemRandom`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6395
msgid ""
"On Linux 3.17 and newer, the ``getrandom()`` syscall is now used when "
"available.  On OpenBSD 5.6 and newer, the C ``getentropy()`` function is now "
"used. These functions avoid the usage of an internal file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"在 Linux 3.17 以上的版本中，現在會在可用時使用 ``getrandom()`` 系統呼叫。在 "
"OpenBSD 5.6 以上的版本中，現在會使用 C 的 ``getentropy()`` 函式。這些函式可避"
"免使用內部的檔案描述器。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6401
msgid ""
"On Linux, if the ``getrandom()`` syscall blocks (the urandom entropy pool is "
"not initialized yet), fall back on reading ``/dev/urandom``."
msgstr ""
"在 Linux 上，如果 ``getrandom()`` 系統呼叫發生阻塞（urandom 熵池尚未初始"
"化），則退而改為讀取 ``/dev/urandom``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6405
msgid ""
"On Linux, ``getrandom()`` is now used in blocking mode to increase the "
"security."
msgstr "在 Linux 上，現在會以阻塞模式使用 ``getrandom()`` 以提高安全性。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6409
msgid ""
"On Windows, ``BCryptGenRandom()`` is used instead of ``CryptGenRandom()`` "
"which is deprecated."
msgstr ""
"在 Windows 上，改用 ``BCryptGenRandom()`` 取代已被棄用的 "
"``CryptGenRandom()``。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6415
msgid ""
"By  default, when reading from ``/dev/random``, :func:`getrandom` blocks if "
"no random bytes are available, and when reading from ``/dev/urandom``, it "
"blocks if the entropy pool has not yet been initialized."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，從 ``/dev/random`` 讀取時，若沒有可用的隨機位元"
"組，:func:`getrandom` 會阻塞；從 ``/dev/urandom`` 讀取時，若熵池尚未初始化，"
"它也會阻塞。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6419
msgid ""
"If the :py:data:`GRND_NONBLOCK` flag is set, then :func:`getrandom` does not "
"block in these cases, but instead immediately raises :exc:`BlockingIOError`."
msgstr ""
"如果設定了 :py:data:`GRND_NONBLOCK` 旗標，:func:`getrandom` 在這些情況下不會"
"阻塞，而是立即引發 :exc:`BlockingIOError`。"

#: ../../library/os.rst:6426
msgid ""
"If  this  bit  is  set,  then  random bytes are drawn from the ``/dev/"
"random`` pool instead of the ``/dev/urandom`` pool."
msgstr ""
"如果設定了此位元，則隨機位元組會從 ``/dev/random`` 池而非 ``/dev/urandom`` 池"
"中取得。"

